{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_34", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -3 cores/bench/generated/selector_formal.log; git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": "SBY  2:33:16 [reg_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\n\nFormal: 53 passed, 0 failed\n M cores/bench/rtl/divider.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n# Balanced radix-8 monotonic-fit selection\n\nImplemented the requested selector in both radix-8 steps in `rtl/divider.sv`.\nThe remainder uses the exact fit[4], fit[2/6], fit[1/3/5/7] three-level mux\ntree. Quotient bits use the same decisions. Removed adjacent-fit `take`\ngeneration and masked candidate OR reduction.\n\nAll seven native 36-bit trials, registered 35-bit divisor multiples, two-bit\npreparation peel, five six-bit iterations, sign/exception correction, and\nrequest/result state timing are unchanged. ALTOPS and every other RTL file\nare unchanged; retirement remains nret=1.\n\nExtended `test/test_alu.py` with a Yosys SAT proof that extracts the actual\nRTL selection assignments and checks all eight monotonic fit patterns against\nthe largest-fitting digit. Candidate data and the prior quotient are arbitrary\nsymbolic inputs. Expanded the existing radix-8 vectors to cover every multiple\n2D through 7D across bit-32, bit-33, and bit-34 boundaries, retaining threshold\nequality/off-by-one, all quotient positions, signed quadrants, and zero divisor\ncases. Existing captured-input, exact-latency, backpressure, and reset checks\nare preserved.\n\nNo architectural deviations or changes to verification gates/depths.\nThe local Makefile's cosim build defaults to NRET=2, so the requested builds\nare invoked with NRET=1 to match the unchanged core.yaml contract.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Verilator lint: passed without warnings.\n- Selector SAT equivalence: passed.\n- Real and ALTOPS ALU vectors: passed.\n- Complete unit suite: 8 pytest runners/checks passed in 52.76 s, including\n  31 real ALU cases, 31 ALTOPS ALU cases, and 31 pipeline cases each with\n  the normal and YOSYS storage declarations. Decoder, immediate generator,\n  and register-file suites also passed.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: PASS,\n  53 checks passed and zero failed on the first attempt, using the unchanged\n  auto-selected nret=1 wrapper/configuration and original depths. No formal\n  counterexample or RTL fix retry was needed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: passed for all five ELFs. Selftest and\n  random1/2/3 were compared retirement-by-retirement with the Python ISS\n  both without stalls and with random instruction/data stalls. CoreMark\n  passed canonical CRC/UART validation and memory bounds checks.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench`: all normal placements passed. CoreMark\n  completed 10 iterations in exactly 3,977,318 bracketed cycles; canonical\n  CRCs, UART validation, bounds, and timing markers passed unchanged.\n\nFull normal Gowin placement results:\n\n| Placement option | Fmax (MHz) | Logic levels |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 0 | 61.264 | 17 |\n| 1 | 64.342 | 10 |\n| 2 | 64.342 | 10 |\n\nMedian Fmax is 64.342 MHz, yielding 161.77233 iterations/s (the evaluator\nreports 161.77), a 0.3478% frequency improvement over 64.119 MHz at unchanged\ncycles. Resources for all placements: 4,053 logic cells, 893 FFs, 49 LUT-RAMs,\nfour BSRAMs, and six DSPs. This DOES NOT meet the required >168.62566\niterations/s acceptance threshold. The complete median is reported, not\nonly the best placement.\n\nThe leading option-0 path runs from registered forwarding metadata through\nEX and branch recovery to the fetch PC. Options 1/2 are limited by the\nMEM/WB reg_write-to-EX ALU-result path, closely followed by branch recovery.\nThe measured result confirms the concern that competing EX paths and\nplacement sensitivity constrain the gain from this isolated selector change.\n\nThe selector proof covers real selection, while ALTOPS formal only checks\nthe substituted arithmetic and pipeline contract. Real arithmetic is checked\nby the ALU vectors and reference cosimulation. No full-core real-arithmetic\nformal-deep result is claimed. Logs and full vendor timing reports are in\n`generated/selector_*.log` and `generated/gowin_p*/impl/pnr/` respectively.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
