{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n# Implementation notes\n\n- Changed only the combinational shift datapaths in `rtl/alu.sv`: four\n  one-hot coarse enables select constant shifts by 0/8/16/24 using masks and\n  a balanced pairwise OR tree, followed by conditional 1/2/4-bit stages.\n  Left shifting is separate; SRL/SRA share a right path whose fill is\n  `(op == ALU_SRA) && a[31]` at every stage. Only `b[4:0]` is used.\n- Kept the ALU result case and operation encodings, all other operations,\n  real/ALTOPS arithmetic, handshakes, sequential state, pipeline, predictor,\n  forwarding, memory and single-channel RVFI interfaces unchanged.\n- Retained every existing test assertion and added all-amount shift coverage\n  in `test/test_alu.py`: sign boundaries, walking ones/zeros, 64 random word\n  pairs with both signs, upper shift-operand masks and random upper bits,\n  and immediate SRA/SRL/SLL/SRA transitions without clock edges. The same\n  test runs in real and ALTOPS builds.\n- No architectural deviations. Fine constant shifts are expressed as\n  concatenations with explicit fill bits. Notes are stored under\n  `cores/bench/` to honor the target-only editing restriction.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Verilator lint: PASS, no warnings.\n- Exhaustive Yosys SAT combinational equivalence: PASS for arbitrary 32-bit\n  `a` and `b` and every five-bit `op`. The miter reads the actual replacement\n  shifter and complete result case verbatim from `alu.sv`, compares against\n  the original native shift formulas, and shares arbitrary multiply/divide\n  result inputs between both cones. Those unchanged sequential units are\n  outside this combinational proof. This covers arithmetic fill, zero\n  shift, ignored upper `b` bits, and all result-case arms.\n- Real and ALTOPS ALU suites: PASS, 35 cocotb tests each, including the new\n  128,000-vector shift test. Both existing pipeline variants: PASS, 37\n  cocotb tests each. Pytest reports all four runners passed in 323.41 s.\n- Unchanged `formal/run_all.sh`: PASS, 53 checks passed, zero failed,\n  including the final `reg_ch0` check. Invoked with\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=6`; it auto-selected the\n  original nret=1 `wrapper_si.sv` and `checks_si.cfg` (ALTOPS) configuration.\n  No counterexamples, RTL fixes or retries. Real M-extension arithmetic\n  was checked by the unchanged unit tests and reference cosimulation;\n  formal-deep was not run because neither arithmetic unit was modified.\n- Canonical cosimulation: PASS for selftest with and without random memory\n  stalls and stalled CoreMark. The unmodified `run_coremark_ipc` validator\n  additionally passes completion, bounds, canonical CRCs/UART, and timing\n  markers, with exactly 3,989,539 bracketed cycles for 10 iterations.\n  Direct `make cosim` initially defaulted to NRET=2 in the build script;\n  rerun with `NRET=1`, matching the unchanged core.yaml and orchestrator.\n\nGowin timing (`python3 -m tools.eval.gowin bench --all-options`):\n\n| Placement option | Fmax (MHz) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 83.019 |\n| 1 | 85.563 |\n| 2 | 85.563 |\n\nMedian Fmax is 85.563 MHz. All options use 5,805 logic cells, 1,256\nregisters, 49 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. This exactly reproduces\nthe proposal's prototype measurements. At unchanged cycles the projected\nscore is 214.468388 iterations/s, 1.39% above 211.52, below the required\n221.24992 iterations/s (approximately 88.269 MHz). No accepted improvement\nis claimed. Timing shows competing forwarding/EX-result, branch recovery\nand divider recurrence paths. No additional optimization was mixed into\nthis local shifter hypothesis.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
