{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_32", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r6s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Preselect branch recovery targets from captured prediction'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 129.31 iterations/s at 54.331 MHz and 4,201,709\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh Gowin placement-0 run reproduced\nits 25.514 ns worst arrival from register-file output through EX\nbranch recovery to the fetch PC. The previous effective-address\nseparation removed the multiplier from RAM addressing. Earlier\nmicro_opt attempts show that preserving the execution schedule can\nimprove fitness without the multiply-stall penalty seen in r5s1.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Simplify the existing combinational branch-recovery network. On a\ndirect BRANCH/JAL redirect, the resolved direction necessarily\nopposes the captured predicted_taken bit. Therefore preselect the\nrecovery address as predicted_taken ? pc+4 : pc+imm; for JALR select\n(rs1+imm)&~1. The late branch comparison then decides whether to\nredirect, but does not also control the wide recovery-target mux.\nredirect_target is consumed only when redirect is asserted; its\ninactive-cycle value need not match the old general resolved target.\nKeep architectural RVFI pc_next based on the actual branch outcome.\n\nFactor recovery qualification by instruction class. Compute direct\nalignment from (pc+imm)[1:0], and JALR alignment from (rs1+imm)[1]\nafter bit zero is cleared. A conditional branch mismatch is\nis_branch && (predicted_taken XOR (branch_cond && direct_aligned));\na direct JAL mismatch is is_jump && \"'!is_jalr &&\n(predicted_taken XOR direct_aligned); legal aligned JALR always\nredirects. OR these cases and gate by ex_accept and !is_illegal.\nKeep the existing misalignment fault and writeback suppression.\nThe decoder produces mutually exclusive branch/jump classes; do\nnot weaken its legality checks or alter reserved instruction behavior.\n\nKeep the six comparisons, forwarding, target adders, predictor size,\nlookup/training/reset policy, and all pipeline registers unchanged.\nDo not add a stage or change a stall or retirement cycle. Recovery\nstill overrides instruction-bus backpressure and cannot fire while\nEX is held by an older memory operation or a blocking divide.\nTaken misaligned controls still trap with linear pc_next; an untaken\nbranch with an unaligned encoded target stays legal. Preserve nret=1\nand all memory and RVFI ports and invariant checks.\n\nRun existing pipeline tests plus targeted checks of both direct\nmisprediction directions, forwarded/load-dependent comparisons,\nJALR bit-zero clearing and bit-one faults, and prolonged independent\nbus stalls. Verify actual retired PC transitions, source values,\ncontiguous order, and no wrong-path side effects. Run unmodified\nformal and stalled cosimulation gates and canonical CoreMark CRC,\nUART, and marker validation. Expect 4,201,709 bracketed cycles;\nacceptance requires fitness above 135.25826 iterations/s, equivalent\nto more than 56.8316 MHz at that cycle count. The impact is currently\nan unmeasured prediction; divider feedback and multiply timing can\nlimit the gain after branch recovery is shortened.\n'\"'''\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Preselect redirect_target from instruction class and the captured\npredicted_taken bit, and factor redirect qualification into legal\nconditional-branch, direct-JAL, and aligned-JALR cases. Keep the\nexisting actual-outcome pc_next, trap generation, training, target\narithmetic, forwarding, EX acceptance, and pipeline schedule.\nRemove only helper signals made unused by this equivalent rewrite.\n'''},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Preserve existing tests and extend control-flow checks for both\nmisprediction directions, correctly predicted transfers, forwarded\nand loaded branch/JALR operands, sign boundaries, reserved branch\nencodings, and taken/untaken misaligned targets. Exercise independent\ninstruction/data stalls around recovery and assert matching retired\nPCs, RVFI operands/order, and suppression of wrong-path side effects.\nDo not assert a particular inactive redirect_target value.\n'''}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False, width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and validated hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
