{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r6s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Flatten EX forwarding and ALU operand selection'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 129.31 iterations/s at 54.331 MHz and 4,201,709\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh Gowin run reproduced the reported\n25.514 ns register-file-to-branch-recovery path. Detailed timing shows\nseveral operand-selection LUTs and routing delays before the actual\ncomparison. The same operand network feeds arithmetic and address\npaths, so reducing this shared delay can help competing endpoints.\nPrior micro_opt successes preserved instruction latency, while the\nr5s1 blocking multiplier lost useful throughput to extra EX waits.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Flatten the EX-stage operand-selection network into mutually exclusive\nmasked data terms. Decode each existing forwarding selector into\nEX/MEM, MEM/WB, and register-file selects, preserving the default\nregister-file case and the existing EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority.\nForm raw rs1/rs2 as the OR of three masked sources. Keep these raw\nforwarded values for branch comparison, stores, effective addresses,\nJALR, captured divide operands, and RVFI.\n\nFor alu_a, build a separate four-source masked OR directly from\nEX/MEM, MEM/WB, the captured register-file value, and PC. AND the three\nregister-source selects with \"'!is_auipc; the fourth select is is_auipc.\nFor alu_b use the same construction with !alu_src on its three\nregister-source selects and alu_src on the immediate. Express each\nfour-term OR as two pairs then a final OR. Do not feed the general\nALU operand through an already formed raw-rs mux followed by another\nwide PC/immediate mux. The intended change is early narrow control\ncombination and one data selection level before arithmetic.\n\nThis is a local combinational rewrite in ex_stage.sv. Keep the encoded\nforward_unit interface, comparison priority, all pipeline bundles and\nregister enables, original ALU/divider/multiplier implementations,\npredictor/recovery policy, dedicated effective_addr, and nret=1 ports.\nNo operation changes latency or acquires a new execution wait. Keep\nheld MEM/WB forwarding available even when retirement valid is clear,\nand preserve saved divider operands and reset/bubble behavior.\n\nValidate the existing pipeline suite and extend forwarded-operand\ncoverage across every source and override: newest-writer priority,\nx0, EX/MEM and held MEM/WB, AUIPC after apparent dependencies,\nimmediate ALU instructions, loads/stores, shifts, signed/unsigned\ncomparisons, MUL and DIV launch, and branch/JALR operands. Exercise\nindependent bus stalls and verify exact RVFI source values, results,\naddresses, PC transitions, and contiguous retirement order.\nRun unchanged formal and stalled cosimulation gates and canonical\nCoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks. Expect 4,201,709 bracketed cycles;\nacceptance requires more than 135.25826 iterations/s, equivalent to\n56.8316 MHz at that count. The expected gain is not yet measured;\nGowin may refactor the masks into muxes, and divider feedback can\nlimit the eventual clock gain.\n'\"'''\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Decode existing forwarding selections into mutually exclusive masks,\nform raw rs1/rs2 by three-source masked OR, and independently form\nalu_a/alu_b by four-source masked OR with PC/immediate controls\ncombined into the masks. Preserve all consumers of raw forwarded\noperands, operation results, launch capture, hazards, and controls.\n'''},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Preserve all tests and add dependency/override sequences covering\nEX/MEM, MEM/WB, register-file and x0 sources; simultaneous matching\nwriters; PC/immediate overrides; and held WB forwarding under data\nstalls. Cover arithmetic, multiply/divide launches, memory addresses,\nstores, branches and JALR with exact RVFI and once-only effects.\n'''}]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda du,v: du.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',v,style='|' if '\\\\n' in v else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and validated hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
