{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r6s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Share one combinational signed-extended multiplier without EX waits'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 129.31 iterations/s at 54.331 MHz with 4,201,709\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. The current ALU separately expresses\nsigned-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned products,\nconsuming six DSP resources in the timed design. The r5s1 shared\nblocking multiplier reached 56.523 MHz and two DSP resources, but\ntwo extra wait cycles per multiply added 4.46 percent to CoreMark\ncycles and left fitness below the current champion. Sharing the\narithmetic without changing latency is the micro_opt opportunity.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the three combinational multiply expressions in alu.sv with\none signed 33-by-33 product. Construct mul_a as {sign_a,a}, where\nsign_a is a[31] for MULH/MULHSU and zero otherwise. Construct mul_b\nas {sign_b,b}, where sign_b is b[31] for MULH and zero otherwise.\nDeclare both operands signed [32:0] and the result signed [65:0],\nand multiply these correctly typed operands once. MUL reads [31:0];\nMULH/MULHU/MULHSU all read [63:32]. Bits [65:64] are redundant\nextension for the requested 64-bit RV32M product, not result bits.\nUnsigned 32-bit inputs must retain a leading zero before conversion\nto signed, so values at or above 0x80000000 are not misinterpreted.\n\nRetain single-cycle combinational multiplication and the existing\nEX/MEM result capture, writeback, and forwarding. Do not add operand\nor result registers, a multiply handshake, or execute_wait conditions.\nThe local area/routing reduction and elimination of selection among\nthree distinct product cones are intended to raise Fmax at unchanged\nCoreMark cycles. Preserve the existing full unmasked effective-address\npath, ALU base operations and division handshake, divider schedule,\nbranch prediction/recovery, bus stalls, nret=1 interface, and all RVFI\nsemantics. Keep all four existing multiplication ALTOPS formulas\nunchanged; the real product must not replace those formulas in formal.\n\nRun real-arithmetic ALU tests for all four multiply operations, including\nzero, all ones, INT_MIN, INT_MAX, opposite signed quadrants, unsigned\nhigh-bit operands, and random 32-bit pairs, checked against a Python\ninteger reference. Verify immediate opcode/operand changes without a\nrequest handshake. Retain every existing test and test forwarded\nmultiply sources and consumers, x0, consecutive mixed multiply kinds,\nand surrounding instruction/data stalls. Run unchanged formal and\nstalled cosimulation plus canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker checks.\n\nExpect the same 4,201,709 bracketed cycles. Acceptance requires more\nthan 135.25826 iterations/s, or 56.8316 MHz at this count. The gain is\ncurrently an unmeasured prediction. Mapping a 33-bit signed product,\nits operation-dependent sign bits, and competing branch/divider paths\nmay limit or erase the benefit; use median vendor timing, not DSP\ncount alone, as the deciding evidence.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Replace mul_ss/mul_uu/mul_su with a single signed 33-by-33 product\nusing operation-dependent sign-extension bits. Select the low or\nhigh 32-bit slice as specified. Preserve combinational latency,\nmodule ports, every ALTOPS formula, all nonmultiply operations,\nand existing divider handshakes. Document signed widths and avoid\nunused-bit lint warnings without weakening verification.\n'''},{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Preserve all current tests and strengthen exact-result coverage of\nall four combinational multiply operations with deterministic random\nfull-width pairs, sign-boundary/high-half cases, and rapid operation\nchanges. Use independent Python integer products with explicit\nsigned/unsigned operand interpretation, retaining ALTOPS checks.\n'''},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Preserve all existing tests and cover dependent/consecutive mixed\nmultiply operations, ALU/load/WB-forwarded operands, consumers that\nstore or branch, x0 destinations, and independent instruction/data\nstalls. Check exact results, RVFI operands/order, once-only side\neffects, and unchanged nonblocking multiply schedule.\n'''}]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda du,v: du.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',v,style='|' if '\\\\n' in v else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and validated hypothesis')\nPY\nNRET=1 make cosim-build TARGET=bench > cores/bench/generated/shared_mul_cosim_build.log 2>&1\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
