l latency.\n'''},{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Update divider-latency documentation to eleven internal clocks and\nnext-available-edge transfer. Keep the ALU datapath, multiplier,\nbase operations, and divider interface unchanged.\n'''},{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Update divide-latency documentation to eleven internal clocks and\nearliest edge-twelve transfer; retain the existing blocking request,\ncompletion, saved-operand and forwarding logic without new states.\n'''},{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain all real-arithmetic and ALTOPS vectors. Update exact latency\nchecks to eleven internal clocks, extend reset-phase coverage, and\ncheck the final single-digit iteration with values differing only\nin the low two dividend bits and all possible final quotient digits.\nPreserve held-result and no-relaunch assertions.\n'''},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all existing architectural, predictor, and memory checks.\nUpdate only exact divide-latency expectations to the longer defined\nschedule and extend bounded test cycle budgets if needed. Exercise\nconsecutive/dependent divides, forwarded launch operands, mixed\noperations, stalled completion, reset cancellation, wrong-path\nsuppression, and strict once-only retirement and side effects.\n'''}]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda du,v: du.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',v,style='|' if '\\\\n' in v else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and validated hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated and validated hypothesis\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
