{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_103","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r6s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Use distributed register storage with validity-gated read selection'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 129.31 iterations/s at 54.331 MHz and 4,201,709\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh Gowin run reproduced its 25.514 ns\nworst path starting at the register-file BSRAM output and traversing\noperand selection and branch recovery. The recent micro_opt history\nshows that separating effective addresses exposed this path without\nadding cycles; the blocking multiplier lost throughput to extra waits.\nThe present 32-by-32 register array has a bulk synchronous reset and\nis mapped into block RAM with absorbed operand registers. A local\nstorage/reset rewrite can restore a faster ID/EX launch boundary\nwhile preserving the exact architectural register-file interface.\n'''\ns=d['hypothesis']\na=s.index('An initial distributed-RAM prototype')\ns=s[:a]+'''An isolated prototype of the described distributed storage and masked\nread selection measured 54.908/57.319/57.319 MHz across the unchanged\nGowin placement options, for a 57.319 MHz median. Placement-0 resources\nwere 3,805 logic cells, 806 FFs, 32 LUT-RAM, four BSRAM and six DSPs,\ncompared with the champion's 3,772/826/8/6/6. Timing reports now show\nID/EX or forwarding registers launching the limiting EX paths instead\nof the register-file BSRAM output; divider feedback also limits timing.\n\nThe existing register-file and pipeline cocotb suites passed. Reference\ncosimulation passed selftest and all three random programs both with\nand without instruction/data stalls. The stalled canonical CoreMark\nrun retained exactly 4,201,709 bracketed cycles (markers 15,053 and\n4,216,762), reached EBREAK with oob=false, and passed the canonical\nfive-CRC/UART validation including the required success literal.\nCombining measured cycles and median Fmax gives 136.4183 iterations/s,\n5.50 percent above 129.31 and above the 135.25826 acceptance threshold.\nThese are prototype measurements, not a completed orchestrator result.\nThe margin over acceptance is modest; reproduce this exact narrow\nrewrite and run every unchanged correctness and timing gate. Do not\ncombine it with comparator, divider, predictor or multiplier changes.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']=s\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'medium'}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda du,v: du.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',v,style='|' if '\\\\n' in v else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261001-001-r6s0' and d['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Final hypothesis saved and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
