{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r6s1.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261001-002-r6s1\ntitle: \\\"Shorten divider recurrence and move correction to held completion\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 129.31 iterations/s at median 54.331 MHz and\n  4,201,709 bracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh unchanged-core Gowin run\n  reproduces its 25.514 ns branch-recovery path and a nearly tied\n  25.480 ns divider feedback path. Prior structural divider staging\n  produced large gains without changing measured CoreMark cycles;\n  blocking multiplication instead charged cycles to a common operation.\n  Three serial radix-4 digit selections remain in the divider recurrence.\n  Shortening that recurrence must avoid chaining final sign correction\n  onto its last iteration or exceeding the unchanged liveness window.\nhypothesis: |\n  Repartition the shared divider into eight iteration clocks of two\n  radix-4 digits each, processing exactly 32 dividend bits. Replace the\n  peeled first-digit schedule with a uniform two-stage recurrence.\n  On request edge 1 capture signed operand magnitudes, original dividend,\n  sign/operation flags, and exceptional-case flags. Compute and register\n  the full 34-bit 3D multiple from the normalized divisor on this same\n  edge; D and 2D remain zero-extended wiring from the captured divisor.\n  This preparation is outside the reused remainder feedback network.\n\n  Reuse only two dependent radix-4 restoring stages, with parallel\n  full-width unsigned trials against D, 2D, and 3D in each stage and\n  one-hot selection of the largest fitting multiple. Keep 34-bit shifted\n  remainders and 35-bit trial differences with an explicit borrow bit.\n  On iteration edges 2 through 9 register quotient_step[2] and\n  remainder_step[2]. Enter DONE after iteration index 7. Do not peel,\n  skip, or repeat any dividend bits. Retain exact divide-by-zero,\n  INT_MIN/-1 overflow, signed truncation, and remainder-sign behavior.\n\n  Move sign correction and final quotient/remainder selection out of\n  the iteration-to-register path. In DONE, drive the result\n  combinationally from the now-stable quotient/remainder registers and\n  captured flags. EX/MEM itself captures this corrected result on the\n  result-valid/result-ready transfer edge, earliest edge 10. Do not add\n  a separate CORRECT clock or feed correction from quotient_step or\n  remainder_step: either would defeat the intended schedule or timing.\n  Keep all completion-source registers unchanged while DONE is blocked,\n  so result_valid and the corrected result remain stable until consumed.\n  DONE returns to IDLE only on result_ready; reset cancels the operation.\n\n  Preserve EX's existing once-only request/completion handshake, saved\n  forwarded operands for RVFI, downstream draining, data-memory hold\n  priority, and full EX/MEM bubbles during execute_wait. The only\n  instruction-latency change is one additional wait cycle per divide or\n  remainder, with earliest transfer at edge 10 instead of edge 9.\n  MUL and base ALU behavior, prediction, dedicated effective addresses,\n  all top-level nret=1 ports, and retirement order remain unchanged.\n  Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS use captured operands and all four original\n  XOR formulas with exactly the same eight iteration clocks and held\n  DONE/result transfer schedule. No correctness gate or formal depth\n  may change; specifically verify consecutive divides against the\n  existing liveness check.\n\n  Expect an 8 percent fitness increase with medium confidence. The\n  intended gain comes from two digit selections between feedback\n  registers and removing the separate corrected-result register;\n  input normalization plus 3D preparation and remaining branch/multiply\n  paths are the principal risks. Measure actual canonical stalled\n  CoreMark cycles and all three vendor placement options. Acceptance\n  requires more than 135.25826 iterations/s. Validate all arithmetic\n  vectors, ALTOPS scheduling, held completion, reset, unmodified formal,\n  reference cosimulation, and canonical CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: |\n      Use two radix-4 stages for eight uniform iterations. Prepare and\n      register 3D from the normalized divisor on request capture. Remove\n      the peeled digit and separate CORRECT/result-register stage; expose\n      corrected stable registered quotient/remainder state in DONE until\n      consumption. Keep precise widths, all exceptional cases, reset,\n      and identical real/ALTOPS control timing. Earliest transfer is edge 10.\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Keep arithmetic and interface unchanged; update divider latency and\n      completion documentation to describe the held-state corrected result\n      captured by EX/MEM. Ensure no new combinational recurrence is added.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Preserve the blocking handshake and forwarding behavior; document\n      the one additional divide wait cycle and EX/MEM as the final\n      correction register. Do not add a completion or acceptance bubble.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve all arithmetic vectors and reference assertions. Update\n      exact latency expectations to request edge 1, eight iteration edges\n      2..9, and earliest consumption at edge 10 in real and ALTOPS builds.\n      Extend reset coverage and verify stable held completion while live\n      operands change. Cover normalization, 3D overflow, all quotient digit\n      positions, signed extremes, zero divisors, and back-to-back operations.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve architectural assertions and add consecutive and dependent\n      divides with ALU/load/WB-forwarded operands and independent bus stalls.\n      Check original RVFI operands, exact results, contiguous once-only\n      retirement, no repeated stores, reset cancellation, and bounded\n      progress. Adapt only latency-specific expectations to edge 10.\n''')\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised structural hypothesis written and schema validated')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
