{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|hyp-20261001-003-r[23]s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Compact bimodal branch prediction with immediate direct targets\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline fetches sequentially and redirects every taken branch and jump\\nfrom EX. Although described as five stages, IF/ID is combinational, so each\\nsuch redirect discards one younger fetch slot. Repeated loops and direct\\njumps in CoreMark therefore incur avoidable bubbles on top of the roughly\\n22 percent bus stalls. The sole recorded experiment is the baseline; there\\nare no prior predictor attempts or LESSONS.md. Its reported critical path\\ncrosses forwarding and the combinational ALU, so a small predictor can\\nimprove iterations per cycle without attempting to change that arithmetic\\npath. Any frequency benefit is excluded from the expected gain.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline fetches sequentially and redirects every taken branch and jump\\nfrom EX. Although described as five stages, IF/ID is combinational, so each\\nsuch redirect discards one younger fetch slot. Repeated loops and direct\\njumps in CoreMark therefore incur avoidable bubbles on top of the roughly\\n22 percent bus stalls. The sole recorded experiment is the baseline; there\\nare no prior predictor attempts or LESSONS.md. Its reported critical path\\ncrosses forwarding and the combinational ALU, so a small predictor can\\nimprove iterations per cycle without attempting to change that arithmetic\\npath. Any frequency benefit is excluded from the expected gain.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one compact next-PC prediction mechanism to the existing combinational\\nfetch/decode stage: a 64-entry table of two-bit saturating direction counters\\nindexed by fetch PC[7:2], reset to weakly taken (2'b10).