{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|bimodal|return|gshare|target buffer' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Compact bimodal branch prediction with immediate direct targets\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline fetches sequentially and redirects every taken branch and jump\\nfrom EX. Although described as five stages, IF/ID is combinational, so each\\nsuch redirect discards one younger fetch slot. Repeated loops and direct\\njumps in CoreMark therefore incur avoidable bubbles on top of the roughly\\n22 percent bus stalls. The sole recorded experiment is the baseline; there\\nare no prior predictor attempts or LESSONS.md. Its reported critical path\\ncrosses forwarding and the combinational ALU, so a small predictor can\\nimprove iterations per cycle without attempting to change that arithmetic\\npath. Any frequency benefit is excluded from the expected gain.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline fetches sequentially and redirects every taken branch and jump\\nfrom EX. Although described as five stages, IF/ID is combinational, so each\\nsuch redirect discards one younger fetch slot. Repeated loops and direct\\njumps in CoreMark therefore incur avoidable bubbles on top of the roughly\\n22 percent bus stalls. The sole recorded experiment is the baseline; there\\nare no prior predictor attempts or LESSONS.md. Its reported critical path\\ncrosses forwarding and the combinational ALU, so a small predictor can\\nimprove iterations per cycle without attempting to change that arithmetic\\npath. Any frequency benefit is excluded from the expected gain.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one compact next-PC prediction mechanism to the existing combinational\\nfetch/decode stage: a 64-entry table of two-bit saturating direction counters\\nindexed by fetch PC[7:2], reset to weakly taken (2'b10). For a legal BRANCH\\nencoding, use the counter MSB and compute its target directly from the\\ncurrent instruction's sign-extended B immediate. Predict legal JAL taken\\nusing its J immediate. Permit taken predictions only for word-aligned\\ndirect targets. All other instructions, including JALR, predict PC\n…[70748 of 73820 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:06bc0cb0acadd2ea]…\ness\": 113.55, \"delta_pct\": 12.03, \"vs_baseline\": 836.88, \"fmax_mhz\": 47.71, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4201709, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3630, \"ff\": 794, \"seeds\": [50.031, 47.71, 47.71], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.031, 12], [1, 47.71, 12], [2, 47.71, 12]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -14.988, \"arrival_ns\": 25.282, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T20:18:14.908708Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r4s2 (improvement, +12.03%): On the radix-4 core, 64-entry bimodal BRANCH/JAL prediction and recovery at the ID/EX boundary combine fetch-bubble reduction with removal of the EX-redirect-to-decode/load-use dependency, improving CoreMark fitness without changing divider latency.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
