{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt' or '-r8s1' in d['id']:\n  print(d['id'], d['title'],d.get('outcome'),d.get('fitness'), d.get('fmax_mhz'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict): print(h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  if d.get('implementation_notes'): print('NOTES', d['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-060f5a0 Baseline retest for cores/bench improvement 12.12 5.442\n\nhyp-20261001-001-r1s0 Shared radix-4 combinational DIV/REM datapath regression 12.8 5.749\nReplace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic inside alu.sv with one\nshared, fully combinational unsigned radix-4 restoring divmod network,\nsurrounded by RV32M signed-magnitude conversion and result correction.\nThis is a local arithmetic implementation change: keep the ALU ports,\nzero-cycle combinational latency, pipeline, forwarding, bus stalls,\nretirement width, and all non-division operations unchanged.\n\nConsume the dividend from most significant to least significant in\nsixteen two-bit digits. Precompute unsigned D, 2D, and 3D at 34 bits\nwithout truncating their high bits. At each stage form T = (R << 2)\n| next_digit, and compute T-D, T-2D, and T-3D in parallel. Select the\nlargest digit whose subtraction has no borrow, or digit zero with\nremainder T. Use subtraction carry/borrow to select the digit rather\nthan a separate magnitude comparison followed by subtraction. Emit\nboth the quotient digits and the final remainder from this one network;\ndo not implement remainder with a second divider or a quotient multiply.\n\nMake the sixteen stages explicit with compile-time bounds so synthesis\nsees their widths. After consuming k digits, the remainder is bounded\nby the consumed 2k-bit dividend prefix. Stage k therefore needs a\n2k-bit trial value and a 2k+1-bit unsigned subtraction. A candidate\nmultiple of D is eligible only if all its bits above that 2k-bit width\nare zero AND its subtraction has no borrow. This high-bit guard is\nrequired for correctness when the divisor is larger than the prefix;\ntruncating the divisor without the guard is incorrect. Keep only the\nselected low 2k remainder bits for the next stage. This produces\nsixteen dependent digit-selection stages with increasing arithmetic\nwidth instead of a conventional thirty-two-step binary division chain.\n\nFor DIV and REM, convert negative operands to unsigned 32-bit magnitudes,\nincluding \n…[40362 of 43434 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:29117bd45383be64]…\n. Option 0 used 4,320 logic cells, 852 FFs, 49 LUT-RAM,\nfour BSRAM and six DSPs. The leading post-route paths moved into the\nunchanged radix-8 divider recurrence. Canonical stalled CoreMark\npassed every CRC/UART, bounds, completion and marker check in exactly\n3,977,318 bracketed cycles, projecting 160.824455 iterations/s or\n4.6353 percent above the stated 153.70 champion. Lint, both existing\npipeline variants (29 cocotb cases each), and reference cosimulation\nof selftest plus three random programs with and without stalls passed.\nAll 53 unchanged ALTOPS formal checks passed, including register\nconsistency, liveness, unique retirement order and PC forwarding.\nThe prototype only narrowly exceeds the 4.6 percent acceptance margin,\nso confidence is low and the implementation must reproduce the median\nvendor result and all unchanged correctness gates. These measurements\nare prototype evidence, not orchestrator acceptance. Preserve the exact\nregister boundaries and the single-field bubble override described above.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The history includes a failed byte carry-select divider rewrite, so I’m accounting for that result. I’ll investigate a different local change: a balanced borrow-prefix network for the current radix-8 trial subtractors, keeping the divide latency unchanged. Gowin timing will determine whether it helps."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r10s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r10s0',\n'title':'Shorten radix-8 trial subtraction with grouped borrow-prefix logic',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The current champion reaches 161.21 iterations/s at 64.119 MHz. Its reported worst path runs from divider quotient_q to remainder_q through 76 cells; the same recurrence dominates all three round-9 outcomes. Each of the two serial radix-8 stages currently waits for seven parallel full-width trial subtractions before selecting its next remainder. The round-3 byte carry-select attempt on six serial binary steps regressed to 24.392 MHz, so duplicating candidate differences and serial byte selection is not justified. This proposal instead targets the two-stage radix-8 implementation with a balanced group-borrow prefix and one selected-borrow difference per small slice.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the fourteen unsigned 35-bit trial subtractors in rtl/divider.sv with exact combinational grouped-borrow subtraction. Preserve both radix-8 stages, all seven divisor multiples, adjacent-fit one-hot digit selection, and the existing balanced masked remainder OR. This is an arithmetic implementation micro-optimization inside the current divider, with no new pipeline register or instruction-cycle change.\n\nPartition X=shifted and Y=kD into small fixed slices, initially four-bit groups with a three-bit top group. For each slice compute unsigned group generate G=(X_slice<Y_slice) and propagate P=(X_slice==Y_slice). With input borrow zero, compute every slice boundary borrow using an explicit balanced parallel prefix. Combine high and low groups as G_hi_lo=G_hi|(P_hi&G_lo), P_hi_lo=P_hi&P_lo; use static prefix distances 1, 2, 4 and 8 across the nine groups. Do not implement a linear chain of group borrows. Boundary borrow into slice j is the prefix generate for groups j-1 through zero.\n\nCompute each result slice using its original X and Y slice and the resolved incoming borrow, with explicitly widened unsigned local arithmetic. Concatenate the selected slice differences and the final outgoing borrow to reproduce exactly the original 36-bit expression {1'b0,X}-{1'b0,Y}. The final outgoing borrow supplies trial[35]; retain all high bits of X and of kD in borrow generation even though only trial[31:0] is used for the remainder. Do not truncate a 35-bit multiple, infer signed comparisons, or approximate quotient selection. Use a helper in the existing divider compilation unit. Avoid the prior duplicated byte carry-select candidates; let native short arithmetic handle each local difference after the parallel borrow calculation.\n\nPreserve capture/normalization at edge 1, first two dividend bits and registered 3D/5D/7D at edge 2, two radix-8 steps on each of edges 3 through 7, correction/result_valid at edge 8 and earliest transfer at edge 9. Preserve the identical ALTOPS control schedule and all existing substitution constants. Keep divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, signed quotient truncation and remainder sign, captured operands, reset cancellation and stable held completion unchanged. No forwarding, multiplier, predictor, memory, decoder, RVFI or external-port change is needed; nret remains 1.\n\nThe expected benefit is shorter trial-borrow and remainder feedback without any CoreMark cycle penalty. This is an unmeasured prediction, with medium confidence: extra prefix routing and group fanout can outweigh arithmetic depth reduction, and WB-to-EX paths may become limiting. Validate exact subtractor equivalence over arbitrary 35-bit operands, then real-arithmetic and ALTOPS ALU tests, unchanged formal and stalled cosimulation, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation. ALTOPS alone cannot verify the changed arithmetic. Inspect actual Gowin mapping and all normal placement options. Acceptance requires more than 168.62566 iterations/s, corresponding to approximately 67.069 MHz if the current 3,977,318 bracketed cycles remain unchanged; use measured cycles and median Fmax, not the fastest placement.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/divider.sv','description':'Replace the seven full-width trial subtractions in each of the two radix-8 steps with a local exact grouped-borrow-prefix helper. Use small unsigned slices, balanced prefix group generate/propagate, one local result subtraction per slice and the exact final borrow. Preserve every arithmetic width, divisor multiple, digit selection, state, handshake and ALTOPS schedule.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain all existing assertions and latency checks. Add directed and deterministic randomized real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU vectors exercising borrow propagation across every slice boundary, high divisor multiples, quotient digits 0 through 7, all signed quadrants, zero divisors and overflow. Retain capture, held completion and reset checks. Establish independent arbitrary-input equivalence of the helper to widened unsigned subtraction as additional validation; do not rely on ALTOPS for real arithmetic.'}\n]}\np.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Wrote and schema-validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
