ssign first_digit = (|divisor_q[31:7]) ? 7'b0 : prep_q[3];\n  assign first_remainder = (|divisor_q[31:7]) ? quotient_q[31:25] : prep_r[3];\n\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('i < 2','i < 1')\nb=s.index('\"'`endif'\"\\\\n\\\\n  always_ff')\ns=s[:b]+'''  // Second digit is radix four: five dividend bits per main clock.\n  logic [33:0] r4_shifted;\n  logic [34:0] r4_trial [1:3];\n  logic [3:0] r4_take;\n  logic [3:1] r4_fit;\n  assign r4_shifted = {remainder_step[1],quotient_step[1][31:30]};\n  assign r4_trial[1] = {1'b0,r4_shifted} - {3'b0,divisor_q};\n  assign r4_trial[2] = {1'b0,r4_shifted} - {2'b0,divisor_q,1'b0};\n  assign r4_trial[3] = {1'b0,r4_shifted} - divisor_three_q;\n  assign r4_fit = {\"'!r4_trial[3][34],!r4_trial[2][34],!r4_trial[1][34]};\n  assign r4_take = {r4_fit[3],r4_fit[2]&&!r4_fit[3],r4_fit[1]&&!r4_fit[2],!r4_fit[1]};\n  assign remainder_step[2] = (({32{r4_take[0]}} & r4_shifted[31:0]) |\n                              ({32{r4_take[1]}} & r4_trial[1][31:0])) |\n                             (({32{r4_take[2]}} & r4_trial[2][31:0]) |\n                              ({32{r4_take[3]}} & r4_trial[3][31:0]));\n  assign quotient_step[2] = {quotient_step[1][29:0],r4_take[2]|r4_take[3],r4_take[1]|r4_take[3]};\n'\"'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('{quotient_q[29:0], first_digit}','{quotient_q[24:0], first_digit}').replace(\\\"{30'b0, first_remainder}\\\",\\\"{25'b0, first_remainder}\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint(rtl)\nPY\npython cores/bench/generated/r10s0_probe/mixed_probe.py\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('cores/bench/generated/r10s0_probe')\nr=build('.',p/'mixed_rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',1,p/'mixed_p1')\n(p/'mixed_p1.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2))\nprint(json.dumps(r,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_17", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r10s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Rebalance the fixed-latency divider into a seven-bit prefix and radix-8/radix-4 recurrence'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 161.21 iterations/s at 64.119 MHz, with its worst reported path traversing 76 cells inside the two-stage radix-8 divider recurrence. All round-9 variants expose that recurrence. Prior byte carry-select logic on six binary stages regressed, and a new exact grouped-borrow-prefix prototype on this parent also regressed to 37.228 MHz for placement option 1. Native arithmetic remains preferable. The existing preparation edge consumes only two dividend bits, leaving an opportunity to move narrow leading-bit work out of the full-width feedback path without extending latency.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Rebalance work inside the existing blocking divider, preserving its exact eight internal clocks and earliest edge-nine result transfer. On the existing preparation edge consume SEVEN leading dividend bits instead of two. On each of the next five iteration edges consume five bits using one radix-8 restoring stage followed by one radix-4 restoring stage, rather than two radix-8 stages. Exactly 7+5*5=32 dividend bits are consumed. This is one local arithmetic micro-optimization of the existing recurrence and preparation logic; no pipeline or protocol change is proposed.\n\nThe preparation dividend H is the captured normalized dividend[31:25]. If the full normalized divisor D is at least 128, emit quotient prefix zero and remainder H. Otherwise compute the exact seven-bit unsigned H/D quotient and H%D remainder with a small combinational network: peel the first bit, then three radix-4 steps with trial widths 3, 5 and 7. Precompute local D, 2D and 3D at nine bits. Guard each trial with zero high multiple bits before accepting its low-width subtraction; truncating an oversized multiple is incorrect. For the first bit D=1 consumes that bit and yields remainder zero; D>=2 emits digit zero and preserves the bit. D=0 may use deterministic all-fitting digits because the captured zero-divisor flag overrides the final result. The D>=128 bypass must inspect every divisor bit [31:7], never only the low seven. Register quotient_q={old_quotient_q[24:0],prefix_quotient} and remainder_q={25'b0,prefix_remainder} on edge 2. Register full-width 3D, 5D and 7D on that same edge exactly as before.\n\nKeep the first main radix-8 stage's seven parallel 36-bit unsigned trials against 35-bit multiples and its balanced one-hot selection. Replace the second main stage with radix four: T={R[31:0],Q[31:30]} is 34 bits; subtract D, 2D and 3D at 35-bit width so bit 34 is the borrow. All bits of the multiples participate. Use monotonic fits for exactly one of digits 0,1,2,3, balanced masked OR selection of the low 32 remainder bits, and append exactly two quotient bits. There are now ten full-width trial subtractors rather than fourteen; the second stage also has a narrower digit/remainder selection. Keep native subtract operators, avoiding the measured prefix/carry-select regressions.\n\nPreserve capture and signed normalization at edge 1, preparation at edge 2, five main iterations at edges 3 through 7, registered correction/result_valid at edge 8, and earliest result consumption at edge 9. Preserve identical control timing and constants under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS. Preserve all RV32M signed/unsigned results, zero-divisor handling, INT_MIN/-1, captured operands, reset cancellation, held DONE results, forwarding and every CPU invariant. Leave multiplier, pipeline, predictor, memory, decoder, nret=1 and top-level IO unchanged.\n\nTarget eight percent fitness improvement with medium confidence, from fewer wide trial subtractors and a simpler second selection without added cycles. This prediction is unmeasured; the narrow preparation network or existing EX paths could become limiting. Independently verify the preparation arithmetic for every seven-bit dividend and divisor including the high-divisor bypass, then test real and ALTOPS DIV/REM, existing formal and stalled cosimulation, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. Compare all three Gowin placement options using median Fmax and measured bracketed cycles. Acceptance requires more than 168.62566 iterations/s, approximately 67.069 MHz at unchanged 3,977,318 cycles. Do not weaken fixed formal depths, liveness or arithmetic checks.'''\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Replace the two-bit preparation peel with exact seven-bit quotient/remainder preparation and replace only the second radix-8 recurrence stage with radix four. Keep 35-bit registered multiples, explicit width/high-bit guards, balanced digit selection and the unchanged state/handshake/ALTOPS schedule. Update comments to document 7+5*5 dividend bits.'\nd['changes'][1]['description']='Retain every existing test and exact latency assertion. Add exhaustive small prefix cases and directed/random real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU vectors around divisors 0,1,2,3,127,128,129, powers of two, high divisor multiples, every radix-8/radix-4 digit and signed extrema. Verify large divisors sharing low seven bits cannot use the small-divisor result. Preserve launch, held completion, reset cancellation and ALTOPS coverage.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema-validated hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_17", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r10s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Rebalance the fixed-latency divider into a seven-bit prefix and radix-8/radix-4 recurrence'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 161.21 iterations/s at 64.119 MHz, with its worst reported path traversing 76 cells inside the two-stage radix-8 divider recurrence. All round-9 variants expose that recurrence. Prior byte carry-select logic on six binary stages regressed, and a new exact grouped-borrow-prefix prototype on this parent also regressed to 37.228 MHz for placement option 1. Native arithmetic remains preferable. The existing preparation edge consumes only two dividend bits, leaving an opportunity to move narrow leading-bit work out of the full-width feedback path without extending latency.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Rebalance work inside the existing blocking divider, preserving its exact eight internal clocks and earliest edge-nine result transfer. On the existing preparation edge consume SEVEN leading dividend bits instead of two. On each of the next five iteration edges consume five bits using one radix-8 restoring stage followed by one radix-4 restoring stage, rather than two radix-8 stages. Exactly 7+5*5=32 dividend bits are consumed. This is one local arithmetic micro-optimization of the existing recurrence and preparation logic; no pipeline or protocol change is proposed.\n\nThe preparation dividend H is the captured normalized dividend[31:25]. If the full normalized divisor D is at least 128, emit quotient prefix zero and remainder H. Otherwise compute the exact seven-bit unsigned H/D quotient and H%D remainder with a small combinational network: peel the first bit, then three radix-4 steps with trial widths 3, 5 and 7. Precompute local D, 2D and 3D at nine bits. Guard each trial with zero high multiple bits before accepting its low-width subtraction; truncating an oversized multiple is incorrect. For the first bit D=1 consumes that bit and yields remainder zero; D>=2 emits digit zero and preserves the bit. D=0 may use deterministic all-fitting digits because the captured zero-divisor flag overrides the final result. The D>=128 bypass must inspect every divisor bit [31:7], never only the low seven. Register quotient_q={old_quotient_q[24:0],prefix_quotient} and remainder_q={25'b0,prefix_remainder} on edge 2. Register full-width 3D, 5D and 7D on that same edge exactly as before.\n\nKeep the first main radix-8 stage's seven parallel 36-bit unsigned trials against 35-bit multiples and its balanced one-hot selection. Replace the second main stage with radix four: T={R[31:0],Q[31:30]} is 34 bits; subtract D, 2D and 3D at 35-bit width so bit 34 is the borrow. All bits of the multiples participate. Use monotonic fits for exactly one of digits 0,1,2,3, balanced masked OR selection of the low 32 remainder bits, and append exactly two quotient bits. There are now ten full-width trial subtractors rather than fourteen; the second stage also has a narrower digit/remainder selection. Keep native subtract operators, avoiding the measured prefix/carry-select regressions.\n\nPreserve capture and signed normalization at edge 1, preparation at edge 2, five main iterations at edges 3 through 7, registered correction/result_valid at edge 8, and earliest result consumption at edge 9. Preserve identical control timing and constants under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS. Preserve all RV32M signed/unsigned results, zero-divisor handling, INT_MIN/-1, captured operands, reset cancellation, held DONE results, forwarding and every CPU invariant. Leave multiplier, pipeline, predictor, memory, decoder, nret=1 and top-level IO unchanged.\n\nTarget eight percent fitness improvement with medium confidence, from fewer wide trial subtractors and a simpler second selection without added cycles. This prediction is unmeasured; the narrow preparation network or existing EX paths could become limiting. Independently verify the preparation arithmetic for every seven-bit dividend and divisor including the high-divisor bypass, then test real and ALTOPS DIV/REM, existing formal and stalled cosimulation, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. Compare all three Gowin placement options using median Fmax and measured bracketed cycles. Acceptance requires more than 168.62566 iterations/s, approximately 67.069 MHz at unchanged 3,977,318 cycles. Do not weaken fixed formal depths, liveness or arithmetic checks.'''\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Replace the two-bit preparation peel with exact seven-bit quotient/remainder preparation and replace only the second radix-8 recurrence stage with radix four. Keep 35-bit registered multiples, explicit width/high-bit guards, balanced digit selection and the unchanged state/handshake/ALTOPS schedule. Update comments to document 7+5*5 dividend bits.'\nd['changes'][1]['description']='Retain every existing test and exact latency assertion. Add exhaustive small prefix cases and directed/random real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU vectors around divisors 0,1,2,3,127,128,129, powers of two, high divisor multiples, every radix-8/radix-4 digit and signed extrema. Verify large divisors sharing low seven bits cannot use the small-divisor result. Preserve launch, held completion, reset cancellation and ALTOPS coverage.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema-validated hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated and schema-validated hypothesis\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
