{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"The balanced selector removes the divider from the leading paths, but its 64.342 MHz result is below the acceptance threshold. My final probe keeps the schedule and two-bit preparation step, but replaces the two radix-8 steps with one radix-64 step. It trades substantially more parallel arithmetic for removing the intermediate selection delay."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/generated/r10s0_probe/r64_probe.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nb=Path('cores/bench/generated/r10s0_probe');r=b/'r64_rtl';shutil.copytree('cores/bench/rtl',r,dirs_exist_ok=True)\np=r/'divider.sv';s=p.read_text()\na=s.index('  logic [34:0] divisor_three_q');z=s.index('  // Initially R=0',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''  logic [37:0] multiples [1:63];\n  logic [37:0] odd_q [1:31];\n  logic [1:0] first_digit, first_remainder;\n  assign multiples[1] = {6'b0,divisor_q};\n'''+''.join(f'  assign multiples[{k}] = '+(f'(multiples[{k//2}] << 1);\\\\n' if k%2==0 else f'odd_q[{k//2}];\\\\n') for k in range(2,64))+s[z:]\na=s.index('  logic [31:0] quotient_step');z=s.index('\"'`endif'\"\\\\n\\\\n  always_ff',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''  logic [37:0] shifted;\n  logic [38:0] trial [1:63];\n  logic [63:1] fit;\n  logic [37:0] select_tree [0:126];\n  logic [31:0] next_quotient,next_remainder;\n  assign shifted = {remainder_q,quotient_q[31:26]};\n  assign select_tree[63] = {6'b0,shifted[31:0]};\n  for (genvar k=1;k<64;k++) begin: trials\n    assign trial[k] = {1'b0,shifted} - {1'b0,multiples[k]};\n    assign fit[k] = \"'!trial[k][38];\n    assign select_tree[63+k] = {6'\"'(k),trial[k][31:0]};\n  end\n  for (genvar level=0;level<6;level++) begin: levels\n    for (genvar j=0;j<(1<<level);j++) begin: nodes\n      localparam integer NODE=(1<<level)-1+j;\n      localparam integer PIVOT=(2*j+1)*(32>>level);\n      assign select_tree[NODE] = fit[PIVOT] ? select_tree[2*NODE+2] : select_tree[2*NODE+1];\n    end\n  end\n  assign next_quotient = {quotient_q[25:0],select_tree[0][37:32]};\n  assign next_remainder = select_tree[0][31:0];\n'''+s[z:]\na=s.index(\\\"      divisor_three_q <= '0;\\\");z=s.index(\\\"      dividend_q <= '0;\\\",a)\ns=s[:a]+\\\"      for (int k=1;k<32;k++) odd_q[k] <= '0;\\\\n\\\"+s[z:]\na=s.index('            divisor_three_q <=');z=s.index('            quotient_q <=',a)\ndef balanced(xs):\n if len(xs)==1:return xs[0]\n n=len(xs)//2\n return '('+balanced(xs[:n])+' + '+balanced(xs[n:])+')'\ndef expr(k):\n digits=[];i=0\n while k:\n  if k%2:\n   d=2-(k%4); digits.append((i,d)); k-=d\n  k//=2;i+=1\n pos=[f'(multiples[1] << {i})' for i,d in digits if d==1];neg=[f'(multiples[1] << {i})' for i,d in digits if d==-1]\n e=balanced(pos)\n if neg:e+=' - '+balanced(neg)\n return e\ns=s[:a]+''.join(f'            odd_q[{k//2}] <= {expr(k)};\\\\n' for k in range(3,64,2))+s[z:]\ns=s.replace('quotient_step[2]','next_quotient').replace('remainder_step[2]','next_remainder')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython cores/bench/generated/r10s0_probe/r64_probe.py\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('cores/bench/generated/r10s0_probe');r=build('.',p/'r64_rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',1,p/'r64_p1')\n(p/'r64_p1.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2));print(json.dumps(r))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r10s0.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Collapse two serial radix-8 divider steps into one parallel radix-64 step'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 161.21 iterations/s at 64.119 MHz and its worst reported path crosses two serial radix-8 trial-subtract/select steps inside the divider. Prior byte carry-select logic regressed; new grouped-prefix, narrow-width and enlarged-preparation probes also failed to improve timing. A balanced radix-8 selector alone measured 64.342 MHz for placement option 1, below the acceptance margin. The remaining opportunity is to remove the entire intermediate remainder-selection dependency, using more parallel trial arithmetic while retaining native carry chains and the existing divider schedule.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the pair of serial radix-8 restoring steps with one radix-64 restoring step that consumes the same six dividend bits per main iteration. Preserve the original two-bit preparation peel and exactly five main iterations: 2+5*6=32 bits. This is a local unroll/radix micro-optimization of the existing clocked divider, with no added register stage, instruction latency or execution-policy change.\n\nUse unsigned 38-bit divisor multiples M[k]=k*D for k=1..63. M[1] is the captured normalized divisor zero-extended to 38 bits. Register the 31 odd multiples 3D,5D,...,63D during the existing preparation edge; derive every even multiple by a width-preserving left shift of the appropriate registered odd multiple or D. Calculate odd multiples from the captured D with explicit constant shifts and balanced add/subtract expressions, preferably minimal signed-digit expressions such as 7D=8D-D, 31D=32D-D and 63D=64D-D. Use only captured normalized D, never live EX operands or the previous request's registered multiples. All intermediate sums and shifts must be at least 38 bits: 64D fits in 38 bits for every 32-bit divisor. Do not infer variable multipliers for the multiple bank or add arithmetic to the recurrence to regenerate multiples.\n\nAt each of the five main edges form T={remainder_q[31:0],quotient_q[31:26]} at 38 bits. In parallel calculate 63 unsigned 39-bit differences {1'b0,T}-{1'b0,M[k]}; trial[k][38] is the borrow and fit[k]=\"'!trial[k][38]. Select the largest fitting k in 1..63, or zero when no multiple fits. Exploit monotonic fits with a balanced six-level binary mux tree: the root uses fit[32], its children fit[16] and fit[48], and subsequent levels use the midpoint of each remaining interval down to odd-index fits. Associate each leaf k with {six_bit_k,remainder_candidate}; candidate zero is T[31:0] and other candidates are trial[k][31:0]. Selecting quotient digit and remainder together avoids a serial encoded-digit-then-data-mux path. Do not use a 63-deep priority chain. For D>0, R<D implies T<64D and the selected remainder is again below D, so its low 32 bits are exact. For D=0 all fits are true and digit 63 wins; the existing captured zero-divisor override still provides the architectural result.\n\nRegister quotient_q={quotient_q[25:0],selected_digit} and the selected remainder at the same main iteration edges as today. Preserve capture/normalization at edge 1, the existing small two-bit first-digit network plus multiple-bank preparation at edge 2, five six-bit iterations on edges 3..7, correction/result_valid at edge 8 and earliest transfer at edge 9. Reset all new multiple registers consistently; no stale multiple may be used before preparation. Preserve every real RV32M exceptional result, signed truncation and remainder sign, request/held-completion/reset behavior, forwarded operand capture and original ALTOPS formulas and control timing. Leave multiplier, forwarding, predictor, memory, legality, nret=1 and top-level ports unchanged.\n\nThe expected benefit is removal of one full dependent subtraction and its intervening remainder selection. The cost is 63 parallel trials and 31 odd-multiple registers instead of 14 trials and three registered odd multiples. Area, divisor distribution, six-level selection routing, multiple preparation and competing EX paths may defeat the frequency gain; confidence is low until vendor timing confirms it. This is a predicted eight percent fitness improvement, not a measured accepted result. Validate all 64 quotient digits and thresholds, high multiples approaching 63*0xffffffff, all signed quadrants and exceptional inputs, original exact latency and backpressure tests, unchanged formal and stalled cosimulation, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. ALTOPS does not prove the new arithmetic. Use the normal three-option Gowin median and actual bracketed cycles; acceptance requires more than 168.62566 iterations/s, approximately 67.069 MHz at unchanged 3,977,318 cycles. Preserve every correctness gate and formal depth.'\"'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Replace the two-stage radix-8 recurrence with a single 63-trial radix-64 recurrence and balanced monotonic-fit selection tree. Expand preparation to register 31 full-width odd multiples using explicit shift/add/subtract expressions. Keep the existing two-bit peel, state machine, eight-clock latency, normalization/correction, request/completion and ALTOPS behavior.'\nd['changes'][1]['description']='Preserve all existing arithmetic and exact latency checks. Add directed and deterministic randomized tests for quotient digits 0..63 in every six-bit position, kD-1/kD/kD+1 boundaries, divisors with multiples above 32 bits, all signed quadrants, divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1. Preserve captured-input, held-result and reset cancellation coverage; independently verify balanced selection against largest-fitting-digit selection.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86));jsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Wrote schema-valid radix-64 hypothesis')\nPY\npython - <<'PY' > cores/bench/generated/r10s0_probe/r64_alu.log 2>&1\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/generated/r10s0_probe').resolve();sys.path.insert(0,str(Path('cores/bench/test').resolve()))\nimport _helpers,test_alu\n_helpers.RTL=p/'r64_rtl';_helpers.SIM_BUILD=p/'r64_sim_build';test_alu.RTL=_helpers.RTL;test_alu.SIM_BUILD=_helpers.SIM_BUILD\ntest_alu.test_alu_runner();test_alu.test_alu_altops_runner()\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
