vel ports unchanged.\n\nThe expected benefit is removal of one full dependent subtraction and its intervening remainder selection. The cost is 63 parallel trials and 31 odd-multiple registers instead of 14 trials and three registered odd multiples. Area, divisor distribution, six-level selection routing, multiple preparation and competing EX paths may defeat the frequency gain; confidence is low until vendor timing confirms it. This is a predicted eight percent fitness improvement, not a measured accepted result. Validate all 64 quotient digits and thresholds, high multiples approaching 63*0xffffffff, all signed quadrants and exceptional inputs, original exact latency and backpressure tests, unchanged formal and stalled cosimulation, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. ALTOPS does not prove the new arithmetic. Use the normal three-option Gowin median and actual bracketed cycles; acceptance requires more than 168.62566 iterations/s, approximately 67.069 MHz at unchanged 3,977,318 cycles. Preserve every correctness gate and formal depth.'\"'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Replace the two-stage radix-8 recurrence with a single 63-trial radix-64 recurrence and balanced monotonic-fit selection tree. Expand preparation to register 31 full-width odd multiples using explicit shift/add/subtract expressions. Keep the existing two-bit peel, state machine, eight-clock latency, normalization/correction, request/completion and ALTOPS behavior.'\nd['changes'][1]['description']='Preserve all existing arithmetic and exact latency checks. Add directed and deterministic randomized tests for quotient digits 0..63 in every six-bit position, kD-1/kD/kD+1 boundaries, divisors with multiples above 32 bits, all signed quadrants, divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1. Preserve captured-input, held-result and reset cancellation coverage; independently verify balanced selection against largest-fitting-digit selection.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86));jsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Wrote schema-valid radix-64 hypothesis')\nPY\npython - <<'PY' > cores/bench/generated/r10s0_probe/r64_alu.log 2>&1\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/generated/r10s0_probe').resolve();sys.path.insert(0,str(Path('cores/bench/test').resolve()))\nimport _helpers,test_alu\n_helpers.RTL=p/'r64_rtl';_helpers.SIM_BUILD=p/'r64_sim_build';test_alu.RTL=_helpers.RTL;test_alu.SIM_BUILD=_helpers.SIM_BUILD\ntest_alu.test_alu_runner();test_alu.test_alu_altops_runner()\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Wrote schema-valid radix-64 hypothesis\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
