{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r10s0.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Replace radix-8 adjacent-fit masking with balanced monotonic-fit selection'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 161.21 iterations/s at 64.119 MHz and its reported worst path crosses two radix-8 subtract/select stages. Prior byte carry-select logic regressed. On this parent, grouped-prefix, enlarged-preparation, narrowed-trial and radix-64 probes also failed to improve timing. Direct balanced selection preserves the small native subtractors and is the strongest observed isolated divider change: a two-stage selector prototype measured 64.342 MHz for placement option 1, with the leading paths moving to WB/EX and branch recovery. That probe does not clear the 4.6 percent acceptance margin.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the remainder and quotient digit selection in the current radix-8 divider with balanced selection driven directly by monotonic fit predicates. Keep all seven full-width native subtractions in each stage, the original registered 35-bit divisor multiples, and the original two-bit preparation peel. Do not use the regressing narrowed-arithmetic, carry-prefix or radix-64 variants.\n\nIn each stage fit[k]=\"'!trial[k][35], for k=1..7. Select trial 6 or 7 with fit[7], trial 4 or 5 with fit[5], and select those pairs with fit[6]. Similarly select trial 2 or 3 with fit[3], shifted or trial 1 with fit[1], and select those pairs with fit[2]. Finally select the upper or lower half with fit[4]. All candidates use their low 32 bits. This is a balanced three-level mux tree whose control fits are computed in parallel, not a seven-deep priority chain. Derive quotient bit 2 as fit[4], bit 1 as fit[4]?fit[6]:fit[2], and bit 0 as fit[4]?(fit[6]?fit[7]:fit[5]):(fit[2]?fit[3]:fit[1]). The ordered multiples make the fit vector monotonic; the tree therefore chooses exactly the largest fitting digit. D=0 makes all fits true and chooses digit seven, with the unchanged final zero-divisor override providing the architectural answer.\n\nThe intent is to remove adjacent-fit take[k] generation, candidate masking and eight-way OR reduction from the dependent remainder path, allowing the FPGA mapper to use direct hierarchical muxes. This is one local arithmetic-selector micro-optimization. Preserve 2+5*6=32 consumed bits and every state/handshake: edge 1 captures/normalizes, edge 2 peels two bits and registers odd multiples, edges 3..7 iterate, edge 8 corrects and asserts result_valid, and edge 9 is the earliest consumption. Preserve ALTOPS arithmetic and schedule, signed and unsigned corner cases, reset cancellation and held completion. Leave all other RTL, nret=1, decoder legality, memory, forwarding, prediction and verification contracts unchanged.\n\nThe placement-option-1 prototype used 4,053 logic cells, 893 FFs, 49 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and six DSPs, at 64.342 MHz. This is approximately 0.35 percent frequency improvement, not an accepted candidate and not a three-option median. Six percent remains an unproven target with low confidence; competing EX paths and placement sensitivity are the major risks. The implementer must retain the single selector focus and measure the complete normal vendor median before claiming a gain. Acceptance requires more than 168.62566 iterations/s, approximately 67.069 MHz at unchanged 3,977,318 bracketed cycles.\n\nValidate selection equivalence for all eight monotonic patterns of seven fit bits and arbitrary candidate data. Run real and ALTOPS ALU vectors with unchanged latency checks, existing pipeline/formal and stalled reference cosimulation, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks, and all normal Gowin placement options. ALTOPS alone cannot prove real arithmetic. Do not weaken any gate or formal depth and do not claim acceptance from a best placement result.'\"'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Replace adjacent-fit one-hot remainder selection in the radix-8 steps with the exact balanced fit[4]/fit[2,6]/fit[1,3,5,7] tree and derive quotient digits from the same decisions. Preserve full-width trials, multiple preparation and all control timing.'\nd['changes'][1]['description']='Preserve all existing assertions and exact timing checks. Add all eight monotonic fit patterns and quotient digits 0..7, threshold equality/off-by-one cases, high divisor multiples, signed quadrants and D=0. Verify the selector against largest-fitting-digit selection and retain captured-input, backpressure and reset tests.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86));jsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Current hypothesis schema validated')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r10s0.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Replace radix-8 adjacent-fit masking with balanced monotonic-fit selection'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 161.21 iterations/s at 64.119 MHz and its reported worst path crosses two radix-8 subtract/select stages. Prior byte carry-select logic regressed. On this parent, grouped-prefix, enlarged-preparation, narrowed-trial and radix-64 probes also failed to improve timing. Direct balanced selection preserves the small native subtractors and is the strongest observed isolated divider change: a two-stage selector prototype measured 64.342 MHz for placement option 1, with the leading paths moving to WB/EX and branch recovery. That probe does not clear the 4.6 percent acceptance margin.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the remainder and quotient digit selection in the current radix-8 divider with balanced selection driven directly by monotonic fit predicates. Keep all seven full-width native subtractions in each stage, the original registered 35-bit divisor multiples, and the original two-bit preparation peel. Do not use the regressing narrowed-arithmetic, carry-prefix or radix-64 variants.\n\nIn each stage fit[k]=\"'!trial[k][35], for k=1..7. Select trial 6 or 7 with fit[7], trial 4 or 5 with fit[5], and select those pairs with fit[6]. Similarly select trial 2 or 3 with fit[3], shifted or trial 1 with fit[1], and select those pairs with fit[2]. Finally select the upper or lower half with fit[4]. All candidates use their low 32 bits. This is a balanced three-level mux tree whose control fits are computed in parallel, not a seven-deep priority chain. Derive quotient bit 2 as fit[4], bit 1 as fit[4]?fit[6]:fit[2], and bit 0 as fit[4]?(fit[6]?fit[7]:fit[5]):(fit[2]?fit[3]:fit[1]). The ordered multiples make the fit vector monotonic; the tree therefore chooses exactly the largest fitting digit. D=0 makes all fits true and chooses digit seven, with the unchanged final zero-divisor override providing the architectural answer.\n\nThe intent is to remove adjacent-fit take[k] generation, candidate masking and eight-way OR reduction from the dependent remainder path, allowing the FPGA mapper to use direct hierarchical muxes. This is one local arithmetic-selector micro-optimization. Preserve 2+5*6=32 consumed bits and every state/handshake: edge 1 captures/normalizes, edge 2 peels two bits and registers odd multiples, edges 3..7 iterate, edge 8 corrects and asserts result_valid, and edge 9 is the earliest consumption. Preserve ALTOPS arithmetic and schedule, signed and unsigned corner cases, reset cancellation and held completion. Leave all other RTL, nret=1, decoder legality, memory, forwarding, prediction and verification contracts unchanged.\n\nThe placement-option-1 prototype used 4,053 logic cells, 893 FFs, 49 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and six DSPs, at 64.342 MHz. This is approximately 0.35 percent frequency improvement, not an accepted candidate and not a three-option median. Six percent remains an unproven target with low confidence; competing EX paths and placement sensitivity are the major risks. The implementer must retain the single selector focus and measure the complete normal vendor median before claiming a gain. Acceptance requires more than 168.62566 iterations/s, approximately 67.069 MHz at unchanged 3,977,318 bracketed cycles.\n\nValidate selection equivalence for all eight monotonic patterns of seven fit bits and arbitrary candidate data. Run real and ALTOPS ALU vectors with unchanged latency checks, existing pipeline/formal and stalled reference cosimulation, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks, and all normal Gowin placement options. ALTOPS alone cannot prove real arithmetic. Do not weaken any gate or formal depth and do not claim acceptance from a best placement result.'\"'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Replace adjacent-fit one-hot remainder selection in the radix-8 steps with the exact balanced fit[4]/fit[2,6]/fit[1,3,5,7] tree and derive quotient digits from the same decisions. Preserve full-width trials, multiple preparation and all control timing.'\nd['changes'][1]['description']='Preserve all existing assertions and exact timing checks. Add all eight monotonic fit patterns and quotient digits 0..7, threshold equality/off-by-one cases, high divisor multiples, signed quadrants and D=0. Verify the selector against largest-fitting-digit selection and retain captured-input, backpressure and reset tests.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86));jsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Current hypothesis schema validated')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Current hypothesis schema validated\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
