{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_36", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r11s0',\n'title':'Register the final writeback value before WB forwarding',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 185.62 iterations/s at 74.054 MHz with 3,989,539 bracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh option-0 vendor timing run reproduces the logged 71.761 MHz and WB load-data-to-fetch-PC critical path. Its next competitive paths include WB-to-EX ALU results. WB currently selects between two registered data banks before forwarding. The r9s0 micro-optimization moved this selection before the register but was limited by the old radix-8 divider; the champion has since removed that competing limit with the radix-32 divider and captured multiply operands. This makes a focused retest of writeback selection retiming justified.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Move the existing load-versus-ALU writeback selection from after MEM/WB to immediately before MEM/WB. Replace the two 32-bit MEM/WB fields alu_result and read_data with a single 32-bit wb_data field. On every ordinary MEM/WB advance capture:\n  reg_q.wb_data <= in.ctrl.mem_to_reg ? load_data : in.alu_result;\nUse the existing byte/halfword sign- or zero-extended load_data, not raw dmem_rdata. In wb_stage drive w_data directly from in.wb_data; keep w_en=in.ctrl.reg_write&&in.valid and w_addr=in.rd unchanged.\n\nThis is one local mux-retiming and redundant-data-bank micro-optimization. It removes the WB output mux from branch recovery, effective-address generation, ALU forwarding and register-file bypass paths while deleting 32 redundant payload flops. It adds no pipeline stage or instruction cycles. Do not combine it with comparator rewrites, EX bubble changes, predictor changes or arithmetic-unit changes.\n\nReset must clear wb_data. A data-memory hold must retain wb_data together with the destination and control fields while clearing only valid, exactly as today. Retained WB data must remain a forwarding source after retirement-valid clears. Capture the selected payload on every existing non-held advance without adding valid, reg_write or exception gating. Preserve EX/MEM.alu_result and effective_addr, raw RVFI mem_rdata, trap-adjusted controls, all load widths and signs, x0 handling and youngest-writer priority. Keep mem_to_reg metadata if needed by the existing bundle; removing unrelated controls is outside scope. Update stale comments about the two old MEM/WB fields.\n\nThe expected gain is eight percent with medium confidence, initially an unmeasured estimate. Gowin may merge the moved selector with load extraction and the existing hold/reset logic. The key risk is shifting the timing limit into the MEM/WB input cone or exposing the registered product, ALU or branch comparator path. Require the unchanged bracketed CoreMark cycle count and the normal three-placement vendor median. Acceptance requires fitness greater than 194.15852 iterations/s, approximately 77.46030 MHz at 3,989,539 cycles.\n\nValidate existing pipeline tests in normal and YOSYS-declaration builds, unchanged formal and stalled reference cosimulation, all canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker/bounds checks, and median Gowin timing. Exercise every load width/sign, ALU and M-extension results, JAL/JALR link values, immediate consumers, same-rd producers, x0, misaligned accesses, reset, and multi-cycle dmem holds that clear WB valid while preserving its forwarding value. Check complete RVFI values and contiguous exactly-once retirement. Keep nret=1, decoder legality, real/ALTOPS arithmetic and scheduling, and every test assertion and formal bound unchanged.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Replace only mem_wb_t.alu_result and mem_wb_t.read_data with one 32-bit wb_data field. Preserve EX/MEM fields, control metadata and all RVFI memory fields.'},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Select the final sign/zero-extended load or ALU value before the existing MEM/WB register and capture wb_data on its ordinary advance. Reset clears it; hold_wb retains it and clears only valid. Keep exception, memory and RVFI behavior unchanged and update payload comments.'},\n{'file':'rtl/wb_stage.sv','description':'Drive w_data directly from registered in.wb_data, removing the load/ALU output selector. Preserve write enable/address equations and update interface comments.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain existing tests and add coverage for mixed-width signed/unsigned loads and ALU/JAL/M-extension writeback values feeding immediate consumers, plus retained WB forwarding during prolonged data stalls, same-rd writers, x0 and misalignment. Verify unchanged retirement timing, architectural values and RVFI fields.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=100))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Revised hypothesis is schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
