{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"WB mux retiming reached 77.044 MHz median, about a 4.0% gain—just below acceptance. I’m testing the other end of that same path: removing the bubble-zero mux from the EX result register while keeping every bubble control cleared."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Remove control muxes from the registered WB-to-EX result loop'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 185.62 iterations/s at 74.054 MHz with 3,989,539 bracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh option-0 vendor timing run reproduces the logged WB load-data-to-fetch-PC critical path, with WB-to-EX result paths nearly tied. The r9s0 result-loop optimization was limited by the old radix-8 divider; the champion has since removed that competing limit with radix-32 division and captured multiply operands. A new WB-only probe reaches 77.044 MHz median at unchanged cycles, about four percent gain, but still leaves WB-qualified EX result capture competitive. Optimize both ends of this same register-to-register result path.'''\nh=d['hypothesis']\nh=h.replace('This is one local mux-retiming and redundant-data-bank micro-optimization. It removes the WB output mux from branch recovery, effective-address generation, ALU forwarding and register-file bypass paths while deleting 32 redundant payload flops. It adds no pipeline stage or instruction cycles. Do not combine it with comparator rewrites, EX bubble changes, predictor changes or arithmetic-unit changes.','''At the receiving end, remove the bubble-zero selector from EX/MEM.alu_result only. Keep reset-first and data-memory-hold-second priority. On reset clear the full EX/MEM bundle; on stall retain all of it. In the existing execute_wait-or-invalid bubble arm keep reg_q <= '0, then override that single field with:\n  reg_q.alu_result <= in.ctrl.is_jump ? (in.pc + 32'd4) : alu_result;\nKeep the normal valid capture arm identical. The result payload thus captures on every unstalled, non-reset edge, while all other bubble fields remain zero. Do not use a bubble-dependent clock enable, which would preserve the late control dependency. In particular, every bubble must still clear valid, reg_write, mem_read, mem_write and destination metadata; the unused payload must never become an architectural writer, memory request or retirement.\n\nThis is one local result-data/control partitioning micro-optimization at the two ends of the existing WB-to-EX feedback loop. It removes the WB output selector and EX result bubble-zero selector without changing instruction scheduling. It also removes the redundant 32-bit WB data bank. Do not add comparator, predictor, forwarding-policy or arithmetic-unit changes.''')\nh=h.replace('The expected gain is eight percent with medium confidence, initially an unmeasured estimate.','The expected gain for the combined loop optimization is six percent with medium confidence, initially an unmeasured estimate.')\nh=h.replace('A disposable prototype has passed','The WB-selection-only disposable prototype has passed')\nh += '\\\\n\\\\nThe WB-only probe measured placement options 0/1/2 at 73.181/77.044/77.044 MHz, with 5,874 logic cells and 1,323 FFs for option 0. This standalone result does not clear the 4.6 percent gate and is not evidence of acceptance for the combined proposal. Measure the final two-ended loop implementation and retain one coherent micro_opt focus.'\nd['hypothesis']=h\nd['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']=6\nd['changes'].insert(3,{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''In the existing unstalled execute_wait/invalid bubble arm, preserve full bundle clearing and then override only alu_result with its normal candidate value. This removes bubble selection from the result payload while keeping reset, dmem hold, all controls and all valid instruction captures unchanged. Do not replace the zero mux with a bubble hold enable.'''})\nclass BlockDumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nBlockDumper.add_representer(str,lambda dump,s:dump.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=BlockDumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Combined hypothesis is schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
