{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"agent_message","text":"The combined prototype reached 79.422 MHz median with unchanged CoreMark cycles, projecting 199.07 iterations/s—a 7.25% gain above the champion. I’ll put those results and the passing simulation checks in the final YAML. Full formal checking is still running, so I won’t claim it has passed."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_76", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nfitness=79.422*1e7/3989539\nprint('Fitness:',fitness,'delta_pct:',100*(fitness/185.62-1))\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['hypothesis']='''Optimize the data/control partition at both ends of the existing registered WB-to-EX result loop. Move the load-versus-ALU writeback selection before MEM/WB, and remove bubble-zero selection from the receiving EX/MEM arithmetic payload. This is one local result-loop micro-optimization, adding no instruction stage or cycles.\n\nReplace only mem_wb_t.alu_result and mem_wb_t.read_data with a single 32-bit wb_data. On each ordinary MEM/WB advance capture:\n  reg_q.wb_data <= in.ctrl.mem_to_reg ? load_data : in.alu_result;\nUse the existing byte/halfword sign- or zero-extended load_data, not raw dmem_rdata. In wb_stage drive w_data directly from in.wb_data. Keep w_en=in.ctrl.reg_write&&in.valid and w_addr=in.rd exactly.\n\nReset clears wb_data. A data-memory hold retains wb_data together with destination and control fields while clearing only valid, exactly as today. Retained WB data remains a forwarding source after retirement-valid clears. Capture the selected payload on every existing non-held advance without adding valid, reg_write or exception gating. Preserve EX/MEM.alu_result and effective_addr, raw RVFI memory data, trap-adjusted controls, all load widths/signs, x0 and youngest-writer priority. Leave unrelated bundle controls alone and update obsolete payload comments.\n\nAt the receiving end change only EX/MEM.alu_result's bubble behavior. Keep reset-first and data-memory-hold-second priority. Reset clears the full bundle; a data stall retains all of it. In the existing execute_wait-or-invalid bubble arm keep reg_q <= '0 and then override this single field:\n  reg_q.alu_result <= in.ctrl.is_jump ? (in.pc + 32'd4) : alu_result;\nThe later field assignment must override the bundle clear in the same always_ff process. Keep the normal valid capture arm unchanged. The unused result payload now captures on every unstalled, non-reset edge; all other bubble bits remain zero. Do not replace the zero mux with a bubble-dependent hold enable, which would preserve the late control dependency.\n\nEvery bubble must still clear valid, reg_write, mem_read, mem_write, destination and all other metadata. Forwarding inspects reg_write independently of valid, so clearing only valid is insufficient. The unused payload must never cause a register write, memory request, predictor update or retirement. Preserve reset and stall priorities, M-extension request/completion schedules, RVFI source/result values and once-only retirement. Do not add comparator, predictor, bypass-policy or arithmetic-unit changes. Keep nret=1, top-level IO, decoder legality, real/ALTOPS arithmetic and all verification contracts unchanged.\n\nAdapt the representation-specific complete-bubble-equals-zero assertion in multiply_radix32_forwarding_and_transaction_order to check the exact new bundle value. At each unstalled M-wait edge record the ALU candidate; on the next observation require the entire EX/MEM bundle to equal that candidate in alu_result and zero in every other bit. EX/MEM packs pc then alu_result, so the candidate shift is bundle_width-64. M-wait instructions cannot be jumps. Do not simply ignore the payload or remove the assertion. Keep all architectural, memory, source-value, prediction, launch/transfer timing, retirement and trace checks. This preserves an exact-state check and every architectural bubble guarantee.\n\nThe mapped circuit launches from a final WB-data register without a load/ALU output mux and captures the EX result without bubble-zero selection. The redundant WB payload bank disappears. WB-selection-only testing on this champion reached 77.044 MHz median, about four percent gain, insufficient for acceptance; the final proposal optimizes both endpoints of the same result loop. Risks remain in the MEM/WB input cone, branch recovery, arithmetic-result selection and placement sensitivity.\n\nA disposable prototype of the combined change measured Gowin placement options 0/1/2 at 79.377/79.422/79.422 MHz, median 79.422 MHz. Option 0 used 5,892 logic cells, 1,323 FFs, 49 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. Canonical stalled CoreMark passed the unchanged CRC/UART/bounds/completion/marker validator in exactly 3,989,539 bracketed cycles, matching the champion. This projects 199.075627 iterations/s, a 7.249 percent gain over 185.62. It exceeds the 194.15852 acceptance threshold, which requires about 77.46030 MHz at that cycle count. This is prototype evidence, not final orchestrator acceptance; reproduce the normal median, never just the best placement.\n\nThe combined prototype passed lint, all 34 pipeline tests in both normal and YOSYS-declaration builds with the exact bubble-payload expectation above, and full-reference cosimulation of selftest plus three random programs both with and without bus stalls. The full unchanged ALTOPS formal suite was launched but had not completed when this evidence was recorded; no full formal pass is claimed. Final implementation must pass every unchanged gate, including register consistency, PC continuity, liveness and unique retirement. Do not alter formal depths or contract files. Add directed mixed-width loads, ALU/M-extension/link values and immediate consumers, same-rd writers, x0, misalignment, reset and prolonged dmem holds that retain WB forwarding after valid clears. Confirm unchanged instruction timing and complete RVFI values. Prototype RTL and tests were restored after measurement; this YAML is the proposal artifact.'''\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nD.add_representer(str,lambda dump,s:dump.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Schema valid:',p)\nPY\n git diff --exit-code\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
