{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*.rpt' -g '*.json' -g '*sta*' -g '*timing*' -g '*notes*' cores/bench fpga | head -80; sed -n '1,240p' tools/eval/gowin.py; sed -n '1,180p' Makefile\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\nfpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\n\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\n\nV2 times designs with Gowin EDA (the FPGA vendor's own synthesis, place and\nroute and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\nmodel for this part misses whole classes of paths. The vendor flow is also\ndeterministic and insensitive to circuit-neutral netlist changes.\n\nFmax is the median over Gowin's placement algorithms (PLACE_OPTIONS), each\na full build of the same RTL; results are deterministic for a given input.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport statistics\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import remove_path\n\nGOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\nGOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\nPART = \"GW2AR-LV18QN88C8/I7\"      # Tang Nano 20K\nDEVICE_VERSION = \"C\"\nPLACE_OPTIONS = (0, 1, 2)\nCST = \"fpga/constraints/Tang_Nano_20K.cst\"\nSDC = \"fpga/constraints/clock.sdc\"\nSTALL_GEN = \"fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\"\nBUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC = 2700\n\n\ndef gowin_env(base: dict | None, workdir: Path) -> dict:\n    env = dict(os.environ if base is None else base)\n    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n    env[\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"] = \":\".join(map(str, libs))\n    env[\"QT_QPA_PLATFORM\"] = \"offscreen\"\n    xdg = workdir / \".xdg\"\n    xdg.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    os.chmod(xdg, 0o700)\n    env[\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\"] = str(xdg)\n    return env\n\n\ndef rtl_sources(rtl_dir: Path) -> list[Path]:\n    srcs = sorted(rtl_dir.glob(\"*.sv\"))\n    pkg = rtl_dir / \"core_pkg.sv\"\n    return ([pkg] if pkg in srcs else []) + [p for p in srcs if p != pkg]\n\n\ndef project_tcl(worktree: Path, rtl_dir: Path, bench_sv: str, place_option: int) -> str:\n    files = [*rtl_sources(rtl_dir), worktree / STALL_GEN, worktree / bench_sv,\n   \n…[14823 of 17895 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:285e92be638d5a6b]…\ns $(N),--iterations 1,$(ORCH_FLAGS)) $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\n\nloop:\nifneq ($(strip $(WORKTREE)),)\n\t@if [ ! -d \"$(WT_PATH)\" ]; then \\\n\t  echo \"[wt] creating branch $(WT_BRANCH) and worktree $(WT_PATH)\"; \\\n\t  if git rev-parse --verify $(WT_BRANCH) >/dev/null 2>&1; then \\\n\t    git worktree add \"$(WT_PATH)\" $(WT_BRANCH); \\\n\t  else \\\n\t    git worktree add -b $(WT_BRANCH) \"$(WT_PATH)\"; \\\n\t  fi; \\\n\t  [ -e \"$(WT_PATH)/formal/riscv-formal\" ] || ln -s \"$(CURDIR)/formal/riscv-formal\" \"$(WT_PATH)/formal/riscv-formal\"; \\\n\tfi\n\t@$(MAKE) -C \"$(WT_PATH)\" loop \\\n\t  WORKTREE= \\\n\t  TARGET=$(TARGET) N=$(N) K=$(K) AGENT=$(AGENT) \\\n\t  $(if $(strip $(BASE)),BASE=$(BASE),) \\\n\t  $(if $(strip $(COREMARK)),COREMARK=$(COREMARK),) \\\n\t  $(if $(strip $(LUT)),LUT=$(LUT),)\nelse\n\tAGENT_PROVIDER=$(AGENT) python3 -m tools.orchestrator $(ORCH_FLAGS) $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\nendif\n\nreport:\n\tpython3 -m tools.orchestrator --report $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\n\nclean:\n\trm -rf test/cosim/sim_build sim_build out\n\trm -rf experiments/worktrees\n\trm -f bench/programs/*.elf\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt' or d.get('id') in ['hyp-20261002-001-r11s0','hyp-20261002-001-r8s0','hyp-20261002-002-r8s1']:\n  print(d['id'],d.get('category'),d.get('title'))\n  print('RESULT',d.get('fitness'),d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('critical_path'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict):\n   print(h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  print('NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt' or d.get('id') in ['hyp-20261002-001-r11s0','hyp-20261002-001-r8s0','hyp-20261002-002-r8s1']:\n  print(d['id'],d.get('category'),d.get('title'))\n  print('RESULT',d.get('fitness'),d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('critical_path'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict):\n   print(h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  print('NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-060f5a0 micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench\nRESULT 12.12 5.442 {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n\nNOTES \nhyp-20261001-001-r1s0 micro_opt Shared radix-4 combinational DIV/REM datapath\nRESULT 12.8 5.749 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -179.278, 'arrival_ns': 189.573, 'logic_cells': 229, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nReplace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic inside alu.sv with one\nshared, fully combinational unsigned radix-4 restoring divmod network,\nsurrounded by RV32M signed-magnitude conversion and result correction.\nThis is a local arithmetic implementation change: keep the ALU ports,\nzero-cycle combinational latency, pipeline, forwarding, bus stalls,\nretirement width, and all non-division operations unchanged.\n\nConsume the dividend from most significant to least significant in\nsixteen two-bit digits. Precompute unsigned D, 2D, and 3D at 34 bits\nwithout truncating their high bits. At each stage form T = (R << 2)\n| next_digit, and compute T-D, T-2D, and T-3D in parallel. Select the\nlargest digit whose subtraction has no borrow, or digit zero with\nremainder T. Use subtraction carry/borrow to select the digit rather\nthan a separate magnitude comparison followed by subtraction. Emit\nboth the quotient digits and the final remainder from this one network;\ndo not implement remainder with a second divider or a quotient multiply.\n\nMake the sixteen stages explicit with compile-time bounds so synthesis\nsees their widths. After consuming k digits, the remainder is bounded\nby the consumed 2k-bit dividend prefix. Stage k therefore needs a\n2k-bit trial value and a 2k+1-bit unsigned subtraction. A candidate\nmultiple of D is eligible only if all its bits above that 2k-bit width\nare zero AND its subtraction has no borrow. This hi\n…[57336 of 60408 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e4f63f2c6da4c8b3]…\n stalls, and the canonical CoreMark run. A Yosys\nSAT miter proved the actual replacement branch_cond equal to the\noriginal for every pair of 32-bit operands and every three-bit branch\noperation, including both default-false encodings. This is exhaustive\ncombinational equivalence, not a claim of completing riscv-formal's\nfull sequential gate. The implementer must still pass every unchanged\nformal and cosimulation gate and reproduce the scored vendor median.\n\nCompeting EX result and recovery-control paths limit the measured gain.\nLarger comparison slices, altered signed/polarity factoring, explicit\nBoolean leaves and moving selection after speculative comparisons did\nnot improve on this tree. Registering complete forwarding selectors\nalso failed to improve it. Do not bundle those alternatives into this\nproposal. Keep this single branch-comparator change and report its\nactual acceptance outcome honestly; no above-threshold gain is claimed.\nAll temporary working RTL edits were restored after measurement.\n\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
