, direct-target arithmetic and PC+4. The selector has\nNORMAL, FALLTHROUGH, DIRECT and INDIRECT states. Reset selects NORMAL\nand resets its PC to RESET_PC. An accepted EX redirect captures the\nappropriate recovery kind at the same edge that the independent banks\ncapture its candidate addresses. Redirect has priority over fetch_accept.\nThe corrected fetch address is visible immediately after this edge,\nexactly as today: add no recovery bubble, pipeline stage or bus cycle.\n\nCapture all\n…[5236 of 8308 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:19e41605085cc513]…\nion\nprobes measured 63.925 and 69.177 MHz and exposed wide squash fanout.\nThe combined narrow-squash version with enabled candidate banks measured\n74.771 MHz, with a worst WB/EX path to the fallthrough candidate register:\nthe shared capture enable still depended on redirect. Narrow squash alone\nmeasured median 75.798 MHz and unchanged CoreMark cycles. Neither clears\nacceptance. The final proposal specifically removes all three candidate\nenables using unconditional sampling and one-cycle source selection;\nit is not a resubmission of those measured below-threshold variants.\nFinal timing and full unchanged formal gates must establish its result.\n\nhyp-20261002-001-r12s0 micro_opt Balance the EX branch comparator into a LUT-sized reduction tree regression 82.257\nhyp-20261002-002-r12s1 structural Fuse load-to-branch execution through a registered comparison stage regression 71.484\nhyp-20261002-003-r12s2 predictor Isolate predictor verification from arithmetic readiness and late polarity selection regression 79.243\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
