{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'hyp-20261002-00[123]-r(8s0|11s2|12s[02]|13s[012])' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "23:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Prequalify writers and flatten one-hot EX operand selection\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Recent vendor paths cross forwarding tag comparison, EX operand muxes\\nand the multiplier. The current EX datapath encodes forwarding choices,\\ndecodes them into a three-way data mux, then selects PC or immediate\\nthrough another mux before arithmetic. Prior load-to-branch forwarding\\nregressed timing, and pipelined multiplication added 4.46 percent more\\nCoreMark cycles. Shortening existing operand steering offers a local\\ntiming improvement without new bypass paths or execution cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Recent vendor paths cross forwarding tag comparison, EX operand muxes\\nand the multiplier. The current EX datapath encodes forwarding choices,\\ndecodes them into a three-way data mux, then selects PC or immediate\\nthrough another mux before arithmetic. Prior load-to-branch forwarding\\nregressed timing, and pipelined multiplication added 4.46 percent more\\nCoreMark cycles. Shortening existing operand steering offers a local\\ntiming improvement without new bypass paths or execution cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the internal two-bit forwarding encoding with three mutually\\nexclusive source enables, then directly select ALU operands from the\\nfour possible sources. This is one EX operand-selection micro-optimization.\\nPreserve the pipeline, divider, multiplier arithmetic, fetch queue,\\npredictor, instruction latency and every architectural interface.\\n\\nPrecompute each writer's eligibility at its existing pipeline boundary.\\nAdd forward_eligible to ex_mem_t and mem_wb_t. In EX capture\\nctrl_with_trap.reg_write && (in.rd!=0) with EX/MEM;