{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nrows=[json.loads(x) for x in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor ident in ['hyp-20261001-002-r4s1','hyp-20261002-003-r11s2','hyp-20261002-002-r13s1']:\n x=next(x for x in rows if x['id']==ident)\n h=x['hypothesis']\n print('\\\\nDETAIL',ident)\n print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n print('NOTES',x.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nDETAIL hyp-20261001-002-r4s1\nRestructure the existing IF-to-ID/EX boundary into an independently\nmoving data payload and a small bubble-control path, without adding a\npipeline stage or changing instruction latencies. Drive IF's instruction\nfield directly from imem_data, even on redirects and unavailable-fetch\ncycles. Continue driving the current PC. Keep redirect priority over PC\nstalls and use the existing fetch-valid indication to mark discarded\ninstructions. The raw instruction, decoder, immediate generator, source\naddresses, and register-file read muxes must have no combinational\ndependence on redirect, flush, or fetch-valid.\n\nSplit ID/EX updates by purpose. Reset still initializes the full bundle.\nOn every non-stalled edge, capture PC, instruction, immediate, register\nindices, and register-file operand values independently of flush and\nincoming valid. On flush clear only the registered ctrl bundle and valid,\nwith the same flush-over-stall priority as today. Otherwise, when ID is\nallowed to advance, set valid from incoming valid and set ctrl to the\ndecoded control only for a valid input, or to all zeros for a bubble.\nA held instruction retains all its fields. Thus payload bits in a bubble\nare defined but irrelevant, and a killed instruction cannot assert a\nmemory, register-write, branch, jump, or divide control. Do not implement\nthis by masking the raw instruction or source addresses earlier in the\ncone, or by zeroing the wide payload on a flush.\n\nDerive load-use dependencies from the raw fetch source fields and the\nregistered ID/EX load destination. Qualify them with imem_ready, which\nis the bus availability indication, rather than the redirect-dependent\nIF valid signal. Retain the current conservative comparison of both\ninstruction source bitfields; semantic source-use optimization is outside\nthis hypothesis. A redirect still flushes the younger instruction and\noverrides fetch hold. Preserve dmem-stall and execute-wait precedence:\nthey hold ID/EX, dmem stalls preserve EX/MEM requests, and a load-use\nbubble\n…[15548 of 18620 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:97ec73ff8d422a02]…\n. The final narrow-slice/shared-prefix execution fabric has not been implemented or timed. Its prediction must be verified rather than inferred from those probes.\n\nValidate all route transitions and candidate pairs, carry/borrow crossing every nibble boundary, all-zero/all-one operands, signed extrema, opposite signs, equality and differing low nibbles. Compare randomized ADD/SUB/SLT/SLTU results and every branch predicate to independent 32-bit reference arithmetic, including PC/immediate routes. Preserve existing assertions while adapting internal selector encodings with exact one-hot/value checks. Test competing writers, x0, trapped JAL/JALR and loads, retained WB data, load-use bubbles, all holds/flush/reset transitions and M waits with draining producers. Run unchanged formal including liveness/reg/unique/pc_fwd, real and ALTOPS unit tests, stalled reference cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. Require unchanged bracketed cycles and median vendor timing for final evaluation.\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
