{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_22", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(x) for x in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nx=next(x for x in rows if x['id']=='hyp-20261002-001-r12s0')\nprint(x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Replace only the EX conditional-branch comparison network with shared\nequality and unsigned-less-than predicates built as a balanced tree.\nPreserve the original forwarded rs1 and rs2, instruction schedule,\nprediction, target calculation, recovery edge and training event.\nThis is a branch-comparator micro-optimization, not a prediction change.\n\nDivide the 32-bit operands into sixteen two-bit slices. At each leaf\ncompute eq=(a_slice==b_slice) and lt=(a_slice<b_slice), both functions\nof four input bits with bounded local comparison depth. Retain the\nnative two-bit relational expression rather than expanding it into\nBoolean terms; that version gave the strongest measured mapping.\nCombine adjacent\ngroups from most significant to least significant with\neq_parent=eq_hi && eq_lo and\nlt_parent=lt_hi || (eq_hi && lt_lo).\nUse four explicitly balanced reduction levels, never a linear priority\nloop or a full-width subtraction. The root yields exact 32-bit equality\nand unsigned less-than. For signed less-than use\n(rs1[31]^rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : unsigned_lt.\nDecode the six existing BR_* cases from these shared predicates:\nBEQ=eq, BNE=!eq, BLT=signed_lt, BGE=!signed_lt,\nBLTU=unsigned_lt, BGEU=!unsigned_lt. Preserve the default-false case.\nDo not alter the general ALU comparisons or introduce new pipeline state.\n\nThe intended gain comes from replacing a long operand-dependent\nmagnitude-comparison chain with shallow LUT logic before the existing\nredirect controls. Keep every original branch_taken, actual_taken,\nmisalignment, redirect, redirect_target and train_valid equation and\nevery pipeline-register update intact. The direct and JALR address\nadders, branch predictor, queue, forwarding selection, load-use stalls,\nmultiplier and divider remain unchanged. This gives a precise\ncycle-for-cycle equivalence target, including arbitrary invalid bubbles.\n\nPreserve nret=1 and all top-level ports, decoder default-illegal\ndiscipline, misaligned-target traps, wrong-path suppression, bus holds,\nRVFI source values, PC continuity and contiguous r\n…[1401 of 4473 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8b5f0b59f06ee280]…\nout bus stalls, and the canonical CoreMark run. A Yosys\nSAT miter proved the actual replacement branch_cond equal to the\noriginal for every pair of 32-bit operands and every three-bit branch\noperation, including both default-false encodings. This is exhaustive\ncombinational equivalence, not a claim of completing riscv-formal's\nfull sequential gate. The implementer must still pass every unchanged\nformal and cosimulation gate and reproduce the scored vendor median.\n\nCompeting EX result and recovery-control paths limit the measured gain.\nLarger comparison slices, altered signed/polarity factoring, explicit\nBoolean leaves and moving selection after speculative comparisons did\nnot improve on this tree. Registering complete forwarding selectors\nalso failed to improve it. Do not bundle those alternatives into this\nproposal. Keep this single branch-comparator change and report its\nactual acceptance outcome honestly; no above-threshold gain is claimed.\nAll temporary working RTL edits were restored after measurement.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
