{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nroot=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/9e6b10b9/70e838ae/r14_micro')\nd=root/'branch_seed/rtl';shutil.copytree('cores/bench/rtl',d,dirs_exist_ok=True)\np=d/'ex_stage.sv';s=p.read_text();start=s.index('  // Native two-bit leaves');end=s.index('    branch_taken  =',start)\ns=s[:start]+'''  logic [31:0] cmp_a, cmp_b;\n  logic ordered;\n  assign cmp_a = {rs1[31] \"'^ in.branch_signed, rs1[30:0]};\n  assign cmp_b = {rs2[31] ''^ in.branch_signed, rs2[30:0]};\n  assign ordered = in.branch_signed || in.branch_unsigned;\n  logic [31:1] branch_eq_tree, branch_result_tree;\n  for (genvar k=0;k<16;k++) begin : branch_compare_leaves\n    assign branch_eq_tree[16+k] = (cmp_a[2*k+:2] == cmp_b[2*k+:2]);\n    if (k==0) begin : seed\n      assign branch_result_tree[16+k] =\n        (ordered && (cmp_a[2*k+:2] < cmp_b[2*k+:2])) ||\n        (in.branch_eq && branch_eq_tree[16+k]);\n    end else begin : order\n      assign branch_result_tree[16+k] = ordered && (cmp_a[2*k+:2] < cmp_b[2*k+:2]);\n    end\n  end\n  for (genvar k=1;k<16;k++) begin : branch_compare_groups\n    assign branch_eq_tree[k] = branch_eq_tree[2*k+1] && branch_eq_tree[2*k];\n    assign branch_result_tree[k] = branch_result_tree[2*k+1] ||\n                                 (branch_eq_tree[2*k+1] && branch_result_tree[2*k]);\n  end\n  always_comb begin\n    branch_cond = branch_result_tree[1] ''^ in.branch_invert;\n'\"'''+s[end:];p.write_text(s)\nshutil.copytree('cores/bench/test',root/'branch_seed/test',dirs_exist_ok=True)\nPY\npython3 -u - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build\nr=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/9e6b10b9/70e838ae/r14_micro/branch_seed')\nx=build(Path.cwd(),r/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',1,r/'gowin_p1')\n(r/'timing_p1.json').write_text(json.dumps(x,indent=2));print(json.dumps(x))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\"place_option\": 1, \"placement_failed\": false, \"fmax_mhz\": 84.473, \"levels\": 11, \"logic\": 5781, \"regs\": 1256, \"lutram\": 49, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_paths\": [{\"from\": \"cpu/u_fwd/rs1_ex_match_q_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/entries[0].instr_entries[0].instr_0_11_s\", \"slack_ns\": -6.838, \"arrival_ns\": 17.133, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/divisor_q_14_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_11_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.836, \"arrival_ns\": 17.13, \"logic_cells\": 27, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_fwd/rs1_ex_match_q_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/entries[0].instr_entries[0].instr_0_1_s\", \"slack_ns\": -6.831, \"arrival_ns\": 17.126, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.reg_write_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_26_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.829, \"arrival_ns\": 17.123, \"logic_cells\": 13, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_31_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_2_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.825, \"arrival_ns\": 17.119, \"logic_cells\": 12, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_45", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r14s0',\n'title':'Seed branch comparison with its predicate before balanced reduction',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 211.52 iterations/s at 84.388 MHz with 3,989,539 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path carries forwarded WB data through EX branch recovery into IF. The accepted r13s0 comparator already has native two-bit leaves and balanced reduction, but still selects signed versus unsigned ordering, selects equality versus ordering, and applies polarity after wide comparison. Move those predicate choices to the leaves of the existing comparator, without replicating the comparator or changing prediction.\n\nPrior larger comparison slices, registered forwarding routes and replicated arithmetic have not consistently improved vendor timing. Local probes against this champion also failed to improve it: removing queue recovery gating reached 82.310 MHz in placement option 1, narrowing ID squash reached 81.242 MHz, and predecoded ALU result selection reached 84.008 MHz. These are rejected probes and are not proposed changes.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the conditional-branch comparator in ex_stage.sv with a predicate-seeded balanced reduction. Preserve the existing four captured branch flags, all forwarding, original branch/redirect/training equations and every pipeline edge. This is a local Boolean topology optimization, with no prediction-policy or instruction-schedule change.\n\nUse the original forwarded rs1 and rs2. Form cmp_a={rs1[31] XOR in.branch_signed,rs1[30:0]} and cmp_b analogously. Flipping both sign bits converts signed ordering to unsigned ordering; equality is unchanged. Let ordered=in.branch_signed OR in.branch_unsigned. Keep sixteen native two-bit comparisons and the same four balanced high/low reduction levels.\n\nFor each leaf k covering bits [2*k +: 2], compute p[k]=(cmp_a_slice==cmp_b_slice). For k>0 compute g[k]=ordered AND (cmp_a_slice<cmp_b_slice). For the least-significant leaf k=0, compute g[0]=(ordered AND (cmp_a_slice<cmp_b_slice)) OR (in.branch_eq AND p[0]). Thus an equality branch seeds the tree with equality at its low end while suppressing every ordering term. An ordering branch seeds it with ordinary unsigned less-than on sign-conditioned words. Combine a more-significant group H with a less-significant group L using P=P_H AND P_L and G=G_H OR (P_H AND G_L). Use an explicit balanced tree, e.g. leaves 16+k and parents 1..15 with child 2*k+1 more significant than child 2*k.\n\nThe root G is already the selected positive predicate: equality for BEQ/BNE, signed less-than for BLT/BGE, and unsigned less-than for BLTU/BGEU. Set branch_cond=root_G XOR in.branch_invert. All-zero predicate flags yield zero, preserving reserved/default behavior; the six legal modes retain their exact comparisons. Remove the old root signed-result mux and three-way predicate selection. Do not change branch predecode, target/address adders, misalignment handling, actual_taken, ex_accept (including \"'!execute_wait), redirect, redirect_target, training, link values or architectural pc_next. All unused bubble controls and all register-update priorities remain unchanged.\n\nThis moves instruction-mode logic ahead of the reduction instead of behind its latest operand-dependent result. Only the top two-bit leaf needs sign conditioning, while equality needs no separate wide late selection. Native two-bit relational expressions should remain native; do not expand them into long bitwise priority chains or replace the tree with subtraction. Keep the original ALU, multiplier, divider, predictor counters and fetch queue. No new pipeline registers or execution/recovery cycles are required.\n\nExpect about six percent higher fitness if removing the late predicate selection shortens the limiting recovery path enough. This is a low-confidence estimate until all Gowin placement options are measured; forwarding, ALU and divider paths are competing limits, and mode gating at every leaf can add fanout. At unchanged cycles, acceptance requires more than 221.24992 iterations/s, or approximately 88.26852 MHz median. Do not claim acceptance from a single placement or from circuit-equivalent synthesis changes.\n\nProve the actual new combinational expressions equivalent to the original branch case for all 32-bit operand pairs and all eight branch-op encodings. Test equality, signed extremes, opposite signs, adjacent values, and each possible highest-differing two-bit leaf, including the special least-significant seed and sign-conditioned most-significant leaf. Preserve all existing tests and add directed seed cases for all six predicates. Exercise every forwarding-source combination, youngest-writer priority, x0, retained WB operands, load-dependent branches, both prediction errors, target faults, queue-full recovery, blocking M operations and prolonged independent bus stalls. Require identical live retirement, training and recovery cycles and precise RVFI operands, PC, trap and order.\n\nKeep nret=1 and every top-level port, full 32-bit addresses, default-illegal decoding, all memory side effects and handshakes, real and ALTOPS arithmetic, reset/stall priorities and formal bounds. Run unchanged sequential formal including liveness/reg/pc_fwd/unique, both pipeline-test variants, stalled reference cosimulation, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation and all three scored Gowin placement options. No contract or evaluation files change.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace the post-forwarding comparator with the sign-conditioned, predicate-seeded sixteen-leaf balanced P/G tree. Fold equality into the least-significant leaf, gate ordering at the leaves, and XOR only the root with captured branch_invert. Preserve all other EX data, controls, handshakes, traps, recovery, training and register updates.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all current assertions and extend branch tests for the equality seed, sign-conditioned top leaf, every two-bit difference position and all six predicates. Cover every forwarding source, competing writers, retained WB, stalls, reset, M waits and recovery/fault cases with exact original cycle and RVFI checks.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=88))\nprint('Replaced rejected draft with focused branch-predicate hypothesis')\nr=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/9e6b10b9/70e838ae/r14_micro/branch_seed')\ns=(r/'rtl/ex_stage.sv').read_text();s=s[s.index('  logic [31:0] cmp_a'):s.index('  always_comb begin\\\\n    branch_cond')]\ns=s.replace('in.branch_signed','branch_signed').replace('in.branch_unsigned','branch_unsigned').replace('in.branch_eq','branch_eq')\nm='''module miter(input [31:0] rs1,rs2,input [2:0] op,output ok);\nwire branch_eq=(op==0||op==1);\nwire branch_signed=(op==4||op==5);\nwire branch_unsigned=(op==6||op==7);\nwire branch_invert=(op==1||op==5||op==7);\n'''+s+'''wire got=branch_result_tree[1]\"'^branch_invert;\nreg expected;\nalways @* case(op)\n0:expected=(rs1==rs2);1:expected=(rs1!=rs2);\n4:expected=($signed(rs1)<$signed(rs2));5:expected=($signed(rs1)>=$signed(rs2));\n6:expected=(rs1<rs2);7:expected=(rs1>=rs2);default:expected=0;\nendcase\nassign ok=(got==expected);\nendmodule\n'\"'''\n(r/'miter.sv').write_text(m)\nPY\nyosys -Q -T -p 'read_verilog -sv /srv/hwebench/tmp/9e6b10b9/70e838ae/r14_micro/branch_seed/miter.sv; prep -top miter -flatten; sat -prove ok 1 -verify' > /srv/hwebench/tmp/9e6b10b9/70e838ae/r14_micro/branch_seed/miter.log 2>&1\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
