{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_59", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0.yaml')\nprint(p.resolve())\nprint(p.read_text())\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0.yaml\nid: hyp-20261002-001-r15s0\ntitle: \"Shorten ALU shifts with parallel coarse selection and fine shifting\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 211.52 iterations/s at 84.388 MHz and 3,989,539\n  bracketed CoreMark cycles. Recent branch-only changes expose a competing\n  forwarding-to-ALU-result path: r14s0 ends at EX/MEM.alu_result through\n  u_alu, and achieves only 0.10 percent. Earlier operand-candidate replication\n  and banked result forwarding regress badly. The three native variable\n  shifts in the base ALU are a localized opportunity to reduce mux depth and\n  routing without changing execution latency or the established bypass loop.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the combinational SLL/SRL/SRA implementation with a factored\n  coarse/fine barrel shifter. Keep left and right data paths separate to\n  avoid introducing direction-dependent bit reversal before or after the\n  shifter. Decode b[4:3] into four mutually exclusive coarse enables.\n  For each direction, form four constant-wired candidates shifted by\n  0,8,16,24 positions, mask them with the coarse enables, and combine\n  them with an explicitly balanced OR tree. Then shift this intermediate\n  by b[2:0] using ordinary conditional shifts by one, two and four bits,\n  in that order. This replaces serial coarse data selection with a\n  parallel decode/mask/reduction network and keeps fine shifting local.\n\n  Share the right-shift network between SRL and SRA with fill equal to\n  (op == ALU_SRA) AND a[31]. Use that same fill for every coarse candidate\n  and all three fine stages; logical right and left shifts fill with zero.\n  Keep full 32-bit values, use only b[4:0], and handle shamt=0 exactly.\n  Keep the current ALU result case and operation encodings, forwarded\n  operands, address/branch adders, comparator, multiplier, divider,\n  request/completion schedules, predictor and pipeline register\n…[2177 of 5249 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c157f7ca8d5c214a]…\nThe four-way coarse implementation is the strongest single local change\n  measured so far. A 32-way shifter, fully masked fine selection, shared\n  bit-reversal shifter, balanced ALU comparison and forwarding-retiming\n  probes were slower and are not part of this proposal.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 1\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement separate left and shared logical/arithmetic-right four-way\n      coarse masked candidate networks with balanced OR reduction, followed\n      by three fine shift stages. Replace only the three shift result arms.\n      Preserve every other ALU operation, interface and sequential state.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing assertions and extend SLL/SRL/SRA coverage across\n      all shift amounts, ignored upper shift-operand bits, sign extremes,\n      walking bits and random values. Check immediate operation changes\n      and unchanged combinational behavior in both real and ALTOPS builds.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
