{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_51", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261001-002-r5s1':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n  print('Metrics:',d['fmax_mhz'],d['cycles'],d['critical_path'])\nPY\ncat cores/bench/experiments/.r9s0-formal.log\nrg -c 'DONE \\\\(PASS|DONE \\\\(FAIL|DONE \\\\(ERROR' formal/last_run-*.log\"", "aggregated_output": "Implement MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU with one shared clocked\nmultiplier inside alu.sv. Put an operand register before the product\nand a 32-bit architectural-result register after it, integrated with\nEX's existing blocking execution protocol. Keep all base operations\nsingle-cycle, preserve the current radix-4 divider schedule, and\nretain the existing predictor and pipeline topology. This is one\nstructural change to the multiply execution boundary.\n\nUse IDLE, COMPUTE, and DONE states. req_ready is true only in IDLE.\nOn accepted request edge 1, capture the operation and two signed\n33-bit operands from the exact forwarded input values. A's extra bit\nis a[31] for MULH or MULHSU and zero otherwise. B's extra bit is b[31]\nfor MULH and zero otherwise. Thus MUL/MULHU use unsigned magnitudes,\nMULH uses two signed values, and MULHSU uses signed A and unsigned B.\nCompute one signed 33-by-33 product with an explicit 66-bit result;\ndo not truncate operands or multiply at 32-bit expression width.\n\nOn edge 2, register product[31:0] for the captured MUL operation or\nproduct[63:32] for the other three operations, and enter DONE. Bits\n65:64 are not architectural result bits. Assert result_valid in DONE,\nwith the registered result held until result_ready accepts it.\nEarliest EX/MEM result transfer is edge 3. The state then returns to\nIDLE; a subsequent multiply launches as a new transaction. Forwarded\nlive operands must end at the input registers, and the old three\ncombinational multiply expressions must disappear. Ordinary ALU\noutput selection sees only the registered multiply result. Reset\nclears state and registers and cancels any pending transaction.\n\nAdd a separate multiply request/completion interface alongside the\nexisting divider interface. In EX, recognize only the four multiply\nALU operations. Launch when in.valid && is_multiply && !stall &&\nmul_req_ready. Assert multiply result_ready only for the held valid\nmultiply when !stall. Extend execute_wait to cover a valid multiply\nwithout a valid result, OR the existing divide\n…[2391 of 5463 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:35c27f5757805dd4]…\nreliminary prototype results, not a completed\norchestrator acceptance or a substitute for formal verification.\n\nImplement the same register boundaries and validate real arithmetic,\nheld completion, reset cancellation, and the matching ALTOPS schedule.\nRun all unchanged formal and stalled cosimulation gates plus canonical\nCoreMark and all Gowin placement options. Acceptance requires fitness\nabove 118.7733 iterations/s; at the prototype's measured cycle count\nthis requires median Fmax above 52.1311 MHz. The next divider-limited\npath, changed placement, and dynamic multiply frequency are remaining\nrisks. The expected net improvement is 13 percent with medium\nconfidence, grounded in the prototype rather than an assumed IPC.\n\nMetrics: 56.523 4389122 {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/quotient_q_31_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_1_s0', 'slack_ns': -13.401, 'arrival_ns': 23.695, 'logic_cells': 98, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider']}\n{\n  \"passed\": true,\n  \"checks_passed\": 53\n}\n53\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
