xact RV32M integer\n  references, including signed-by-unsigned asymmetry. Exercise forwarded\n  operands and dependent consumers with instruction/data stalls. Run\n  unchanged real/ALTOPS ALU tests, pipeline tests, formal and reference\n  cosimulation, plus canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks.\n  Measure all normal Gowin placement options and actual bracketed cycles.\n  Acceptance requires fitness above 160.7702 iterations/s, or median\n  Fmax above 63.9435 MHz if cycles remain 3,977,318. The expected gain is\n  a prediction until this prototype'\"'s median timing is available.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace mul_ss, mul_uu and mul_su with explicitly signed 33-bit\n      operands and one 66-bit combinational product. Select extension\n      signs by multiply opcode, return bits 31:0 or 63:32, and remove\n      duplicate multiply expressions. Preserve ports, timing, division,\n      all base operations and every ALTOPS formula.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve existing vectors and latency assertions. Extend real\n      arithmetic coverage by cycling all four multiply opcodes on each\n      extreme or deterministic random operand pair, including unequal\n      signed/unsigned operands, then changing inputs without a clock\n      edge. Check exact low/high products and retain the existing ALTOPS\n      reference behavior.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing coverage and add mixed MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU\n      sequences using both forwarding sources, same-rd writers and\n      immediate consumers under imem/dmem holds. Check architectural\n      source/result values, unchanged execute timing and once-only\n      ordered retirement.\n''')\nprint('Revised hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Revised hypothesis: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r9s0.yaml\n", "exit_c