ormal and stalled reference cosimulation,\n  plus canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/completion/marker checks.\n  Specifically exercise bubbles during load-use interlocks and divide\n  waits, invalid or wrong-path arithmetic, older memory operations held\n  by dmemReady, and a younger consumer using retained MEM/WB data. Assert\n  that invalid results never forward, write registers or memory, train\n  prediction or retire. Verify all real instruction result and source\n  fields, once-only retirement and unchanged execution timing.\n  Measure all three vendor placement options and actual bracketed cycles.\n  Acceptance requires fitness above 160.7702 iterations/s, approximately\n  63.9435 MHz if cycles remain 3,977,318. The gain below is a prediction\n  pending this prototype's vendor timing.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      In the execute_wait/invalid bubble arm, retain the whole-bundle\n      clear and override only reg_q.alu_result with the normal ALU/link\n      candidate. Keep reset clearing, data-stall retention, every bubble\n      control and all valid-instruction captures unchanged. Ensure the\n      synthesized result register captures on every nonreset unstalled\n      edge without an execute_wait/in.valid data mux.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve existing tests and exercise load-use and divide bubbles\n      with changing arithmetic candidates, wrong-path instructions,\n      same-rd writers and long dmem holds. Check architectural/RVFI\n      results, no side effects from invalid EX/MEM entries, retained WB\n      forwarding, contiguous retirement order and unchanged latency.\n''')\nprint('Revised hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Revised hypothesis: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r9s0.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
