{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_80", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r9s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Remove avoidable control muxes from the registered WB-to-EX result loop'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 153.70 iterations/s at 61.131 MHz and 3,977,318\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst path starts at MEM/WB.mem_to_reg\nand ends at EX/MEM.alu_result through WB selection, forwarding and\narithmetic. The loop contains a load/ALU selector after the launch\nregister and an invalid-bubble zero selector before the destination\nregister. Neither selector needs to occupy that timed arithmetic path.\nRegistered forwarding address matches are already present. Prior\none-hot operand selection alone regressed; this proposal moves or\nremoves result-data selection at existing register boundaries.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Optimize this single registered result loop at both ends without\nchanging pipeline topology or instruction latency. First select the\nfinal architectural WB value before the existing MEM/WB register.\nReplace only mem_wb_t.alu_result and mem_wb_t.read_data with one 32-bit\nwb_data field. In mem_stage's ordinary advancing arm capture\n  reg_q.wb_data <= in.ctrl.mem_to_reg ? load_data : in.alu_result;\nusing the existing aligned, sign/zero-extended load_data. In wb_stage\ndrive w_data directly from in.wb_data, retaining w_en and w_addr exactly.\nThe existing core wiring then forwards registered final data without\na WB load/ALU mux. Preserve EX/MEM.alu_result and effective_addr, and\nall raw RVFI memory fields; raw mem_rdata is not the extended load value.\nReset clears wb_data. hold_wb retains it with destination and controls\nwhile clearing only valid, preserving post-retirement WB forwarding.\nDo not introduce valid or reg_write gating on this payload capture.\n\nSecond remove the bubble-zero selector at the arithmetic-result\nregister's input. Change only EX/MEM.alu_result's behavior on the\nexisting execute_wait or \"'!in.valid bubble arm in ex_stage. Retain\nreset-first and data-memory-stall-second priority. On reset clear the\nentire bundle; on stall retain it completely. On an unstalled bubble\ncontinue clearing the entire bundle, but override alu_result with the\nsame candidate captured for a real instruction:\n  in.ctrl.is_jump ? (in.pc + 32'\"'d4) : alu_result.\nExpress this as reg_q <= '0 followed by reg_q.alu_result <= candidate\nin the same bubble arm and the same existing always_ff process. The\nlater field assignment overrides the bundle zero. Keep the normal\nvalid-instruction arm unchanged. Equivalently, the result register\nclears on reset, holds on stall and otherwise captures regardless of\nin.valid or execute_wait. Do not replace the zero mux with a bubble-\ndependent hold enable, which would retain the late control dependency.\n\nAll other EX/MEM fields retain their current capture/clear rules,\nespecially ctrl='0 and valid=0 on bubbles. Forwarding eligibility uses\nreg_write independently of valid, so every bubble must still clear\nreg_write, mem_read and mem_write. Its unused arithmetic payload must\nnever become a writer, memory request, prediction update or retirement.\nKeep EX/MEM data-stall retention, MEM/WB retained forwarding, trap-\nadjusted controls, x0, youngest-writer priority and write-first register\nreads exactly. Preserve actual instruction result and source values,\nall ALU/divider arithmetic and ALTOPS behavior, load-use timing, decode\nlegality, prediction, fetch queue, nret=1 and every external contract.\nThis is one micro-optimization of the result-data/control partition;\nit adds no stage, bypass policy, arithmetic unit or execute cycles.\n\nThe intended circuit launches from a final WB-data flip-flop and ends\nat an ALU-result flip-flop whose data input has no invalid-bubble mux.\nWB selection moves into the shorter MEM input cone, and a redundant\n32-bit MEM/WB data bank and its selector register disappear. Inspect\nactual mapped timing: the divider and branch-recovery cones compete\nclosely, so deleting RTL muxes alone does not establish an improvement.\nSeparate prototype trials measured 62.052 MHz median for WB selection\nretiming and 61.287 MHz for EX bubble-gate removal, each below the 4.6\npercent margin. The final candidate combines these two ends of the\nsame loop; neither standalone result is claimed as an accepted gain.\nA shared-multiplier trial also failed to clear the margin and is excluded.\n\nRun unchanged lint, pipeline tests, formal and stalled reference\ncosimulation plus canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/completion/marker\nchecks. Exercise all load widths and signs, ALU/MUL/JAL results,\nload-use and divide bubbles, wrong-path instructions, same-rd writers,\nlong dmem holds and consumers of retained WB data. Assert correct RVFI\nsource/results, contiguous once-only retirement and unchanged latency.\nMeasure all three normal Gowin placement options and actual bracketed\ncycles. Acceptance requires fitness above 160.7702 iterations/s, or\nmedian Fmax above 63.9435 MHz if cycles remain 3,977,318. The estimate\nbelow applies to the combined candidate and remains a prediction until\nits vendor timing completes; no evaluation settings or checks change.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Replace only the separate MEM/WB alu_result and read_data fields with a single 32-bit wb_data. Preserve EX/MEM and all raw memory/RVFI metadata.'},\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Capture the existing extended-load-versus-ALU selection into wb_data before the MEM/WB edge. Preserve reset, hold_wb retention, trap controls and raw memory/RVFI data; remove the two old result captures.'},\n {'file':'rtl/wb_stage.sv','description':'Drive w_data directly from registered wb_data with the existing write enable and destination. Remove the WB data selector and update comments.'},\n *d['changes']]\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper):\n pass\ndef string(dumper,s):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nD.add_representer(str,string)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=90))\nprint('Final combined scope written:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
