ion path or implement the iteration with / or %.\n\nAdd a request/completion handshake at EX. A divide starts only for a\nvalid instruction when the older MEM operation can advance. Hold PC and\nID/EX until the result transfers, but let older MEM/WB instructions drain.\nOn divide-wait cycles clear the entire outgoing EX/MEM bundle once any\nolder memory transaction is accepted; merely clearing valid is unsafe\nbecause existing memory and forwarding enables also use control fields.\nA data-memory stall retains priority and preserves its pending request.\nCapture the forwarded source values at launch for both arithmetic and\nRVFI, since older forwarding sources dis\n…[44957 of 48029 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b4edc8f695f0c413]…\nMHz at the observed cycle count. Do not claim acceptance from\nthe current probe or select its fastest placement instead of the\nmedian. Keep the captured 32-bit operands plus opcode arrangement:\na probe registering already sign-extended 33-bit operands fell to\n59.076 MHz median, and adding preselected WB result registers fell to\n61.553 MHz. Neither rejected variant belongs in this proposal.\n\nValidate all real and ALTOPS arithmetic vectors with the new handshake,\ncaptured operands, held completion, reset cancellation, consecutive\nrequests and every signed high-product corner. Test forwarded multiply\ninputs from ALU/load/WB, immediate consumers, same-rd writers, x0,\ndependent branches, back-to-back multiplies and alternating divides,\nplus older stores and arbitrary bus stalls. Check once-only retirement,\nexact RVFI source/result data, contiguous order and memory effects.\nRun unchanged formal and stalled reference cosimulation, canonical\nCoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation and median Gowin timing.\n\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
