{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"agent_message","text":"Routing retiming alone also missed the threshold at 76.496 MHz. I’m refining the final hypothesis to combine those registered routes with narrow arithmetic slices: select local sums and carry information before a shared carry tree. This targets the remaining wide arithmetic paths without duplicating whole ALUs; the final design is unmeasured."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_61", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r13s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Partition EX into operand-candidate arithmetic slices'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 199.08 iterations/s at 79.422 MHz and 3,989,539 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Prior r8s1 registered address matches but retained live qualification and priority before arithmetic. The r12 balanced comparator gained only 3.57 percent because arithmetic and recovery paths competed. Local probes confirm that retiming routing alone leaves these paths dominant, while replicating whole ALUs creates excessive area and routing. A structural execution fabric that selects narrow arithmetic summaries before one shared carry tree targets both limitations without extra instruction latency.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the shared mux-then-wide-arithmetic EX topology with a bank of narrow operand-candidate arithmetic slices and one shared carry-prefix network. Register complete operand routes before EX so their matching and priority work is not chained through arithmetic. This is one structural redesign of operand delivery and base execution; preserve the five-stage schedule, one-retire interface, predictor, fetch queue, load-use bubble, memory protocol and blocking M-extension schedules.\n\nFirst compute exact next-cycle producer identities and write eligibility at the current ID/EX boundary. Retain the existing next_rs1/next_rs2, next_ex_rd and next_wb_rd rules. Next EX/MEM reg_write is its held value on dmem stall, zero on an EX bubble or execute_wait, otherwise the actual post-trap control that EX will capture. Next MEM/WB reg_write is its held value on hold_mem_wb, otherwise MEM's post-alignment/trap control. Do not gate retained WB eligibility with retirement valid. Expose these controls internally, without guessing from opcodes or ignoring faults.\n\nResolve nonzero-source matches, actual write eligibility and youngest EX/MEM priority over MEM/WB before the edge. Register one-hot raw routes: saved ID/EX operand, EX/MEM result, or MEM/WB result. Refresh them every edge, including consumer holds, because producers can drain. Also register four-way ALU routes, incorporating PC for AUIPC and immediate for alu_src before the edge. Use actual incoming decoded controls, or retained ID/EX controls during a hold. Reset routes to saved operand. Flushed/invalid consumers retain inert pipeline controls; unused route metadata may reflect the presented head, like existing match flags, and is refreshed before another valid consumer executes. Do not add recovery fanout merely to sanitize unused route bits. Remove obsolete match registers and post-edge priority/qualification logic.\n\nIn the new combinational execution fabric, ALU A has four candidate words: saved rs1, EX/MEM result, MEM/WB result and PC. ALU B has saved rs2, EX/MEM result, MEM/WB result and immediate. Partition every candidate into eight four-bit slices. For ADD use B unchanged and initial carry zero; for SUB, SLT, SLTU and conditional-branch comparison use complemented B and initial carry one. The conditional-branch flag selects subtraction for the comparison fabric even though the existing decoder's branch alu_op is ADD. Branch instructions never write the ALU result, so their arithmetic value is unused; preserve raw operands and all architectural branch/link/trap calculations.\n\nFor each slice and each candidate pair compute only local five-bit sums for carry-in zero and one, plus carry-generate and carry-propagate: t0={0,a4}+{0,b4_effective}, s0=t0[3:0], s1=(t0+1)[3:0], g=t0[4], p=AND(a4 XOR b4_effective). All widths must be explicit, and s1 is a local four-bit increment, not a serial inter-slice carry. Compute equality of the original uncomplemented candidate nibbles alongside these summaries. Select s0/s1/g/p/equality with the registered one-hot A/B routes, using balanced masked reductions or a factored two-dimensional selection. Constant-identical candidates may share logic. Do not build sixteen full-width ALUs, multipliers or shifters, and do not reintroduce a wide operand mux ahead of the local arithmetic.\n\nCombine the eight selected (g,p) summaries with a balanced three-level parallel-prefix network. For adjacent high and low groups use G=G_high OR (P_high AND G_low), P=P_high AND P_low. Compute each nibble boundary carry from its prefix and initial carry, then select that nibble's already-computed s0 or s1. Never ripple eight nibble carries or use a 32-bit final correction adder. This shares wide carry propagation AFTER candidate selection instead of repeating it for every operand pair. Keep full modulo-2\"'^32 arithmetic and expose the final subtraction carry for comparisons.\n\nUse the same subtraction summaries for unsigned less-than, equal and signed less-than: unsigned_less is the inverse of final carry, equality is the balanced AND of selected original-nibble equalities, and signed_less selects A'\"'s sign when original operand signs differ, otherwise unsigned_less. For the six legal branch conditions choose equal/not-equal, signed_less/not-signed_less, or unsigned_less/not-unsigned_less. Preserve default-false handling of reserved branch selectors. ADD/SUB results and SLT/SLTU bits feed the ordinary base result. LUI, Boolean operations and shifts remain single shared operations on shallow one-hot-selected ALU operands; replicate none of those wide functions.\n\nKeep raw rs1/rs2 selectors separate from PC/immediate overrides for RVFI, stores, M-extension capture and the dedicated full rs1-plus-immediate address path. Do not alter the divider, multiplier or their real/ALTOPS arithmetic and latency. Integrate the new base result without leaving a second live conventional wide ADD/SUB/comparison path selected in parallel. One option is a default-disabled external-base-result mode on alu.sv: standalone ALU tests keep its original interface behavior, while EX enables the new execution fabric and the ALU still owns the unchanged M-extension handshakes. Add internal ports or a new RTL module as needed; external core ports remain unchanged.\n\nThe structural benefit is that register routing resolves before EX, candidate arithmetic is only four bits wide, and a single balanced prefix handles carry and branch ordering. The same mechanism shortens the competing arithmetic and recovery operand paths. Estimated fitness gain is eight percent, low confidence. Acceptance requires more than 208.23768 iterations/s, approximately 83.08 MHz at unchanged 3,989,539 cycles. Candidate-summary selection fanout, added LUTs, synthesis refactoring and untouched M-extension paths may defeat the gain. Target comfortably below 10,000 logic cells; inspect inferred structure and all scored Gowin placement options.\n\nPreliminary probes are negative evidence, not measurements of this final fabric. Moving older forwarding into ID operands reached 76.220 MHz median. Replicating complete arithmetic and branch functions reached 67.618 MHz and 11,456 logic cells. Registering complete one-hot raw/ALU routes alone reached 76.496 MHz, with arithmetic/recovery paths still critical; its adapted pipeline tests and stalled reference/CoreMark cosimulation passed. None clears acceptance. The final narrow-slice/shared-prefix execution fabric has not been implemented or timed. Its prediction must be verified rather than inferred from those probes.\n\nValidate all route transitions and candidate pairs, carry/borrow crossing every nibble boundary, all-zero/all-one operands, signed extrema, opposite signs, equality and differing low nibbles. Compare randomized ADD/SUB/SLT/SLTU results and every branch predicate to independent 32-bit reference arithmetic, including PC/immediate routes. Preserve existing assertions while adapting internal selector encodings with exact one-hot/value checks. Test competing writers, x0, trapped JAL/JALR and loads, retained WB data, load-use bubbles, all holds/flush/reset transitions and M waits with draining producers. Run unchanged formal including liveness/reg/unique/pc_fwd, real and ALTOPS unit tests, stalled reference cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. Require unchanged bracketed cycles and median vendor timing for final evaluation.'''\nd['changes'].insert(0,{'file':'rtl/execute_slice.sv','description':'Add the combinational candidate-slice execution fabric: explicit four-bit local sums and original-operand equality, selected summaries, one balanced eight-slice carry-prefix network, ADD/SUB/SLT/SLTU results and branch predicates. Share shifts/Boolean operations; do not replicate complete ALUs or chain nibble carries.'})\nd['changes'].insert(1,{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Integrate the externally computed base result behind an internal/default-disabled mode or equivalent interface, pruning the old live base ADD/SUB/comparator path in the core configuration. Preserve standalone base ALU coverage and all real/ALTOPS M-extension arithmetic, constants, captured operands and handshake timing.'})\nfor c in d['changes']:\n if c['file']=='rtl/ex_stage.sv': c['description']='Export exact next EX/MEM write eligibility. Instantiate the candidate-slice execution fabric and feed registered raw/ALU routes and candidate data. Use its base results and branch predicates while preserving branch target/trap/recovery semantics, dedicated address generation, raw RVFI/store operands and unchanged M-extension handshakes.'\n if c['file']=='test/test_pipeline.py': c['description']+=' Include any new RTL module in this allowed test runner source list. Exercise slice carry/compare results through forwarding, branches and stalls without weakening architectural assertions.'\nd['changes'].append({'file':'test/test_execute_slice.py','description':'Add independent reference checks for candidate selection and ADD/SUB/SLT/SLTU plus all branch predicates, nibble carry/borrow boundaries, signed extremes, original-operand equality and randomized values. Exercise raw and PC/immediate routes and exact one-hot route assumptions.'})\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value or len(value)>140 else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final structural hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_61", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r13s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Partition EX into operand-candidate arithmetic slices'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 199.08 iterations/s at 79.422 MHz and 3,989,539 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Prior r8s1 registered address matches but retained live qualification and priority before arithmetic. The r12 balanced comparator gained only 3.57 percent because arithmetic and recovery paths competed. Local probes confirm that retiming routing alone leaves these paths dominant, while replicating whole ALUs creates excessive area and routing. A structural execution fabric that selects narrow arithmetic summaries before one shared carry tree targets both limitations without extra instruction latency.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the shared mux-then-wide-arithmetic EX topology with a bank of narrow operand-candidate arithmetic slices and one shared carry-prefix network. Register complete operand routes before EX so their matching and priority work is not chained through arithmetic. This is one structural redesign of operand delivery and base execution; preserve the five-stage schedule, one-retire interface, predictor, fetch queue, load-use bubble, memory protocol and blocking M-extension schedules.\n\nFirst compute exact next-cycle producer identities and write eligibility at the current ID/EX boundary. Retain the existing next_rs1/next_rs2, next_ex_rd and next_wb_rd rules. Next EX/MEM reg_write is its held value on dmem stall, zero on an EX bubble or execute_wait, otherwise the actual post-trap control that EX will capture. Next MEM/WB reg_write is its held value on hold_mem_wb, otherwise MEM's post-alignment/trap control. Do not gate retained WB eligibility with retirement valid. Expose these control