{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261002-002-r13s1':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'][:14000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Replace the shared mux-then-wide-arithmetic EX topology with a bank of narrow operand-candidate arithmetic slices and one shared carry-prefix network. Register complete operand routes before EX so their matching and priority work is not chained through arithmetic. This is one structural redesign of operand delivery and base execution; preserve the five-stage schedule, one-retire interface, predictor, fetch queue, load-use bubble, memory protocol and blocking M-extension schedules.\n\nFirst compute exact next-cycle producer identities and write eligibility at the current ID/EX boundary. Retain the existing next_rs1/next_rs2, next_ex_rd and next_wb_rd rules. Next EX/MEM reg_write is its held value on dmem stall, zero on an EX bubble or execute_wait, otherwise the actual post-trap control that EX will capture. Next MEM/WB reg_write is its held value on hold_mem_wb, otherwise MEM's post-alignment/trap control. Do not gate retained WB eligibility with retirement valid. Expose these controls internally, without guessing from opcodes or ignoring faults.\n\nResolve nonzero-source matches, actual write eligibility and youngest EX/MEM priority over MEM/WB before the edge. Register one-hot raw routes: saved ID/EX operand, EX/MEM result, or MEM/WB result. Refresh them every edge, including consumer holds, because producers can drain. Also register four-way ALU routes, incorporating PC for AUIPC and immediate for alu_src before the edge. Use actual incoming decoded controls, or retained ID/EX controls during a hold. Reset routes to saved operand. Flushed/invalid consumers retain inert pipeline controls; unused route metadata may reflect the presented head, like existing match flags, and is refreshed before another valid consumer executes. Do not add recovery fanout merely to sanitize unused route bits. Remove obsolete match registers and post-edge priority/qualification logic.\n\nIn the new combinational execution fabric, ALU A has four candidate words: saved rs1, EX/MEM result, MEM/WB result and PC. ALU B has saved rs2, EX/MEM res\n…[4384 of 7456 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d05f8adabc5edc5a]…\neptance. The final narrow-slice/shared-prefix execution fabric has not been implemented or timed. Its prediction must be verified rather than inferred from those probes.\n\nValidate all route transitions and candidate pairs, carry/borrow crossing every nibble boundary, all-zero/all-one operands, signed extrema, opposite signs, equality and differing low nibbles. Compare randomized ADD/SUB/SLT/SLTU results and every branch predicate to independent 32-bit reference arithmetic, including PC/immediate routes. Preserve existing assertions while adapting internal selector encodings with exact one-hot/value checks. Test competing writers, x0, trapped JAL/JALR and loads, retained WB data, load-use bubbles, all holds/flush/reset transitions and M waits with draining producers. Run unchanged formal including liveness/reg/unique/pc_fwd, real and ALTOPS unit tests, stalled reference cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. Require unchanged bracketed cycles and median vendor timing for final evaluation.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
