{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"agent_message","text":"The recovery and smaller-divider prototypes did not beat the champion; the longer divide schedule also failed liveness. The final hypothesis will instead target the EX result-selection bottleneck exposed by those probes: register results in separate operation banks and combine bank selection with forwarding. This preserves instruction latency, but its expected gain remains unmeasured."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_74", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r14s1.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-002-r14s1',\n'title':'Bank EX results before selection and flatten their forwarding into execution',\n'category':'structural',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 211.52 iterations/s at 84.388 MHz and 3,989,539\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path starts at MEM/WB data\nand crosses EX branch verification into IF. Prior r13s2 removed wide\nforwarding ahead of branch comparison, but then forwarding-to-ALU-result\nbecame critical. Structural r13s1 instead shared arithmetic slices with\nbranch verification and exposed an alu_op-to-recovery path, losing 36.79%.\nThe promising structural target is the organization of EX result capture\nand selection: the current forwarded operands feed many operations whose\nresults reconverge through a common mux before EX/MEM. Bank those results\nat the existing edge and select them as part of the next operand route,\nwhile giving branch verification its own independent comparison lanes.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the single selected EX/MEM arithmetic-result register with four\nparallel result banks and a registered one-hot result class. Integrate bank\nselection into the next instruction's operand forwarding, instead of putting\na common ALU-result mux before the capture edge. Pair this organization with\nindependent branch comparison lanes that select one-bit results after\ncomparison. This is one structural redesign of the EX feedback network;\nretain every instruction stage, execution latency, retirement edge and\npredictor policy. Do not pipeline recovery or lengthen division.\n\nUse four 32-bit result banks: arithmetic (ADD/SUB/SLT/SLTU), shift\n(SLL/SRL/SRA), logic/link (AND/OR/XOR/LUI and PC+4 for JAL/JALR), and M\n(the existing multiply/divide completion). Preserve native arithmetic and\nthe existing real/ALTOPS M units. Compute each bank's result independently;\nselect only operations within that class before its register. Do not derive\nthese banks by copying the already-selected common alu.out value. The\nlogic/link bank alone handles the jump link override, removing the final\njump-versus-full-ALU mux from the other result captures. Preserve a normal\ncombined ALU output for standalone tests if useful, but do not reconnect\nthat combined output to the timed EX/MEM bank inputs.\n\nAt the existing EX/MEM edge capture all four bank payloads whenever the\nolder memory stage can advance, including bubbles, independently of late\ninstruction-valid/execute-wait control. Hold all banks on real dmem stall.\nCapture a one-hot class selector alongside the producing instruction;\nreset gives a defined selector and payloads. A valid writing instruction\nhas exactly one class. Use original jump classification to select the link\nbank even though the decoded ALU operation is ADD. All pipeline bubbles\nstill clear valid, reg_write, mem_read, mem_write and the remaining control\nmetadata. Bank payloads of a bubble may change but can cause no effect.\nRetain the dedicated effective_addr register and raw store-data path.\n\nFor MEM/WB and RVFI, select the producer's bank result and retain the\nchampion's load-versus-ALU selection before MEM/WB.wb_data. That short\nbank-selection path ends at MEM/WB. For forwarding to EX, expose the four\nregistered bank words and their class bits directly, not just a selected\n32-bit result. For each source derive mutually exclusive route enables\nfrom the existing forwarding selector: original ID/EX value, MEM/WB value,\nor one of the four EX/MEM banks. Each bank enable is EX-forward-selected\nAND that bank's captured class. Combine masked words with an explicitly\nbalanced reduction. Preserve EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority and x0 suppression.\nRetained MEM/WB forwarding eligibility must not be gated by retirement valid.\n\nForm the actual ALU operands with PC/immediate overrides in these route\nenables: AUIPC chooses PC instead of every raw A route, and alu_src chooses\nimmediate instead of every raw B route. Avoid rebuilding a raw-forwarded\nword followed by another PC/immediate mux on the arithmetic path. Keep\nseparate exact raw rs1/rs2 selection for stores, JALR/effective addresses,\nRVFI operands and captured M-operation source values. Do not change operand\nvalues or permit speculative register/memory writes. The intended gain is\nremoving the common multi-class result selection before EX/MEM and combining\nits post-register choice with forwarding rather than serializing two muxes.\n\nKeep branch verification independent of all arithmetic-bank opcode and\ncarry logic. Use the three architectural forwarding-source candidates on\neach side: saved ID operand, selected EX/MEM bank result, and registered\nMEM/WB data. Compare the seven nonidentical source pairs in parallel;\nEX-versus-EX and WB-versus-WB have constant equality=true, less-than=false.\nEach real lane uses the champion's sixteen native two-bit equality/unsigned\nordering leaves and four balanced high/low merge levels. Derive signed\nordering from original sign bits. Select the one-bit equality/ordering\nresults using the existing forwarding selectors, then apply the captured\nbranch_eq/branch_signed/branch_unsigned/branch_invert controls. A source\npair must never use a subtract result whose mode depends on alu_op. This\navoids the precise r13s1 failure while moving wide source selection after\ncomparison, as demonstrated by r13s2. Keep the EX-bank selection confined\nto its candidate; the WB and original-source comparison lanes must not\ntraverse that mux. Preserve original raw RVFI operand values separately.\n\nKeep the original legal/aligned actual_taken, ex_accept including\n\"'!execute_wait, architectural pc_next, redirect edge, recovery target,\ntraining edge and target-fault behavior. Keep the 64-entry predictor,\nregistered training, fall-through queue and all hazards unchanged. Do not\nadd early load forwarding, a recovery register, speculative arithmetic\nrequests or different memory acceptance. Preserve the existing two-edge\nmultiply and nine-edge divide transfer schedules, captured operands and\nheld completion. Keep nret=1, decoder default-illegal behavior, all memory\nand RVFI ports, and every proof/benchmark invariant.\n\nExpect an eight percent fitness gain, with low confidence: the final banked\nexecution topology has not been implemented or measured. Register banks add\nroughly 96 physical payload bits over the single result register before\nsynthesis, plus class metadata; comparison replication adds LUTs and may\nincrease routing cost. Keep the implementation comfortably below 10,000\nlogic cells. A naive bank mux feeding the original forwarding mux defeats\nthe architectural purpose; inspect the timed netlist paths to establish\nthat bank and operand routes are combined. General shifter, memory, divider\nand branch-recovery paths can still limit the clock, so acceptance depends\non measured median Fmax times measured iterations/cycle.\n\nLocal disposable probes during hypothesis generation reinforce the need to\naddress competing feedback paths; they are not evidence for this unbuilt\nbanked design. Delaying recovery one cycle reached 85.259 MHz but increased\nCoreMark cycles and failed liveness. Registered logical fetch rebasing kept\n3,989,539 cycles and passed all 53 unchanged formal checks, but reached only\n83.651 MHz. A smaller radix-16 divider reduced area to 4,403 logic cells and\n971 registers, yet reached only 83.931 MHz; its longer schedule failed\nliveness in a combined probe. These approaches are rejected. Do not import\nany of their recovery, FIFO, divider or latency changes into this proposal.\nThe proposal instead changes the result-capture/bypass structure while\npreserving the champion'\"'s schedule and arithmetic algorithms.\n\nValidate every result class and every route, including back-to-back\nsame/different classes, youngest competing writers, x0, AUIPC/immediate\nselection, jumps and target faults, retained WB values, long bus holds,\nload-use bubbles, and M waits/completion with draining producers. Test\nparallel branch predicates for all source pairs, same-producer constants,\nsigned extremes and differing bits in every two-bit leaf. Check precise\nRVFI sources/results/PCs/traps/orders and no wrong-path bus effects. Preserve\nall existing architectural tests; update internal packet-layout assertions\nonly where the new bank representation requires it. Run both real and\nALTOPS unit suites, all unchanged formal gates, stalled reference cosim,\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and every scored Gowin\nplacement. Require unchanged 3,989,539 bracketed cycles. At that count,\nacceptance requires Fmax above approximately 88.27 MHz and fitness above\n221.24992 iterations/s. Never relax formal depth or weaken liveness.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Represent four EX/MEM result banks and a one-hot result class, preserving architectural metadata, instruction validity, dedicated effective address and raw operands. Keep IF and ID prediction packet conventions unchanged.'},\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Expose independent arithmetic, shift, logic and M result lanes computed directly from operands. Retain a combined standalone output and existing arithmetic definitions, real/ALTOPS multiplier/divider interfaces, latency and held results. Avoid a common full-result mux feeding any bank.'},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Capture class-specific results at the original EX/MEM edge, with only genuine memory hold on payload banks and inert bubble controls. Combine bank selection with operand forwarding and PC/immediate selection. Preserve separate raw operands and dedicated address generation. Implement independent balanced branch comparison lanes followed by one-bit selection, retaining original architectural branch and recovery/training equations.'},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Pass EX/MEM bank payloads and captured class to EX forwarding. Keep original hazard timing, memory wiring, selected WB result and nret=1 retirement interface.'},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Select the captured result bank before the existing load/ALU MEM/WB capture. Preserve load extraction, store lanes, misalignment suppression, memory handshakes and retained WB forwarding data.'},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain existing real and ALTOPS arithmetic assertions and handshakes; verify exposed class lanes against independent RV32I results and unchanged M completion behavior.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Extend result-bank, routing and parallel-branch coverage through competing writers, class transitions, raw versus immediate/PC sources, traps, resets, stalls and blocking arithmetic. Assert original retirement/recovery timing, complete RVFI and exact bank selection without weakening existing architectural checks.'}\n]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent(dumper,s):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,represent)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint(f'{p}: final structural hypothesis written and schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_74", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r14s1.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-002-r14s1',\n'title':'Bank EX results before selection and flatten their forwarding into execution',\n'category':'structural',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 211.52 iterations/s at 84.388 MHz and 3,989,539\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path starts at MEM/WB data\nand crosses EX branch verification into IF. Prior r13s2 removed wide\nforwarding ahead of branch comparison, but then forwarding-to-ALU-result\nbecame critical. Structural r13s1 instead shared arithmetic slices with\nbranch verification and exposed an alu_op-to-recovery path, losing 36.79%.\nThe promising structural target is the organization of EX result capture\nand selection: the current forwarded operands feed many operations whose\nresults reconverge through a common mux before EX/MEM. Bank those results\nat the existing edge and select them as part of the next operand route,\nwhile giving branch verification its own independent comparison lanes.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the single selected EX/MEM arithmetic-result register with four\nparallel result banks and a registered one-hot result class. Integrate bank\nselection into the next instruction's operand forwarding, instead of putting\na common ALU-result mux before the capture edge. Pair this organization with\nindependent branch comparison lanes that select one-bit results after\ncomparison. This is one structural redesign of the EX feedback network;\nretain every instruction stage, execution latency, retirement edge and\npredictor policy. Do not pipeline recovery or lengthen division.\n\nUse four 32-bit result banks: arithmetic (ADD/SUB/SLT/SLTU), shift\n(SLL/SRL/SRA), logic/link (AND/OR/XOR/LUI and PC+4 for JAL/JALR), and M\n(the existing multiply/divide completion). Preserve native arithmetic and\nthe existing real/ALTOPS M units. Compute each bank's result independently;\nselect only operations within that class before its register. Do not derive\nthese banks by copying the already-selected common alu.out value. The\nlogic/link bank alone handles the jump link override, removing the final\njump-versus-full-ALU mux from the other result captures. Preserve a normal\ncombined ALU output for standalone tests if useful, but do not reconnect\nthat combined output to the timed EX/MEM bank inputs.\n\nAt the existing EX/MEM edge capture all four bank payloads whenever the\nolder memory stage can advance, including bubbles, independently of late\ninstruction-valid/execute-wait control. Hold all banks on real dmem stall.\nCapture a one-hot class selector alongside the producing instruction;\nreset gives a defined selector and payloads. A valid writing instruction\nhas exactly one class. Use original jump classification to select the link\nbank even though the decoded ALU operation is ADD. All pipeline bubbles\nstill clear valid, reg_write, mem_read, mem_write and the remaining control\nmetadata. Bank payloads of a bubble may change but can cause no effect.\nRetain the dedicated effective_addr register and raw store-data path.\n\nFor MEM/WB and RVFI, select the producer's bank result and retain the\nchampion's load-versus-ALU selection before MEM/WB.wb_data. That short\nbank-selection path ends at MEM/WB. For forwarding to EX, expose the four\nregistered bank words and their class bits directly, not just a selected\n32-bit result. For each source derive mutually exclusive route enables\nfrom the existing forwarding selector: original ID/EX value, MEM/WB value,\nor one of the four EX/MEM banks. Each bank enable is EX-forward-selected\nAND that bank's captured class. Combine masked words with an explicitly\nbalanced reduction. Preserve EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority and x0 suppression.\nRetained MEM/WB forwarding eligibility must not be gated by retirement valid.\n\nForm the actual ALU operands with PC/immediate overrides in these route\nenables: AUIPC chooses PC instead of every raw A route, and alu_src chooses\nimmediate instead of every raw B route. Avoid rebuilding a raw-forwarded\nword followed by another PC/immediate mux on the arithmetic path. Keep\nseparate exact raw rs1/rs2 selection for stores, JALR/effective addresses,\nRVFI operands and captured M-operation source values. Do not change operand\nvalues or permit speculative register/memory writes. The intended gain is\nremoving the common multi-class result selection before EX/MEM and combining\nits post-register choice with forwarding rather than serializing two muxes.\n\nKeep branch verification independent of all arithmetic-bank opcode and\ncarry logic. Use the three architectural forwarding-source candidates on\neach side: saved ID operand, selected EX/MEM bank result, and registered\nMEM/WB data. Compare the seven nonidentical source pairs in parallel;\nEX-versus-EX and WB-versus-WB have constant equality=true, less-than=false.\nEach real lane uses the champion's sixteen native two-bit equality/unsigned\nordering leaves and four balanced high/low merge levels. Derive signed\nordering from original sign bits. Select the one-bit equality/ordering\nresults using the existing forwarding selectors, then apply the captured\nbranch_eq/branch_signed/branch_unsigned/branch_invert controls. A source\npair must never use a subtract result whose mode depends on alu_op. This\navoids the precise r13s1 failure while moving wide source selection after\ncomparison, as demonstrated by r13s2. Keep the EX-bank selection confined\nto its candidate; the WB and original-source comparison lanes must not\ntraverse that mux. Preserve original raw RVFI operand values separately.\n\nKeep the original legal/aligned actual_taken, ex_accept including\n\"'!execute_wait, architectural pc_next, redirect edge, recovery target,\ntraining edge and target-fault behavior. Keep the 64-entry predictor,\nregistered training, fall-through queue and all hazards unchanged. Do not\nadd early load forwarding, a recovery register, speculative arithmetic\nrequests or different memory acceptance. Preserve the existing two-edge\nmultiply and nine-edge divide transfer schedules, captured operands and\nheld completion. Keep nret=1, decoder default-illegal behavior, all memory\nand RVFI ports, and every proof/benchmark invariant.\n\nExpect an eight percent fitness gain, with low confidence: the final banked\nexecution topology has not been implemented or measured. Register banks add\nroughly 96 physical payload bits over the single result register before\nsynthesis, plus class metadata; comparison replication adds LUTs and may\nincrease routing cost. Keep the implementation comfortably below 10,000\nlogic cells. A naive bank mux feeding the original forwarding mux defeats\nthe architectural purpose; inspect the timed netlist paths to establish\nthat bank and operand routes are combined. General shifter, memory, divider\nand branch-recovery paths can still limit the clock, so acceptance depends\non measured median Fmax times measured iterations/cycle.\n\nLocal disposable probes during hypothesis generation reinforce the need to\naddress competing feedback paths; they are not evidence for this unbuilt\nbanked design. Delaying recovery one cycle reached 85.259 MHz but increased\nCoreMark cycles and failed liveness. Registered logical fetch rebasing kept\n3,989,539 cycles and passed all 53 unchanged formal checks, but reached only\n83.651 MHz. A smaller radix-16 divider reduced area to 4,403 logic cells and\n971 registers, yet reached only 83.931 MHz; its longer schedule failed\nliveness in a combined probe. These approaches are rejected. Do not import\nany of their recovery, FIFO, divider or latency changes into this proposal.\nThe proposal instead changes the result-capture/bypass structure while\npreserving the champion'\"'s schedule and arithmetic algorithms.\n\nValidate every result class and every route, including back-to-back\nsame/different classes, youngest competing writers, x0, AUIPC/immediate\nselection, jumps and target faults, retained WB values, long bus holds,\nload-use bubbles, and M waits/completion with draining producers. Test\nparallel branch predicates for all source pairs, same-producer constants,\nsigned extremes and differing bits in every two-bit leaf. Check precise\nRVFI sources/results/PCs/traps/orders and no wrong-path bus effects. Preserve\nall existing architectural tests; update internal packet-layout assertions\nonly where the new bank representation requires it. Run both real and\nALTOPS unit suites, all unchanged formal gates, stalled reference cosim,\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and every scored Gowin\nplacement. Require unchanged 3,989,539 bracketed cycles. At that count,\nacceptance requires Fmax above approximately 88.27 MHz and fitness above\n221.24992 iterations/s. Never relax formal depth or weaken liveness.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Represent four EX/MEM result banks and a one-hot result class, preserving architectural metadata, instruction validity, dedicated effective address and raw operands. Keep IF and ID prediction packet conventions unchanged.'},\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Expose independent arithmetic, shift, logic and M result lanes computed directly from operands. Retain a combined standalone output and existing arithmetic definitions, real/ALTOPS multiplier/divider interfaces, latency and held results. Avoid a common full-result mux feeding any bank.'},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Capture class-specific results at the original EX/MEM edge, with only genuine memory hold on payload banks and inert bubble controls. Combine bank selection with operand forwarding and PC/immediate selection. Preserve separate raw operands and dedicated address generation. Implement independent balanced branch comparison lanes followed by one-bit selection, retaining original architectural branch and recovery/training equations.'},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Pass EX/MEM bank payloads and captured class to EX forwarding. Keep original hazard timing, memory wiring, selected WB result and nret=1 retirement interface.'},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Select the captured result bank before the existing load/ALU MEM/WB capture. Preserve load extraction, store lanes, misalignment suppression, memory handshakes and retained WB forwarding data.'},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain existing real and ALTOPS arithmetic assertions and handshakes; verify exposed class lanes against independent RV32I results and unchanged M completion behavior.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Extend result-bank, routing and parallel-branch coverage through competing writers, class transitions, raw versus immediate/PC sources, traps, resets, stalls and blocking arithmetic. Assert original retirement/recovery timing, complete RVFI and exact bank selection without weakening existing architectural checks.'}\n]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent(dumper,s):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,represent)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint(f'{p}: final structural hypothesis written and schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r14s1.yaml: final structural hypothesis written and schema valid\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
