{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r7s1.yaml');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('''  of cycles. Prior structural arithmetic changes face a divider timing\n  ceiling: a disposable MEM-stage multiplier prototype removed the EX\n  multiply cone but measured only 56.463 MHz median. A small elastic\n  queue instead targets wasted fetch opportunities and iterations/cycle.\n''','''  of cycles. Structural attempt hyp-20261001-002-r5s1 paid 4.46 percent\n  more cycles for registered multiplication, while hyp-20261001-002-r6s1\n  lost fitness after shortening the divider. LESSONS.md shows diminishing\n  returns from arithmetic staging as other EX paths become limiting.\n  A small elastic queue targets wasted fetch opportunities and cycles.\n''');s=s.replace('''  Expect a 7 percent net fitness gain with medium confidence, pending\n  measurements.''','''  Expect a 7 percent net fitness gain with medium confidence.''');s=s.replace('''expected_impact:\n''','''  A disposable prototype of this exact four-entry circular, fall-through\n  structure completed canonical stalled CoreMark in 3,977,318 bracketed\n  cycles versus 4,201,709, a 5.34 percent cycle reduction. The unchanged\n  validator passed all CRC/UART/bounds/completion/marker checks. Gowin\n  placement options 0/1/2 measured 56.359/58.222/58.222 MHz, for a median\n  of 58.222 MHz. Their product projects 146.3851 iterations/s, 7.30 percent\n  above 136.42 and above the 142.69532 acceptance threshold. Option-0\n  resources were 4,094 logic cells, 813 FFs, 49 LUT-RAM, four BSRAM and\n  six DSPs. The worst paths remain EX arithmetic and divider recurrence.\n  Preserve the circular representation and unreset payload storage used\n  by this prototype; changing to a shifting flop queue is not measured.\n\n  All 26 existing pipeline tests passed after retaining their complete\n  architectural assertions and adapting the predictor observer to model\n  a software FIFO separately from speculative fetch PC. The check that\n  a stalled branch cannot redirect remains; speculative fetch may now\n  continue while it waits. The stalled selftest also passed full RVFI\n  comparison for 115 retirements. These are preliminary prototype results,\n  not completed orchestrator acceptance. Full formal and reference-cosim\n  results must still pass the unchanged gates before implementation can\n  be accepted. At this measured cycle count the acceptance threshold\n  requires median Fmax above 56.75447 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n''');p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
