{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_108","type":"agent_message","text":"The plain-vector version preserved CoreMark’s cycle count but mapped worse in Gowin. I’m testing a tool-specific declaration for the same 66-bit FIFO: packed structs for Gowin/Verilator and plain vectors for Yosys. The queue’s contents and control logic stay identical."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_109","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv');s=p.read_text().replace('  logic [65:0] entries [0:DEPTH-1];','''\"'`ifdef YOSYS\n  // The Yosys frontend loses unpacked dimensions on struct typedef arrays.\n  // Same 66 packed bits per entry, same array depth and read/write logic.\n  logic [65:0] entries [0:DEPTH-1];\n`else\n  if_id_t entries [0:DEPTH-1];\n`endif'\"''');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r7s1.yaml');s=p.read_text();start=s.index('  three-bit occupancy count.');end=s.index('  word and imemReady,',start);s=s[:start]+'''  three-bit occupancy count. Store one full 66-bit if_id_t packet per\n  entry. Use if_id_t entries [0:3] for Gowin/Verilator. The Yosys frontend\n  loses the unpacked array dimension on this struct typedef, producing\n  an actual pc_fwd failure. Under its predefined YOSYS macro declare\n  logic [65:0] entries [0:3] instead. This is solely a frontend syntax\n  workaround: identical packed field order, 66-bit width, four entries,\n  and bit-for-bit shared read/write/valid/pointer/control expressions.\n  Do not branch on FORMAL/ALTOPS or substitute behavioral logic. Test\n  both declarations in simulation against the same architectural traces\n  and queue scoreboard; formal must analyze the complete four-entry FIFO.\n  Gowin's plain-vector declaration maps differently and measured only\n  52.686 MHz, so preserve the vendor's measured struct-array declaration.\n  Empty queue output bypasses the live bus\n'''+s[end:];p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
