{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_49", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261001-001-r3s0': print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Replace each of the six restoring steps' inferred full-width trial\nsubtraction with an explicit byte-partitioned carry-select subtractor\nwhose inter-byte borrows use parallel lookahead. Retain the restoring\nalgorithm, six-step unroll, five full iterations plus a final two-step\niteration, and all existing architectural and handshake behavior. This\nis one local arithmetic micro-optimization, with no pipeline changes.\n\nFor each step let X = {remainder_step[i], quotient_step[i][31]} at\n33 bits and D = divisor_q at 32 bits. For each byte k=0..3, independently\ncompute two explicitly unsigned nine-bit differences:\n  T0[k] = {1'b0, X[8*k +: 8]} - {1'b0, D[8*k +: 8]}\n  T1[k] = {1'b0, X[8*k +: 8]} - {1'b0, D[8*k +: 8]} - 9'd1.\nBoth candidates must be computed in parallel from the input bytes;\ndo not wait for the actual incoming borrow before doing subtraction.\nDefine G[k] = T0[k][8] and P[k] = (X_byte[k] == D_byte[k]).\nG is the outgoing borrow with incoming borrow zero; P means an\nincoming borrow propagates through an equal pair of bytes.\n\nCompute byte-boundary borrows directly from these group signals:\n  B0 = 0\n  B1 = G0\n  B2 = G1 | (P1 & G0)\n  B3 = G2 | (P2 & G1) | (P2 & P1 & G0)\n  B4 = G3 | (P3 & G2) | (P3 & P2 & G1) | (P3 & P2 & P1 & G0).\nUse explicit balanced Boolean expressions for the lookahead, rather\nthan a serial chain of byte-borrow muxes. Select each result byte as\nBk ? T1[k][7:0] : T0[k][7:0]. Since the extended divisor's bit 32 is\nzero, the original trial subtraction's bit 32 is X[32] XOR B4. Retain\nthat bit exactly: it controls selection of the old shifted remainder\nversus the difference and supplies the complemented quotient bit.\nDo not drop X[32], truncate trial candidates, infer signed arithmetic,\nor replace this bit with B4 alone. The resulting trial vector must\nequal the original 33-bit modular subtraction for every input pair.\n\nKeep this helper local to rtl/divider.sv and instantiate or inline it\nat each existing step using static generate indices. Use ordinary\nsynthesizable RTL accepted by Gowin and the formal frontend. The\nintended dependency is an eight-bit local carry chain, a small group\nborrow network, and byte selection, instead of a 33-bit carry chain\nat every quotient bit. Do not add registers, duplicate the whole\ndivider, change the number of effective dividend shifts, or add\nunrelated arithmetic, predictor, hazard, or register-file changes.\n\nPreserve edge 1 capture/normalization, edges 2..7 iteration, edge 8\ncorrection/result_valid, and earliest edge 9 result transfer. Keep\nquotient/remainder selection, signed truncation toward zero, original\ndividend remainder on division by zero, all-ones zero-divisor quotient,\nINT_MIN/-1 handling, reset cancellation, and stable held completion.\nKeep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas and identical control schedule;\nthe carry-select datapath belongs only in the real-arithmetic branch.\nPreserve the nret=1 external interface and every existing invariant.\n\nPredict a 20 percent fitness gain with medium confidence, from a\nshorter divider feedback path and unchanged instruction-cycle counts.\nThis is unmeasured. Parallel byte candidates add arithmetic and mux\narea, and Gowin may favor its native carry chain or move the critical\npath to multiplication/forwarding. A successful implementation must\ndemonstrate the intended shorter path in vendor timing and exceed\n94.27598 iterations/s, the champion times 1.046. With unchanged\n4,491,485 bracketed cycles, the corresponding Fmax threshold is about\n42.344 MHz. Use actual measured cycles and median Gowin Fmax to decide.\n\nValidate subtraction equivalence independently