ill occupy EX/MEM or MEM/WB after the next\n  edge. With stall_id meaning ID/EX holds, compute next_rs1/next_rs2 as\n  stall_id ? id_ex_rs?_addr : if_id.instr's source bitfields. Compute\n  next_ex_rd as stall_ex_mem ? ex_mem.rd : id_ex.rd, and next_wb_rd as\n  hold_mem_wb ? mem_wb.rd : ex_mem.\n…[6561 of 9633 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8ed0f55b48541658]…\ng real/ALTOPS arithmetic vector and exact\n      latency assertion. Add all radix-8 digit choices and boundaries\n      around kD, divisors whose 3D/5D/7D overflow 32 bits, high-bit\n      magnitudes, signed extrema, zero divisors, held completion with\n      changing live inputs, reset cancellation and consecutive requests.\n      Compare complete architectural results against the RV32M model.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve all existing pipeline assertions. Exercise the new digit\n      boundaries with forwarded divide operands, adjacent divides and\n      dependent consumers under imem/dmem stalls. Check bit-exact RVFI\n      results and saved source operands, once-only retirement, contiguous\n      order, unchanged divide latency and exactly-once memory effects.\n      Exercise same-rd writers in both forwarding stages, x0, load-use\n      bubbles, retained MEM/WB forwarding over long data stalls, producer\n      drain during divide wait, reset, redirects and trap-suppressed writes.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
