{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261001-002-r5s1|hyp-20261002-002-r8s1|hyp-20261002-003-r8s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division off the single-cycle EX path with a shared clocked divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The sole recorded baseline scores 12.12 iterations/s at 5.442 MHz. Its\\nworst reported path is 199.837 ns through forwarding and the EX ALU,\\nwith 156 cells. The ALU currently evaluates full-width signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder combinationally. This strongly suggests\\nthat the unrolled divider constrains the clock for every instruction,\\nalthough a detailed cell-level timing report must confirm the inference.\\nThere is no LESSONS.md and no previous structural attempt in log.jsonl.\\nBreaking this arithmetic dependency across clock edges is a substantially\\nlarger opportunity than the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The sole recorded baseline scores 12.12 iterations/s at 5.442 MHz. Its\\nworst reported path is 199.837 ns through forwarding and the EX ALU,\\nwith 156 cells. The ALU currently evaluates full-width signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder combinationally. This strongly suggests\\nthat the unrolled divider constrains the clock for every instruction,\\nalthough a detailed cell-level timing report must confirm the inference.\\nThere is no LESSONS.md and no previous structural attempt in log.jsonl.\\nBreaking this arithmetic dependency across clock edges is a substantially\\nlarger opportunity than the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU execution path with one\\nshared, blocking, clocked divider. Keep the existing single-cycle base\\nALU and multiplier paths. Capture the forwarded operands and operation\\nonce, normalize signed operands to unsigned magnitudes, and reuse an\\neight-step radix-2 restoring divide datapath for four iteration clocks.\\nEach step shifts the partial remainder and quotient/dividend and uses\\none 33-bit trial subtraction to select the next remainder and quotient\\nbit. Register normalization before iteration and register\n…[121221 of 124293 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6dab445096089108]…\nde=1)\\nSBY  1:21:38 [liveness_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY  1:21:38 [liveness_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:23 (23)\\nSBY  1:21:38 [liveness_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:22 (22)\\nSBY  1:21:38 [liveness_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY  1:21:38 [liveness_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: liveness_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY  1:21:38 [liveness_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_liveness_check_sv_38_58 at rvfi_liveness_check.sv:38.5-38.28 step 20\\nSBY  1:21:38 [liveness_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261002-003-r8s2/formal/last_run-h13d4fe8ad5e9460.log\\nPer-check logs in: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261002-003-r8s2/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-h13d4fe8ad5e9460/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
