{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_106","type":"agent_message","text":"Capturing sign extension earlier reduced median Fmax, so I’ve dropped that variant. I’m checking one final arrangement of the execution path: the better operand-capture multiplier plus a registered final WB value. Both shorten the path from WB through EX arithmetic; neither adds a pipeline stage.\n"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_107", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r9s1.yaml');s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('title: \\\"Capture multiply operands and use EX/MEM as the product register\\\"','title: \\\"Retime the EX feedback path with captured multiply operands and final WB values\\\"')\ns=s.replace('sign-extended operands and result-half bit; edge 2 captures the product','operands and multiply opcode; edge 2 captures the selected product')\ns=s.replace('  On request acceptance save signed 33-bit A and B, a low-half selection\\\\n  bit and set pending. Decode signedness BEFORE this operand-register edge.','  On request acceptance save 32-bit A, B and the opcode, and set pending.')\ns=s.replace(\\\"  backpressure. Capture A's extra bit as A[31] only for MULH/MULHSU,\\\\n  and B's extra bit as B[31] only for MULH; otherwise capture zero.\\\\n  Capture low-half selection as op==MUL. Do not register just 32-bit\\\\n  operands then decode their signedness before the DSPs in the next\\\\n  cycle. Multiply the saved signed 33-bit operands into a signed 66-bit\\\", \\\"  backpressure. A's signed extension bit is saved A[31] only for MULH\\\\n  and MULHSU; B's is saved B[31] only for MULH. Otherwise extend with\\\\n  zero. Multiply explicit signed 33-bit operands into a signed 66-bit\\\")\ns=s.replace('  before its operand registers. The product stage uses only the signed\\\\n  operand registers and saved low-half selection; it has no opcode decoder.', '  before its operand registers. Sign extension and high/low result\\\\n  selection use the captured opcode, not the live instruction.')\ns=s.replace('  using the original constants. Capture the 32-bit operands and opcode\\\\n  separately in the ALTOPS branch when needed. Only arithmetic changes under ALTOPS;', '  using the original constants. Only arithmetic changes under ALTOPS;')\ns=s.replace('  This single multiply-boundary change should trade roughly half the\\\\n  earlier multiplier proposal\\\\'s cycle penalty for a shorter global EX\\\\n  path and fewer DSPs.', '''  Complete the EX feedback-path retiming by moving WB's load-versus-ALU\n  mux before the existing MEM/WB register. Replace mem_wb_t.alu_result\n  and read_data with one 32-bit wb_value captured in MEM as\n  in.ctrl.mem_to_reg ? load_data : in.alu_result. WB directly wires that\n  registered value to the register file, forwarding and RVFI; keep its\n  write-enable and destination semantics unchanged. Retain raw memory\n  data and all RVFI fields independently. On hold_mem_wb keep wb_value\n  and destination/control metadata while clearing only retirement valid,\n  preserving forwarding of the last retired value through a long dmem\n  stall. Keep reset, aligned load extraction, traps and x0 unchanged.\n  This moves selection off ordinary WB-to-EX ALU/redirect paths while\n  multiplication's operand registers break the deeper arithmetic path.\n  These are the two boundaries of one EX feedback-path restructuring;\n  do not add unrelated divider, predictor or memory-system changes.\n\n  A measured operand-capture multiplier alone consumed 3,989,539 cycles,\n  only 0.31 percent above the champion with the current fetch queue,\n  and reached 63.735 MHz median, about 3.94 percent net improvement.\n  Separately moving WB selection reached 62.052 MHz at unchanged cycles.\n  Neither alone cleared acceptance. Their combination is the proposed\n  candidate, with no assumption that frequency gains add linearly.''')\ns=s.replace('      33-by-33 shared product from saved sign-extended operands. Capture\\\\n      signedness before the operand edge and one high/low selection bit.', '      33-by-33 shared product from saved 32-bit operands and opcode.\\\\n      Form signed extensions and select the result from saved metadata.')\ns += '''  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the separate MEM/WB ALU and load-result registers with\n      one 32-bit wb_value. Preserve all other RVFI and control fields.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Select the extracted load result versus ALU result before the\n      MEM/WB edge. Capture wb_value, clear it on reset and retain it\n      when hold_wb clears valid. Preserve memory outputs, traps and\n      raw RVFI memory data, masks and addresses.\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive w_data directly from registered wb_value, removing the\n      late mem_to_reg mux. Keep existing w_en and w_addr semantics,\n      including forwarding consumers of retained WB data during holds.\n'''\np.write_text(s)\nprint('Final-boundary candidate saved.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
