{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_116","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema,shutil\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r9s1.yaml');s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('title: \\\"Retime the EX feedback path with captured multiply operands and final WB values\\\"','title: \\\"Capture multiply operands and use EX/MEM as the product register\\\"')\nstart=s.index('  Complete the EX feedback-path retiming')\nend=s.index('  Validate all real and ALTOPS arithmetic vectors',start)\ns=s[:start]+'''  A disposable prototype of this exact two-cycle multiplier measured\n  59.786, 63.735 and 63.735 MHz for Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2,\n  giving a 63.735 MHz median. It used 4,353 logic cells, 955 flip-flops,\n  49 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. CoreMark completed in 3,989,539\n  bracketed cycles with all canonical CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks\n  passing: only 0.31 percent more cycles than the champion. Its median\n  projected fitness is approximately 159.76 iterations/s, a 3.94 percent\n  improvement, which DOES NOT yet clear the 4.6 percent acceptance gate.\n  The same prototype passed both existing pipeline test variants, all\n  handshake-adapted ALU vectors in real and ALTOPS builds, stalled and\n  unstalled selftest reference cosimulation, lint, and all 53 unchanged\n  ALTOPS formal checks. ALTOPS does not prove real multiply arithmetic.\n\n  The operand boundary removes the multiplier from the leading paths;\n  the divider recurrence is now dominant. Keep the current radix-8\n  divider unchanged in this hypothesis, avoiding a second architectural\n  angle. Target six percent net improvement with low confidence: the\n  positive prototype is close, but additional frequency headroom in the\n  final implementation is unproven. Acceptance still requires fitness\n  greater than 160.7702 iterations/s, equivalent to median Fmax above\n  64.140 MHz at the observed cycle count. Do not claim acceptance from\n  the current probe or select its fastest placement instead of the\n  median. Keep the captured 32-bit operands plus opcode arrangement:\n  a probe registering already sign-extended 33-bit operands fell to\n  59.076 MHz median, and adding preselected WB result registers fell to\n  61.553 MHz. Neither rejected variant belongs in this proposal.\n\n'''+s[end:]\nstart=s.index('  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\n')\ns=s[:start]\np.write_text(s)\nd=yaml.safe_load(s)\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261002-002-r9s1'\nassert d['category']=='structural'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Final hypothesis valid:',p)\nprint('Measured fitness:',63.735*1e6*10/3989539)\nprint('Required Fmax:',160.7702*3989539/10/1e6)\nbackup=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/9e6b10b9/0bf4956d/r9s1-original-rtl')\nfor name in ['core_pkg.sv','mem_stage.sv','wb_stage.sv','alu.sv','ex_stage.sv']:\n shutil.copyfile(backup/name,Path('cores/bench/rtl')/name)\nshutil.copyfile('/srv/hwebench/tmp/9e6b10b9/0bf4956d/r9s1-original-test_alu.py','cores/bench/test/test_alu.py')\nprint('Restored all temporary RTL and test edits.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
