 deferred metadata, bypassing verification only for that case. Keep ordinary branch/jump resolution in EX. Add an older-recovery kill with priority over holds; suppress killed divider launch, acceptance, redirects and learning. Preserve normal ALU, divide and memory datapaths.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Verify only deferred branches using marked operands repaired from matching WB writes, with correct trapping-load fallbacks. Produce accepted MEM recovery and training events, resolved RVFI operands, next PC and trap state. Preserve all existing load/store formatting, alignment, bus and WB-retention behavior.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Provide decode-head instruction qualification and WB fallback/repair metadata. Merge MEM and EX recovery by age, wire the EX kill and IF/ID flush, and arbitrate the existing single training input with eligible MEM learning ahead of EX learning. On a simultaneous correct-path collision intentionally drop only the younger EX learning event; never stall execution for predictor updates. Keep the persistent IF table and registered update implementation unchanged.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Extend predictor observation for selective MEM verification and explicit MEM-priority learning collisions, retaining every architectural assertion. Add warm dependent-branch cycle checks, independent EX-resolution checks, all conditions and operand dependencies, stalls, reset, trapping-load fallback, target faults, full-queue recovery and wrong-path store/divide/jump suppression. Include load/branch/divide and consecutive branch sequences relevant to bounded liveness; never relax the unchanged formal liveness gate.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=92))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()));print('Revised hypothesis is schema valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Revised hypothesis is schema valid: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r10s2.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
