and-repair flags and the original prediction in EX/MEM. Reuse its existing full-width branch_target, PC, source addresses and source values. A branch immediately behind a load may advance early only because this deferred path will verify it; ordinary load-use interlocks remain for all nonbra\n…[6463 of 9535 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:52f43d3ff99b5eb9]…\nde-head instruction qualification and WB fallback/repair metadata. Merge MEM and EX recovery by age, wire the EX kill and IF/ID flush, and arbitrate the existing single training input with eligible MEM learning ahead of EX learning. On a simultaneous correct-path collision intentionally drop only the younger EX learning event; never stall execution for predictor updates. Keep the persistent IF table and registered update implementation unchanged.\n- file: test/test_pipeline.py\n  description: |-\n    Extend predictor observation for selective MEM verification and explicit MEM-priority learning collisions, retaining every architectural assertion. Add warm dependent-branch cycle checks, independent EX-resolution checks, all conditions and operand dependencies, stalls, reset, trapping-load fallback, target faults, full-queue recovery and wrong-path store/divide/jump suppression. Include load/branch/divide and consecutive branch sequences relevant to bounded liveness; never relax the unchanged formal liveness gate.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
