d PC and immediate.\\nMoving these existing results with the prediction offers a different\\nopportunity: remove duplicated adders from recovery and the jump-link\\nresult path while preserving every prediction decision and cycle.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Extend the existing direct predictor's metadata with two full-width\\nvalues: direct_target, computed in IF from the current instruction's\\nB/J immediate, and fallthrough_pc, computed as current PC+4. Carry\\nboth through if_id_t into id_ex_t alongside predicted_taken. Capture\\nthem only with an accepted instruction; hold them with the entire\\nID/EX payload during stalls and clear th\n…[21241 of 24313 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0f597f8e64d09b2b]…\n-edge lookup, fetch queue and immediate\\nEX recovery; do not assume or force RAM inference.\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Model one-cycle pending training separately from accepted EX events,\\nand retain the abstract counter history across runtime resets. Establish\\nknown predictor states through training or fresh simulation rather than\\nassuming reset restores weakly taken. Check consecutive same-index\\noutcomes, saturation, pre-edge lookup, bubbles/stalls without duplicate\\nupdates, pending-event cancellation on reset, retained history after\\nreset, and an older event surviving younger recovery. Preserve every\\narchitectural, queue, wrong-path-side-effect, trap, forwarding, arithmetic\\nand RVFI-order assertion; add repeated-reset directed coverage.'}]}\nNOTES: \nhyp-20261002-002-r10s1 Repartition M-extension execution at operand and completion registers improvement 185.62 3989539\nhyp-20261002-003-r10s2 Selectively verify load-dependent predicted branches in MEM regression 152.82 3865867\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
