{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_30", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r12s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r12s2',\n'title':'Shorten prediction verification with a balanced branch comparison tree',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 199.08 iterations/s at 79.422 MHz and 3,989,539 measured CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path starts at ID/EX rs2_val and ends at the IF PC through branch resolution. Accuracy-only headroom is limited by the existing bimodal predictor's small miss count. Prior schemes carrying targets (r7s2), deferring verification (r8s2 and r10s2), or banking recovery PCs (r11s2) failed to clear acceptance or failed liveness. The useful target is the combinational verification of the existing predictions on the original EX acceptance edge.\n\nA local probe carrying one preselected alternative successor in ID/EX passed the existing pipeline suite and CoreMark with unchanged cycles, but measured only 69.09 MHz median. Its late branch decision still reached fetch and squash controls. The final proposal instead shortens that decision itself without introducing pipeline state, adding recovery latency or changing prediction policy.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the EX branch predicate network used to verify fetched predictions with a balanced hierarchical comparator. Compute unsigned less-than and equality independently for each of four eight-bit operand slices after the existing rs1/rs2 forwarding muxes. Combine each adjacent high/low pair using EQ = EQ_hi & EQ_lo and LT = LT_hi | (EQ_hi & LT_lo), then apply the same operation to combine the two sixteen-bit halves. This is a fixed two-level tree above four short comparisons, not a serial priority loop or a new 32-bit relational expression.\n\nThe root EQ supplies BEQ and its complement supplies BNE. The root unsigned LT supplies BLTU and its complement BGEU. For signed LT, when operand sign bits differ use rs1[31], otherwise use the root unsigned LT; use its complement for BGE. Preserve the default false branch predicate for unsupported encodings. Do not change the ALU's SLT/SLTU datapath, arithmetic execution, forwarding selection, or operand capture. This is a predictor-verification timing change confined to the branch comparator.\n\nKeep all existing downstream branch_taken, target arithmetic, misalignment faults, actual_taken, accepted redirect detection, redirect_target selection, RVFI pc_next and training definitions exactly intact. The comparator must be bit-exact for every pair of 32-bit forwarded operands, including equality, sign boundaries and values differing in only a low slice. Do not derive architectural outcomes from predictions or early speculative values. Preserve single EX acceptance, once-only registered counter training and the original recovery edge; do not defer branch verification to MEM.\n\nRetain the 64 persistent two-bit counters and their pre-edge lookup, four-entry fall-through fetch queue and its packet layout, complete queue squash, load-use interlocks and all bus-stall behavior. Correct predictions must still avoid flushes; either prediction error must recover on the existing edge, before any younger memory, register or M-extension side effect. Preserve nret=1, every top-level port, decoder default-illegal checks, trap/write suppression, full-width addresses, precise RVFI order and canonical evaluation contracts.\n\nExpect approximately six percent greater fitness from a higher clock at unchanged bracketed cycles, with low confidence until vendor timing is measured. At 3,989,539 cycles, acceptance requires more than 208.23768 iterations/s, approximately 83.08 MHz median Fmax. Short local carry chains plus a balanced merge can beat Gowin's long full-width comparator chain, but added equality logic and routing may instead hurt, and JALR/ALU/divider paths may become limiting. Gowin mapping and all scored placement options must decide the outcome.\n\nValidate comparator equivalence on arbitrary 32-bit operands, including equal words, each possible first differing byte, opposite signs, signed extremes and equality prefixes. Run the existing pipeline suite with all six branch conditions and EX/MEM/WB-forwarded operands, both prediction errors, trained loops, aliases, misaligned targets, queue-full recovery and prolonged independent bus stalls. Check exact recovery latency, unchanged RVFI traces, absence of wrong-path side effects and exact training events. Run unchanged formal gates, especially liveness and branch instruction checks, stalled reference cosimulation, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation and median Gowin timing. Require the champion's identical 3,989,539 bracketed cycles.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace the six full-width branch comparison expressions with shared four-by-eight-bit equality/unsigned-less-than leaves and an explicit balanced two-level merge. Derive signed comparison from root unsigned comparison and operand signs, and map the exact six branch predicates. Keep existing forwarding, all EX acceptance/recovery/training/target/trap calculations and arithmetic units unchanged; add no state or new interface.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Extend branch coverage with values equal through the high 8, 16 or 24 bits but differing below, both signed extrema, equal operands and opposite signs for all six conditions. Exercise each forwarding source, repeated prediction hits, both mismatch directions, aliases, target faults, load-use/dmem holds and full-queue recovery. Check exact RVFI operand/PC/order traces, unchanged recovery edge, once-only training and no wrong-path side effects. Preserve every existing assertion and formal bound.'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema-validated hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_30", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r12s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r12s2',\n'title':'Shorten prediction verification with a balanced branch comparison tree',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 199.08 iterations/s at 79.422 MHz and 3,989,539 measured CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path starts at ID/EX rs2_val and ends at the IF PC through branch resolution. Accuracy-only headroom is limited by the existing bimodal predictor's small miss count. Prior schemes carrying targets (r7s2), deferring verification (r8s2 and r10s2), or banking recovery PCs (r11s2) failed to clear acceptance or failed liveness. The useful target is the combinational verification of the existing predictions on the original EX acceptance edge.\n\nA local probe carrying one preselected alternative successor in ID/EX passed the existing pipeline suite and CoreMark with unchanged cycles, but measured only 69.09 MHz median. Its late branch decision still reached fetch and squash controls. The final proposal instead shortens that decision itself without introducing pipeline state, adding recovery latency or changing prediction policy.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the EX branch predicate network used to verify fetched predictions with a balanced hierarchical comparator. Compute unsigned less-than and equality independently for each of four eight-bit operand slices after the existing rs1/rs2 forwarding muxes. Combine each adjacent high/low pair using EQ = EQ_hi & EQ_lo and LT = LT_hi | (EQ_hi & LT_lo), then apply the same operation to combine the two sixteen-bit halves. This is a fixed two-level tree above four short comparisons, not a serial priority loop or a new 32-bit relational expression.\n\nThe root EQ supplies BEQ and its complement supplies BNE. The root unsigned LT supplies BLTU and its complement BGEU. For signed LT, when operand sign bits differ use rs1[31], otherwise use the root unsigned LT; use its complement for BGE. Preserve the default false branch predicate for unsupported encodings. Do not change the ALU's SLT/SLTU datapath, arithmetic execution, forwarding selection, or operand capture. This is a predictor-verification timing change confined to the branch comparator.\n\nKeep all existing downstream branch_taken, target arithmetic, misalignment faults, actual_taken, accepted redirect detection, redirect_target selection, RVFI pc_next and training definitions exactly intact. The comparator must be bit-exact for every pair of 32-bit forwarded operands, including equality, sign boundaries and values differing in only a low slice. Do not derive architectural outcomes from predictions or early speculative values. Preserve single EX acceptance, once-only registered counter training and the original recovery edge; do not defer branch verification to MEM.\n\nRetain the 64 persistent two-bit counters and their pre-edge lookup, four-entry fall-through fetch queue and its packet layout, complete queue squash, load-use interlocks and all bus-stall behavior. Correct predictions must still avoid flushes; either prediction error must recover on the existing edge, before any younger memory, register or M-extension side effect. Preserve nret=1, every top-level port, decoder default-illegal checks, trap/write suppression, full-width addresses, precise RVFI order and canonical evaluation contracts.\n\nExpect approximately six percent greater fitness from a higher clock at unchanged bracketed cycles, with low confidence until vendor timing is measured. At 3,989,539 cycles, acceptance requires more than 208.23768 iterations/s, approximately 83.08 MHz median Fmax. Short local carry chains plus a balanced merge can beat Gowin's long full-width comparator chain, but added equality logic and routing may instead hurt, and JALR/ALU/divider paths may become limiting. Gowin mapping and all scored placement options must decide the outcome.\n\nValidate comparator equivalence on arbitrary 32-bit operands, including equal words, each possible first differing byte, opposite signs, signed extremes and equality prefixes. Run the existing pipeline suite with all six branch conditions and EX/MEM/WB-forwarded operands, both prediction errors, trained loops, aliases, misaligned targets, queue-full recovery and prolonged independent bus stalls. Check exact recovery latency, unchanged RVFI traces, absence of wrong-path side effects and exact training events. Run unchanged formal gates, especially liveness and branch instruction checks, stalled reference cosimulation, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation and median Gowin timing. Require the champion's identical 3,989,539 bracketed cycles.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace the six full-width branch comparison expressions with shared four-by-eight-bit equality/unsigned-less-than leaves and an explicit balanced two-level merge. Derive signed comparison from root unsigned comparison and operand signs, and map the exact six branch predicates. Keep existing forwarding, all EX acceptance/recovery/training/target/trap calculations and arithmetic units unchanged; add no state or new interface.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Extend branch coverage with values equal through the high 8, 16 or 24 bits but differing below, both signed extrema, equal operands and opposite signs for all six conditions. Exercise each forwarding source, repeated prediction hits, both mismatch directions, aliases, target faults, load-use/dmem holds and full-queue recovery. Check exact RVFI operand/PC/order traces, unchanged recovery edge, once-only training and no wrong-path side effects. Preserve every existing assertion and formal bound.'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema-validated hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated and schema-validated hypothesis\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
