{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_59", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r12s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r12s2',\n'title':'Predecode prediction polarity and factor same-cycle branch recovery',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 199.08 iterations/s at 79.422 MHz and 3,989,539 measured CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path starts at an ID/EX branch operand and reaches the IF PC. The present verification path selects among six branch predicates, applies taken-target fault qualification, compares against the prediction and selects a correction address using the resolved outcome. Much of that work depends only on instruction metadata and the captured prediction, so it can be prepared independently of the late operands.\n\nPrior target-carrying, deferred verification and recovery-bank designs failed to clear acceptance or failed liveness. Local probes confirmed that simply segmenting the comparator or moving a correction address into ID does not suffice, and registering the recovery event fails the unchanged liveness check. Keep the existing recovery edge and instead specialize its predicate around the original prediction.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Predecode one bit of prediction-verification metadata in ID: branch_recover_invert = original predicted_taken XOR decoded branch_op[0]. Add this bit to ID/EX only, before the trailing instruction/prediction/valid fields so the existing low-bit packet conventions remain intact. Capture it atomically with the instruction, hold it on all existing stalls and clear it with the existing complete bubble/reset. Do not alter the 66-bit IF packet or four-entry fetch FIFO. This prepares BEQ/BNE and LT/GE inversion plus prediction polarity before forwarded operand comparison.\n\nIn EX replace the separate signed/unsigned branch relational expressions with one shared unsigned comparison. Transform each forwarded operand's most-significant bit by XOR with \"'!branch_op[1], leaving bits 30:0 unchanged; compare the resulting 32-bit unsigned words. For BLT/BGE this flips the sign bit in both operands and exactly implements signed ordering, while BLTU/BGEU leave both words unchanged. Independently compute equality of the original operands. Set base_predicate = branch_op[2] ? shared_less : equal. For each of the six legal branch funct3 values, architectural branch_cond = base_predicate XOR branch_op[0]; preserve default false for reserved values. Do not change the ALU'\"'s SLT/SLTU operations or any forwarding mux.\n\nCompute conditional prediction mismatch directly as base_predicate XOR the saved branch_recover_invert. Qualify this with branch eligibility prepared independently of the condition: \"'!is_illegal && direct_target[1:0]==0. The conditional recovery term is is_branch && ((eligible && mismatch) || (!eligible && predicted_taken)). The second term keeps recovery to fallthrough explicit even for a captured taken prediction whose transfer is ineligible. A not-taken branch with an unaligned encoded target remains legal, trains not taken and does not redirect when predicted not taken. Keep architectural misalign_branch, misalign_jump, ctrl_with_trap and branch_taken calculations unchanged.\n\nKeep jump recovery separate from conditional comparison. Define jump_eligible = !is_illegal && !misalign_jump. The direct-JAL term is is_jump && !is_jalr && (predicted_taken != jump_eligible). The JALR term is is_jump && is_jalr && jump_eligible. OR these with the conditional term and apply the original ex_accept = !reset && in.valid && !stall && !execute_wait. Use only jump-specific alignment to qualify jumps; do not route a conditional branch predicate through a shared actual_taken/misalign_fault expression into the jump terms. Decoded branch and jump classes are mutually exclusive. Keep once-only accepted training exactly as today, with the original actual condition and fault rules.\n\nSelect the correction address independently of the resolved condition: for JALR use the existing full forwarded (rs1+immediate)&~1 sum; otherwise use predicted_taken ? PC+4 : PC+immediate. On an accepted direct-control mismatch this is exactly the alternative to the captured prediction, including fallthrough recovery for an ineligible taken prediction. The target is irrelevant when redirect is false. Keep architectural EX/MEM.pc_next, link values and trap write suppression resolved exactly as before; never substitute a speculative or alternative address into RVFI pc_wdata. No additional target register or post-register PC mux is required.\n\nKeep the original single IF PC register, recovery priority, complete younger-queue squash and ID/EX bubble at the existing EX acceptance edge. Add no recovery cycle, pipeline stage, annul protocol, load-use optimization or arithmetic change. Preserve the 64 persistent bimodal counters, registered training event, pre-edge lookup, fetch queue, independent memory backpressure, retained forwarding data, decoder default-illegal behavior, nret=1 and all top-level/RVFI interfaces. Correct predictions, actual misses and training events must occur on exactly the same cycles as the champion, including holds and fault cases.\n\nExpect approximately six percent higher fitness through a shorter verification/recovery path at identical CoreMark cycles; confidence is low until median vendor timing establishes it. Acceptance requires more than 208.23768 iterations/s, approximately 83.08 MHz at 3,989,539 cycles. The new metadata bit and shared comparison can reduce serial selection and comparator duplication, but physical routing, general ALU or divider paths may still limit Fmax. This is one predictor-verification redesign, not a claim of improved prediction accuracy.\n\nValidate the shared comparator and direct mismatch expression on equal values, all six conditions, sign extremes, opposite signs, and first differences in each byte. Exercise EX/MEM/WB forwarding, both direction errors, direct jumps, forwarded JALR, reserved encodings, misaligned targets, aliases, long independent bus stalls and queue-full recovery. Check atomic metadata hold/clear, exact unchanged recovery latency, original training events, RVFI operands/PCs/orders/traps and no wrong-path stores or M-extension requests. Run the existing unchanged pipeline tests and formal suite, including liveness, then stalled reference cosimulation and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. Measure all scored Gowin placement options and require unchanged bracketed cycles.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add a single branch_recover_invert bit to id_ex_t before its instruction field. Keep all architectural fields, the trailing instruction/prediction/valid layout and the IF queue packet unchanged.'''},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Capture original predicted_taken XOR decoded branch_op[0] into branch_recover_invert with every accepted instruction. Preserve complete reset/flush/invalid bubble clearing and whole-packet stall retention.'''},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Share one unsigned branch comparator after signed-mode MSB transformation, retain original equality and derive the six architectural predicates. Use the prepared prediction polarity for direct mismatch detection, static direct-target eligibility for conditional recovery and separate jump eligibility for JAL/JALR. Select direct correction addresses from the original prediction rather than the live outcome. Preserve exact EX acceptance, architectural target/trap/link/RVFI calculations, original training semantics, forwarding, all execution handshakes and recovery latency.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Add boundary and forwarding cases for the shared comparator and saved prediction polarity, including equal operands, opposite signs, signed extrema and low-byte differences for all six branch conditions. Cover both mismatch directions, eligibility faults, JAL/JALR, full queues and prolonged independent stalls. Assert metadata capture/hold/clear, exact original recovery and training cycles, precise RVFI state and absence of wrong-path effects. Retain every existing assertion and all formal bounds.'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=92))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final-design hypothesis written and schema-validated')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_59", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r12s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r12s2',\n'title':'Predecode prediction polarity and factor same-cycle branch recovery',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 199.08 iterations/s at 79.422 MHz and 3,989,539 measured CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path starts at an ID/EX branch operand and reaches the IF PC. The present verification path selects among six branch predicates, applies taken-target fault qualification, compares against the prediction and selects a correction address using the resolved outcome. Much of that work depends only on instruction metadata and the captured prediction, so it can be prepared independently of the late operands.\n\nPrior target-carrying, deferred verification and recovery-bank designs failed to clear acceptance or failed liveness. Local probes confirmed that simply segmenting the comparator or moving a correction address into ID does not suffice, and registering the recovery event fails the unchanged liveness check. Keep the existing recovery edge and instead specialize its predicate around the original prediction.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Predecode one bit of prediction-verification metadata in ID: branch_recover_invert = original predicted_taken XOR decoded branch_op[0]. Add this bit to ID/EX only, before the trailing instruction/prediction/valid fields so the existing low-bit packet conventions remain intact. Capture it atomically with the instruction, hold it on all existing stalls and clear it with the existing complete bubble/reset. Do not alter the 66-bit IF packet or four-entry fetch FIFO. This prepares BEQ/BNE and LT/GE inversion plus prediction polarity before forwarded operand comparison.\n\nIn EX replace the separate signed/unsigned branch relational expressions with one shared unsigned comparison. Transform each forwarded operand's most-significant bit by XOR with \"'!branch_op[1], leaving bits 30:0 unchanged; compare the resulting 32-bit unsigned words. For BLT/BGE this flips the sign bit in both operands and exactly implements signed ordering, while BLTU/BGEU leave both words unchanged. Independently compute equality of the original operands. Set base_predicate = branch_op[2] ? shared_less : equal. For each of the six legal branch funct3 values, architectural branch_cond = base_predicate XOR branch_op[0]; preserve default false for reserved values. Do not change the ALU'\"'s SLT/SLTU operations or any forwarding mux.\n\nCompute conditional prediction mismatch directly as base_predicate XOR the saved branch_recover_invert. Qualify this with branch eligibility prepared independently of the condition: \"'!is_illegal && direct_target[1:0]==0. The conditional recovery term is is_branch && ((eligible && mismatch) || (!eligible && predicted_taken)). The second term keeps recovery to fallthrough explicit even for a captured taken prediction whose transfer is ineligible. A not-taken branch with an unaligned encoded target remains legal, trains not taken and does not redirect when predicted not taken. Keep architectural misalign_branch, misalign_jump, ctrl_with_trap and branch_taken calculations unchanged.\n\nKeep jump recovery separate from conditional comparison. Define jump_eligible = !is_illegal && !misalign_jump. The direct-JAL term is is_jump && !is_jalr && (predicted_taken != jump_eligible). The JALR term is is_jump && is_jalr && jump_eligible. OR these with the conditional term and apply the original ex_accept = !reset && in.valid && !stall && !execute_wait. Use only jump-specific alignment to qualify jumps; do not route a conditional branch predicate through a shared actual_taken/misalign_fault expression into the jump terms. Decoded branch and jump classes are mutually exclusive. Keep once-only accepted training exactly as today, with the original actual condition and fault rules.\n\nSelect the correction address independently of the resolved condition: for JALR use the existing full forwarded (rs1+immediate)&~1 sum; otherwise use predicted_taken ? PC+4 : PC+immediate. On an accepted direct-control mismatch this is exactly the alternative to the captured prediction, including fallthrough recovery for an ineligible taken prediction. The target is irrelevant when redirect is false. Keep architectural EX/MEM.pc_next, link values and trap write suppression resolved exactly as before; never substitute a speculative or alternative address into RVFI pc_wdata. No additional target register or post-register PC mux is required.\n\nKeep the original single IF PC register, recovery priority, complete younger-queue squash and ID/EX bubble at the existing EX acceptance edge. Add no recovery cycle, pipeline stage, annul protocol, load-use optimization or arithmetic change. Preserve the 64 persistent bimodal counters, registered training event, pre-edge lookup, fetch queue, independent memory backpressure, retained forwarding data, decoder default-illegal behavior, nret=1 and all top-level/RVFI interfaces. Correct predictions, actual misses and training events must occur on exactly the same cycles as the champion, including holds and fault cases.\n\nExpect approximately six percent higher fitness through a shorter verification/recovery path at identical CoreMark cycles; confidence is low until median vendor timing establishes it. Acceptance requires more than 208.23768 iterations/s, approximately 83.08 MHz at 3,989,539 cycles. The new metadata bit and shared comparison can reduce serial selection and comparator duplication, but physical routing, general ALU or divider paths may still limit Fmax. This is one predictor-verification redesign, not a claim of improved prediction accuracy.\n\nValidate the shared comparator and direct mismatch expression on equal values, all six conditions, sign extremes, opposite signs, and first differences in each byte. Exercise EX/MEM/WB forwarding, both direction errors, direct jumps, forwarded JALR, reserved encodings, misaligned targets, aliases, long independent bus stalls and queue-full recovery. Check atomic metadata hold/clear, exact unchanged recovery latency, original training events, RVFI operands/PCs/orders/traps and no wrong-path stores or M-extension requests. Run the existing unchanged pipeline tests and formal suite, including liveness, then stalled reference cosimulation and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. Measure all scored Gowin placement options and require unchanged bracketed cycles.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add a single branch_recover_invert bit to id_ex_t before its instruction field. Keep all architectural fields, the trailing instruction/prediction/valid layout and the IF queue packet unchanged.'''},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Capture original predicted_taken XOR decoded branch_op[0] into branch_recover_invert with every accepted instruction. Preserve complete reset/flush/invalid bubble clearing and whole-packet stall retention.'''},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Share one unsigned branch comparator after signed-mode MSB transformation, retain original equality and derive the six architectural predicates. Use the prepared prediction polarity for direct mismatch detection, static direct-target eligibility for conditional recovery and separate jump eligibility for JAL/JALR. Select direct correction addresses from the original prediction rather than the live outcome. Preserve exact EX acceptance, architectural target/trap/link/RVFI calculations, original training semantics, forwarding, all execution handshakes and recovery latency.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Add boundary and forwarding cases for the shared comparator