{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r12s2.yaml');h=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='Isolate predictor verification from arithmetic readiness and late polarity selection'\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'].replace('OR these with the conditional term and apply the original ex_accept = \"'!reset && in.valid && !stall && !execute_wait.'\"', '''OR these with the conditional term and apply a predictor-specific control_accept = \"'!reset && in.valid && !stall. Remove execute_wait only from the acceptance used by recovery and predictor training: a positively decoded BRANCH, JAL or JALR always has base ALU_ADD and can never be a blocking MUL/DIV operation. Conversely, every blocking M instruction has is_branch=is_jump=is_jalr=0, so it cannot redirect or train even though control_accept ignores its wait. Do not remove execute_wait from real execution, pipeline holds or any arithmetic handshake. This static instruction-class exclusion cuts the ALU/divider readiness-to-predictor path without changing the event sequence. Preserve !stall so an older unready data-memory operation still defers control-flow acceptance.'\"''')\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'].replace('Keep once-only accepted training exactly as today, with the original actual condition and fault rules.', 'Use control_accept also for train_valid, retaining the original is_branch, actual condition, illegal and target-fault qualifications. Thus accepted training remains exactly once and on the original cycle for every reachable decoded instruction.')\nh['hypothesis']+='''\\\\n\\\\nA preliminary version containing the polarity/shared-comparator/address changes but retaining execute_wait in predictor acceptance passed the existing pipeline suite, stalled cosimulation and the unchanged liveness check, yet reached only 76.788 MHz median. Placement option zero exposed a new path from ID/EX alu_op through divider readiness to the IF PC. The final proposal additionally removes that logically redundant arithmetic-ready dependency from predictor event qualification. It is not a resubmission of the measured preliminary version. Final timing and the complete unchanged formal suite must establish whether this last isolation clears acceptance; no final fitness result is claimed here.'''\nh['changes'][2]['description']=h['changes'][2]['description'].replace('Preserve exact EX acceptance,', 'Give recovery and training their own valid/nonreset/\"'!dmem-stall acceptance, omitting execute_wait solely because decoded control-transfer classes and blocking arithmetic are mutually exclusive. Preserve real EX acceptance/holds/handshakes,'\"')\nh['changes'][3]['description']+=' Include held M instructions and adjacent control transfers to prove that removing arithmetic readiness from predictor qualification never creates training or a recovery event on an M operation and does not let a data-stalled branch advance.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=92));jsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()));print('Schema valid')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
