{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_44", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r13s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Balanced prediction-mismatch tree with early polarity and correction selection'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 199.08 iterations/s at 79.422 MHz and 3,989,539 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path starts at an ID/EX branch operand and ends at the IF PC. The r12s0 balanced comparator shortened magnitude comparison but retained late signed-result selection and the original recovery-control cascade; it reached only 82.257 MHz. The r12s2 predictor-specific verification removed that control cascade but used a full-width relational comparator and reached only 79.243 MHz. Neither isolated change cleared acceptance. This proposal combines a balanced, sign-conditioned comparison topology with early prediction-recovery metadata in one verification network.\n\nA retirement-order CoreMark direction model found 51,419 misses for the current 64-entry bimodal organization and 39,844 for a folded 256-entry table among 529,588 timed conditional branches. The timed architectural trace contains only 13,735 JALRs. These are advisory model counts rather than cycle-accurate prediction results; they suggest limited headroom from a larger direction table or return stack. Focus on the verified recovery timing bottleneck while preserving the prediction policy.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the existing predictor-verification cone with a balanced comparison tree whose signed interpretation and prediction polarity are prepared before its late result. Retain the current 64-entry persistent bimodal table, registered learning event, direct JAL prediction, four-entry fall-through queue, forwarding and EX recovery edge. This is one predictor-verification redesign; it changes neither instruction scheduling nor arithmetic execution.\n\nAdd branch_recover_invert to id_ex_t before its trailing instr, predicted_taken and valid fields, preserving the existing low-bit layout and the unchanged 66-bit if_id_t. Capture original predicted_taken XOR decoded branch_op[0] in ID. Capture, hold and clear it atomically with the existing ID/EX packet. The bit folds branch polarity (BEQ/BNE and LT/GE) and the original prediction together before forwarded operands reach EX.\n\nKeep the original EX rs1/rs2 forwarding muxes and every consumer of their architectural values. For predictor comparison only, form compare_a={rs1[31] XOR \"'!branch_op[1],rs1[30:0]} and the corresponding compare_b. BLT/BGE thereby flip both sign bits, turning signed order into unsigned order; BLTU/BGEU leave the words unchanged. Equality is invariant under this shared sign transformation. Apply the sign transform before the tree, not a signed-result mux after its root.\n\nDivide these comparison words into sixteen two-bit slices, ordered most significant first. At each leaf use native two-bit equality and unsigned less-than expressions. Explicitly combine adjacent high/low groups through four balanced levels: eq_parent=eq_high AND eq_low; lt_parent=lt_high OR (eq_high AND lt_low). Do not express a 32-bit relational comparison, full-width subtraction, serial priority loop, or comparator matrix over forwarding candidates. The root yields equality and the appropriately signed/unsigned less-than result. Set base_predicate=branch_op[2] ? root_lt : root_eq. For the six legal branch_op values, architectural branch_cond=base_predicate XOR branch_op[0]; preserve default false for the two reserved values. Keep the ALU'\"'s own SLT/SLTU unchanged.\n\nCompute conditional prediction mismatch directly as base_predicate XOR branch_recover_invert. Independently prepare direct_eligible=\"'!is_illegal AND direct_target[1:0]==0. Conditional recovery is is_branch AND ((direct_eligible AND mismatch) OR (!direct_eligible AND predicted_taken)). This preserves fallthrough recovery for an ineligible taken prediction. A not-taken branch with a misaligned encoded target remains legal and trains not taken; a taken misaligned branch retains the original trap and linear architectural PC behavior.\n\nGive jumps their original architectural targets and separate recovery qualification. Let jump_eligible=!is_illegal AND !misalign_jump. The direct-JAL term is is_jump AND !is_jalr AND (predicted_taken != jump_eligible). The indirect term is is_jump AND is_jalr AND jump_eligible. OR these with conditional recovery and qualify by control_accept=!reset AND in.valid AND !stall. This predictor-specific acceptance omits execute_wait only because every positively decoded branch/JAL/JALR has base ALU_ADD and is mutually exclusive with blocking MUL/DIV. Preserve execute_wait in real pipeline holds and all arithmetic handshakes; a held M instruction has no control-transfer classification and cannot redirect or learn. Retain !stall so older data-memory backpressure defers recovery. Use control_accept for the existing training enable, retaining legal conditional-branch and target-fault qualifications and the actual branch outcome. Each learning event remains on exactly its original acceptance edge.\n\nSelect the correction address independently of the late comparison: for JALR retain the full forwarded (rs1+immediate)&~1 target; for direct control use predicted_taken ? PC+4 : PC+immediate. This is the alternative to the original direct prediction whenever recovery is asserted. The value is irrelevant without redirect. Keep architectural EX/MEM.pc_next, misalignment traps, link results and RVFI operand values resolved exactly as before. Never use the alternative correction address as architectural next-PC merely because it was preselected.\n\nRetain the single IF PC register, existing recovery priority, full younger-queue squash and ID/EX bubble on the current EX edge. Preserve load-use interlocks, independent imem/dmem backpressure, complete bubble controls, retained MEM/WB forwarding, decoder default-illegal behavior, nret=1 and all top-level/RVFI interfaces. Add no verification stage or recovery cycle; the unchanged bounded liveness check must pass. Correct predictions, misses, learning and retirement must have exactly the champion'\"'s cycle sequence.\n\nThe expected fitness gain is seven percent, with low confidence until median vendor timing establishes it. At unchanged 3,989,539 cycles, acceptance requires Fmax above approximately 83.08 MHz and fitness above 208.23768 iterations/s. The intended advantage over r12s0 is removing late signed-result, recovery-polarity and arithmetic-readiness selection; the advantage over r12s2 is replacing its long full-width magnitude comparator with native two-bit leaves and four balanced reductions. Competing general ALU paths and physical placement may still prevent acceptance. Do not infer a gain from RTL depth or a single placement option.\n\nA temporary implementation passed the complete existing test_pipeline.py invocation, all selftest/random-program reference cosimulations with and without both bus-stall flags, and the unchanged canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/completion/bounds/marker validator. Its bracketed cycles are exactly 3,989,539. A Yosys SAT miter proved branch_cond equivalent to all original signed/unsigned/equality cases for every operand pair and every branch_op, and proved the conditional mismatch/eligibility equation for both predictions. These checks do not replace full sequential riscv-formal, including liveness; the implementation phase must run every unchanged gate. Final vendor timing is pending at this writing.\n\nExtend predictor tests with equality, opposite signs, INT_MIN/MAX, adjacent values and highest differences in every two-bit leaf; all six conditions; every forwarding-source pair; simultaneous competing writers; x0; retained WB values; load-dependent branches; both mismatch directions; correctly predicted branches; direct and indirect jumps; reserved encodings; target faults; queue-full recovery and long independent bus stalls. Preserve existing predictor-history assertions and check exact recovery/learning cycles, new metadata hold/clear, RVFI source values/PCs/traps/orders, and absence of wrong-path stores or M-extension requests. Keep all formal bounds and contracts intact.'''\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add branch_recover_invert to id_ex_t before its trailing instruction/prediction/valid fields. Preserve all architectural fields and the unchanged IF packet/FIFO layout.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Capture predicted_taken XOR decoded branch_op[0] atomically with ID/EX, preserving whole-packet hold and reset/flush/invalid clearing.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace full-width branch comparison with a sign-conditioned sixteen-leaf, two-bit native-comparator tree and four balanced reduction levels. Derive architectural branch_cond and direct mismatch from its shared root and saved polarity. Prepare eligibility, separate jump terms and prediction-selected correction addresses independently of the late predicate. Use predictor-specific control acceptance without arithmetic wait while retaining older-memory stalls and all real execution holds/handshakes. Preserve original forwarding, architectural trap/link/PC behavior, training outcomes and recovery latency.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Extend branch and predictor checks across two-bit boundaries, signed extrema, forwarding combinations, both mismatch directions, jumps, target faults and prolonged independent stalls. Verify new metadata lifetime, exact unchanged recovery/learning cycles and complete RVFI state. Retain every existing architectural/predictor assertion and all formal bounds; cover held arithmetic and adjacent branches to enforce instruction-class exclusion.'}\n]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=100000,default_flow_style=False))\nprint('Updated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
