{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r13s2.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Parallel balanced branch-verification lanes with predecoded recovery polarity'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 199.08 iterations/s at 79.422 MHz and 3,989,539 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path starts at an ID/EX branch operand and ends at the IF PC. The current verifier first selects two 32-bit forwarded operands, then compares them and qualifies recovery. Branch comparison also loads the same forwarded operand nets used by the general ALU.\n\nPrior r12s0 comparator balancing reached only 82.257 MHz, while r12s2 early prediction polarity and recovery qualification reached only 79.243 MHz. Neither cleared acceptance. Replace that shared data-mux-then-compare topology with parallel balanced comparisons of forwarding candidates, selecting only one-bit predicates; predecode recovery polarity so the saved selection feeds a short mismatch path. This is one integrated predictor-verification topology, retaining the current prediction policy and recovery edge.\n\nAn advisory retirement-order CoreMark model found 51,419 direction misses for the current 64-entry bimodal organization versus 39,844 for a folded 256-entry table among 529,588 timed conditional branches. The architectural trace contains only 13,735 JALRs. These are trace-model counts, not cycle-accurate prediction results, and suggest limited cycle-saving headroom from a larger direction table or return stack. The proposed gain instead targets the observed verification timing bottleneck.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the existing predictor-verification cone with parallel, balanced comparison lanes over the possible forwarding sources, followed by one-bit source selection and predecoded prediction mismatch. Keep the 64 persistent bimodal counters, registered training event, direct JAL prediction, four-entry fall-through fetch queue, instruction schedule and EX recovery edge. This is one predictor-resolution redesign; leave arithmetic execution and architectural operand forwarding unchanged.\n\nAdd branch_recover_invert to id_ex_t immediately before its trailing instr, predicted_taken and valid fields. Preserve the current low-bit packet conventions and the unchanged 66-bit if_id_t/FIFO. ID captures original predicted_taken XOR decoded branch_op[0]. Hold and clear this bit atomically with the existing ID/EX packet. This folds the BEQ/BNE and LT/GE polarity together with the original prediction before operand comparison.\n\nRetain the original EX rs1/rs2 forwarding muxes for the ALU, effective address, JALR, stores and RVFI operands. Build separate branch candidate arrays: A0=in.rs1_val, A1=fwd_ex_mem, A2=fwd_mem_wb; B0=in.rs2_val, B1=fwd_ex_mem, B2=fwd_mem_wb. For comparison only, XOR every candidate's bit 31 with \"'!branch_op[1], leaving its low 31 bits intact. B1 and B2 share A1 and A2 after this transform. Signed BLT/BGE thereby become unsigned ordering on sign-flipped words; BLTU/BGEU remain unchanged. Equality is invariant. Perform this sign transform before the comparison trees, not as a signed-result mux after their roots.\n\nUse seven real source-pair comparison lanes: 00, 01, 02, 10, 12, 20 and 21. For each pair, divide the transformed words into sixteen two-bit slices ordered most significant first. Use native two-bit equality and unsigned less-than at each leaf. Combine high/low groups through four explicitly balanced levels: eq_parent=eq_high AND eq_low; lt_parent=lt_high OR (eq_high AND lt_low). A convenient exact layout uses tree[16+k] for bits [31-2*k -: 2], k=0..15, and parent k combines 2*k and 2*k+1 for k=1..15. Do not substitute full-width comparisons, subtraction, or a serial priority chain. Each lane'\"'s base result is branch_op[2] ? root_lt : root_eq. Pairs 11 and 22 compare the same physical producer against itself; set their base result directly to \"'!branch_op[2] (equality true, less-than false), with no comparator.\n\nDecode each existing fwd_rs*_sel into three mutually exclusive enables: selector 1 chooses source 1, selector 2 source 2, and both 0 and 3 choose original source 0, matching the original forwarding case default. For pair ai,bi, enable=select_a[ai] AND select_b[bi]. Number lanes 3*ai+bi. Select only the one-bit base results: mask lanes 0..7 with their enables and OR them through a balanced eight-leaf reduction, then OR the enabled lane-8 result. This yields base_predicate without putting either 32-bit forwarding mux ahead of the branch comparator. Keep the original EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority supplied by forward_unit. Do not add valid gating to retained MEM/WB forwarding; its held data remains a legitimate source during a data stall.\n\nFor the six legal branch_op values, architectural branch_cond=base_predicate XOR branch_op[0]; default false for reserved branch_op values. Feed branch_cond into the original architectural branch_taken, target-fault, training outcome and resolved pc_next calculations. Compute conditional prediction mismatch directly as base_predicate XOR branch_recover_invert. Independently prepare direct_eligible=!is_illegal AND direct_target[1:0]==0. Conditional recovery is is_branch AND ((direct_eligible AND mismatch) OR (!direct_eligible AND predicted_taken)). This includes fallthrough correction for an ineligible taken prediction. A not-taken branch whose encoded target is misaligned remains legal and trains not taken; taken target faults retain their existing trap and linear architectural PC behavior.\n\nSeparate jump recovery from conditional comparison. Let jump_eligible=!is_illegal AND !misalign_jump. Direct-JAL recovery is is_jump AND !is_jalr AND (predicted_taken != jump_eligible); indirect recovery is is_jump AND is_jalr AND jump_eligible. OR these with conditional recovery and qualify by control_accept=!reset AND in.valid AND !stall. Omit execute_wait only from this predictor-specific acceptance: every positively decoded branch/JAL/JALR uses base ALU_ADD and is mutually exclusive with blocking MUL/DIV. Keep execute_wait in all real pipeline holds and arithmetic handshakes. A held M operation has no branch/jump classification and cannot redirect or learn. Retain !stall so older data-memory backpressure defers control-flow acceptance. Use control_accept for the original conditional-branch training enable, retaining legality and target-fault qualifications. Training still occurs exactly once at the original edge and carries the real branch condition.\n\nSelect the correction address independently of the late predicate. JALR retains the full forwarded (rs1+immediate)&~1 target; direct control uses predicted_taken ? PC+4 : PC+immediate. This selects the alternative to the original direct prediction whenever recovery is asserted; it is irrelevant otherwise. Keep architectural EX/MEM.pc_next, misalignment traps, link values and RVFI source values resolved exactly as before. Never use speculative correction metadata as the retiring architectural PC.\n\nKeep the original IF PC register, recovery priority, complete younger-queue squash and ID/EX bubble on the current EX edge. Preserve load-use interlocks, independent bus backpressure, complete bubble controls, retained WB forwarding, decoder default-illegal behavior, nret=1 and all IO/RVFI ports. Add no recovery or verification cycle and do not change liveness bounds. Prediction decisions, accepted recoveries, learning and retirements must retain exactly the champion'\"'s cycle sequence.\n\nA disposable implementation of this final topology measured Gowin placement options 0/1/2 at 79.416/83.648/83.648 MHz, median 83.648 MHz. It used 6,211 logic cells, 1,324 FFs, 49 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. Canonical stalled CoreMark passed the unchanged CRC/UART/completion/bounds/marker validator in exactly 3,989,539 bracketed cycles. This projects 209.673351 iterations/s, 5.320 percent above the rounded 199.08 champion, exceeding the 208.23768 acceptance threshold. The integer impact estimate rounds to five percent. This is a measured temporary-prototype result, not a completed orchestrator acceptance; the implementer must reproduce it and pass every unchanged gate.\n\nThe final prototype passed both existing test_pipeline.py pytest invocations (ordinary and YOSYS declarations), all selftest/random-program reference cosimulations with and without imem/dmem stalls, and canonical stalled CoreMark. A Yosys SAT miter proved the actual comparison network equal to the original forwarded signed/unsigned/equality predicates for all four 32-bit source values, all forwarding selectors and all eight branch_op values. It also proved conditional mismatch/eligibility equivalent for both predictions. Full unchanged sequential riscv-formal checks are running in a disposable copy at this writing; no completed full-suite result is claimed yet.\n\nComparator replication increases area and routing, and the general ALU remains a competing critical path. Local ablations explain why the complete topology matters: parallel full-width comparison lanes with original recovery control reached only 75.917 MHz; a single balanced tree with predecoded recovery but after the shared operand muxes reached 80.046 MHz. Do not simplify the final seven balanced lanes back into either measured subthreshold topology. These ablations are evidence for this single integrated verifier, not additional proposed categories or variants.\n\nExtend tests with equality, opposite signs, INT_MIN/MAX, adjacent values and highest differences in every two-bit leaf; all six conditions; all nine source-pair combinations; both operands selecting the same producer; competing writers; x0; retained WB values; load-dependent branches; both mismatch directions; correctly predicted branches; direct and indirect jumps; reserved encodings; target faults; queue-full recovery and long independent bus stalls. Preserve all existing predictor-history and architectural assertions. Verify new metadata hold/clear, exact original recovery/learning cycles, full RVFI source values/PCs/traps/orders, and absence of wrong-path stores or arithmetic requests. Keep all formal bounds and contracts unchanged.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes'][2]['description']='''Replace the post-forwarding comparator with seven sign-conditioned, balanced sixteen-leaf comparison lanes plus two same-producer constant lanes. Use native two-bit comparisons and four high/low reduction levels; choose only the one-bit lane results using existing forwarding selectors and a balanced masked OR. Retain wide forwarding for all architectural data and arithmetic. Derive architectural branch_cond and prediction mismatch from the selected base result and saved polarity. Prepare eligibility, separate jump terms and correction addresses independently of late comparison, and use predictor-specific acceptance excluding only the redundant arithmetic wait. Preserve all real holds, handshakes, traps, link values, training outcomes and original recovery latency.'''\nd['changes'][3]['description']='''Extend branch/predictor checks across two-bit boundaries, signed extrema and all forwarding-source pairs, including same-producer constants, competing writers and selector fallback behavior. Exercise both mismatch directions, jumps, target faults, queue-full recovery and long independent bus stalls. Verify metadata lifetime, exact unchanged recovery/learning cycles, no wrong-path effects and complete RVFI state. Retain all current assertions and formal bounds; cover held arithmetic adjacent to control transfers and retained WB data.'''\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef string(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,string)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=100))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nfit=83.648*1000000*10/3989539\nprint('Schema valid:',p)\nprint('Projected fitness',fit,'delta pct',(fit/199.08-1)*100)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
