{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"The comparison-lane probes also fell short. I’m testing a different recovery protocol: register the correction, then hold the resolving branch in EX/MEM until that correction is applied. This removes the same-cycle EX-to-fetch control path and should avoid the retirement-gap problem that made earlier delayed-recovery designs fail liveness. The unchanged formal check will test that assumption."}}
