nd-linear-PC behavior. An unpredicted legal JALR\n  still redirects exactly when its resolved target is aligned.\n\n  Implement redirect as ex_accept AND the OR of:\n  (in.ctrl.is_branch AND (in.predicted_taken XOR branch_cond) AND\n  (branch_target[1:0] == 0)), and\n  (in.ctrl.is_jal\n…[1888 of 4960 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ffbc3a69b5b947f0]…\nmpact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the generic direct_control/predicted-versus-actual recovery\n      expression with the branch-direction-mismatch/aligned-target and\n      aligned-JALR expression above. Remove unused direct_control only.\n      Preserve all actual target computation, trap controls, link values,\n      ex_accept, training, pipeline registers and RVFI resolved PC logic.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain the existing predictor reference model and architectural\n      assertions. Extend directed cases to establish that aligned direct\n      JAL never needs recovery, unaligned direct targets remain linear\n      with the original trap discipline, and conditional corrections\n      match the original generic expression on every reachable prediction.\n      Exercise forwarded operands, wrong-path stores/divides, imem stalls,\n      dmem holds, both prediction errors and complete retirement traces.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
