{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'predictor|bimodal|gshare|return.address|ras|branch.target' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division off the single-cycle EX path with a shared clocked divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The sole recorded baseline scores 12.12 iterations/s at 5.442 MHz. Its\\nworst reported path is 199.837 ns through forwarding and the EX ALU,\\nwith 156 cells. The ALU currently evaluates full-width signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder combinationally. This strongly suggests\\nthat the unrolled divider constrains the clock for every instruction,\\nalthough a detailed cell-level timing report must confirm the inference.\\nThere is no LESSONS.md and no previous structural attempt in log.jsonl.\\nBreaking this arithmetic dependency across clock edges is a substantially\\nlarger opportunity than the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The sole recorded baseline scores 12.12 iterations/s at 5.442 MHz. Its\\nworst reported path is 199.837 ns through forwarding and the EX ALU,\\nwith 156 cells. The ALU currently evaluates full-width signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder combinationally. This strongly suggests\\nthat the unrolled divider constrains the clock for every instruction,\\nalthough a detailed cell-level timing report must confirm the inference.\\nThere is no LESSONS.md and no previous structural attempt in log.jsonl.\\nBreaking this arithmetic dependency across clock edges is a substantially\\nlarger opportunity than the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU execution path with one\\nshared, blocking, clocked divider. Keep the existing single-cycle base\\nALU and multiplier paths. Capture the forwarded operands and operation\\nonce, normalize signed operands to unsigned magnitudes, and reuse an\\neight-step radix-2 restoring divide datapath for four iteration clocks.\\nEach step shifts the partial remainder and quotient/dividend and uses\\none 33-bit trial subtraction to select the next remainder and quotient\\nbit. Register normalization before iteration and register\n…[159285 of 162357 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3914ec20699a8761]…\nregression\", \"fitness\": 130.4, \"delta_pct\": -4.41, \"vs_baseline\": 975.91, \"fmax_mhz\": 54.79, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4201709, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3903, \"ff\": 867, \"seeds\": [53.405, 54.79, 54.79], \"perturbations\": [[0, 53.405, 25], [1, 54.79, 25], [2, 54.79, 25]], \"lutram\": 32, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_2_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_1_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -13.725, \"arrival_ns\": 24.019, \"logic_cells\": 96, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 25, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:36:24.897365Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r7s2 (regression, -4.41%): Carrying IF direct_target and PC+4 through 64 extra ID/EX bits removes EX adders but leaves divider remainder_q feedback critical, so unchanged CoreMark cycles cannot offset median Fmax falling from 57.319 to 54.790 MHz.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
