{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"The first prototype kept CoreMark at 3,977,318 cycles, but Gowin retained the counters as flip-flops and timing regressed. I’ve revised the proposal to leave RAM data uninitialized and reset only a validity bitmap, as the register file does. I also caught a Yosys parser limitation and replaced the typedef-based queue width with an explicit 68-bit width.\n\n"}}
