{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_21", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r9s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r9s2',\n'title':'Local Gray-coded bimodal counters simplify predictor update hardware',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion already predicts direct BRANCH/JAL and queues four fetches.\nPrior trace profiling found only about 52,000 conditional misses; enlarging\nthe table has insufficient cycle headroom. A fresh architectural replay\ncounts only 13,735 returns in the measured CoreMark region, ruling out a\nreturn stack as a likely threshold-clearing change by itself. Prior\npredictor reset simplification showed useful physical gains on older\nparents, while carrying direct targets regressed and MEM verification\nfailed liveness. Reduce the physical cost of the existing direction\npredictor without changing its prediction policy or recovery latency.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Implement the existing 64-entry two-bit bimodal predictor as independent\nGray-coded four-state machines, one per PC[7:2] entry. Encode strongly\nnot-taken=00, weakly not-taken=01, weakly taken=11, strongly taken=10.\nThe high bit remains the predicted direction. Reset each entry to 11,\nwhich is the same weakly-taken prediction state as the current binary 10.\nPreserve synchronous runtime reset and all predictor interfaces.\n\nUse a generate loop of entry-local clocked updates. Entry i updates only\nwhen train_valid && train_index == i, using its own pre-edge two bits.\nWith direction d, weak-state bit w, and resolved outcome t, its next\nstate is d_next = w ? t : d and w_next = t XOR d. Both expressions use\nthe old direction. This exactly implements the existing saturating\nSmith counter transitions under the Gray encoding. Do not read a\nvariable-indexed current counter to compute a shared saturator result;\nonly the prediction lookup is a 64-to-1 read of the direction bits.\n\nThis replaces a central training read/multiplexer and saturation network\nfeeding a decoded write bank with small local next-state functions.\nThe goal is lower predictor logic and routing cost, potentially helping\nplacement of the existing competing EX paths. The recorded worst path\nis WB-through-ALU, not the predictor; do not claim that this change\nshortens that arithmetic path or guarantees a frequency increase.\n\nKeep lookup observing pre-edge state when lookup and training alias.\nRetain once-only accepted legal conditional training, alignment rules,\ncurrent-entry update semantics, direct JAL prediction and unpredicted\nJALR. Preserve the original one-bit prediction packet, four-entry queue,\nempty bypass, EX correction, queue flush priority, load-use interlocks,\nbus stalls, forwarding, divider/ALTOPS, decoder legality and nret=1.\nNo additional pipeline stage, history table, cached instruction or target\nmetadata belongs in this candidate. Architectural behavior and direction\npredictions should be cycle-for-cycle identical for the same input stream.\n\nEstimate six percent net fitness improvement with low confidence pending\nvendor timing. With unchanged 3,977,318 bracketed cycles, acceptance over\n153.70 requires more than 160.7702 iterations/s, or roughly 63.944 MHz\nmedian Fmax. Reduced area without that timing gain is insufficient.\nValidate all Gray transitions, saturation, reset, aliases, pre-edge reads\nand stalls against an abstract binary-counter reference. Check identical\nCoreMark cycles plus canonical CRC/UART/bounds/markers, unchanged formal\nand cosimulation gates, and median Gowin timing over all three options.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Replace the binary counter bank's central indexed update with 64\nentry-local Gray-state update processes and a decoded train enable.\nReset to weakly taken 11, retain counters[pc[7:2]][1] lookup, and\npreserve every other predictor, queue and recovery behavior.'''.strip()},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Preserve the abstract binary saturation reference and architectural\nassertions. Decode Gray state only for internal representation checks;\nverify equivalent predictions for all states/outcomes, saturation,\nreset, aliasing, concurrent lookup/training and held branch behavior.\nRetain once-only training, full-queue recovery, target fault, load-use,\nbus-stall, divide, wrong-path side-effect and RVFI-order checks.'''.strip()}\n]}\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef st(d,s): return d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nD.add_representer(str,st)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=88))\nprint('Revised complete hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
