{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_34", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r9s2.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Register predictor training to decouple EX decisions from counter updates'\nd['hypothesis']='''Insert a one-entry, one-cycle training pipeline ahead of the existing\n64-entry binary bimodal counter bank. Capture train_valid, train_index\nand train_taken from EX each cycle into eight resettable bits. On the\nfollowing edge, update the current indexed counter using only the saved\nvalid/index/outcome. Keep reset priority; clear pending valid on reset.\nCapture the event regardless of instruction-bus availability, fetch-queue\noccupancy, pipeline holds and younger redirects. EX already emits exactly\none event for an accepted legal nonfaulting conditional branch; do not\nreinterpret acceptance or use a held valid bit as a new event.\n\nThe event stage captures incoming valid every cycle, including zero, so\na held EX instruction cannot duplicate training. Back-to-back branches\ncan supply one event per cycle while the prior event drains. Read the\ncurrent table entry at update time, not a saved lookup counter, so two\nconsecutive outcomes for the same entry accumulate without lost updates.\nFetch observes pre-edge counter state; the one-cycle later update can\nchange prediction timing, but EX always verifies the captured prediction.\nNever flush an older pending training event on a younger recovery.\n\nRetain all 64 counters, binary encoding, weakly-taken synchronous reset,\nPC[7:2] indexing, saturation and prediction policies. This moves only\npredictor learning one cycle later. Branch resolution, actual next-PC,\nmisalignment handling, EX redirect and recovery stay on their existing\ncycle. Preserve the one-bit prediction packet, four-entry fetch queue,\nempty bypass, queue flush priority, load-use interlocks, bus handshakes,\nforwarding, divider/ALTOPS, decoder legality, full addresses and nret=1.\nDo not add target prediction, late verification, a new execution stage\nor any other category change.\n\nThe goal is to terminate EX's outcome/qualification fanout at a small\nregister bank and let counter lookup, saturation and write selection\noperate from registered inputs. Current timing probes expose a path\nfrom WB write qualification through EX to the counter bank when reset\nlogic is removed. The champion also has competing ALU/divider paths;\nthis change does not eliminate those paths or guarantee a clock gain.\n\nEstimate six percent net improvement with low confidence pending timing.\nAgainst 153.70, acceptance requires more than 160.7702 iterations/s.\nAt the parent 3,977,318 cycles this means over 63.943421 MHz; delayed\nlearning may change actual measured cycles, so use the actual marker\nbrackets and median vendor Fmax. Preserve every formal, liveness,\ncosimulation, canonical CRC/UART and memory-bounds check. Validate the\npending event protocol under aliases, consecutive branches, data and\ninstruction stalls, reset and redirects, and keep precise RVFI checks.'''\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Add resettable pending training valid/index/outcome registers and\nfeed the unchanged binary counter update process from that stage.\nAccept one event every clock and drain the previous event, clearing\nvalid on reset. Keep lookup, reset state, direct prediction, queue\nformat, fetch acceptance and immediate EX recovery unchanged.'''},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Extend the predictor observer with a one-cycle pending training event;\nkeep EX acceptance assertions and model counter application separately.\nCheck continuous events, consecutive same-index outcomes, pre-edge\nlookup and current-entry saturation, bubbles/stalls without duplicates,\nreset cancellation, and preservation of an older event across younger\nredirects. Keep all architectural, queue, wrong-path-side-effect, trap,\nforwarding, arithmetic and RVFI-order assertions unchanged.'''}]\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\nD.add_representer(str,lambda d,s:d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=88));print('Updated complete hypothesis to registered training')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
