load-use interlocks, bus handshakes,\nforwarding, divider/ALTOPS, decoder legality, full addresses and nret=1.\nDo not add target prediction, late verification, a new execution stage\nor any other category change.\n\nThe goal is to terminate EX's outcome/qualification fanout at a small\nregister bank and let counter lookup, saturation and write selection\noperate from registered inputs. Current timing probes expose a path\nfrom WB write qualification through EX to the counter bank when reset\nlogic is removed. The champion also has competing ALU/divider paths;\nthis change does not eliminate those paths or guarantee a clock gain.\n\nEstimate six percent net improvement with low confidence pending timing.\nAgainst 153.70, acceptance requires more than 160.7702 iterations/s.\nAt the parent 3,977,318 cycles this means over 63.943421 MHz; delayed\nlearning may change actual measured cycles, so use the actual marker\nbrackets and median vendor Fmax. Preserve every formal, liveness,\ncosimulation, canonical CRC/UART and memory-bounds check. Validate the\npending event protocol under aliases, consecutive branches, data and\ninstruction stalls, reset and redirects, and keep precise RVFI checks.'''\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Add resettable pending training valid/index/outcome registers and\nfeed the unchanged binary counter update process from that stage.\nAccept one event every clock and drain the previous event, clearing\nvalid on reset. Keep lookup, reset state, direct prediction, queue\nformat, fetch acceptance and immediate EX recovery unchanged.'''},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Extend the predictor observer with a one-cycle pending training event;\nkeep EX acceptance assertions and model counter application separately.\nCheck continuous events, consecutive same-index outcomes, pre-edge\nlookup and current-entry saturation, bubbles/stalls without duplicates,\nreset cancellation, and preservation of an older event across