{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_42", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r9s2.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Persistent bimodal predictor with registered EX training'\nd['motivation']='''The champion already predicts direct BRANCH/JAL and buffers four fetches.\nPrior profiling found only about 52,000 conditional misses; fresh trace\nreplay counts just 13,735 returns, so larger direction tables and return\nprediction have limited cycle headroom. LESSONS.md records clock gains\nfrom removing predictor reset logic on older parents, but carrying direct\ntargets regressed and MEM-stage verification failed liveness.\n\nOn this exact parent, placement-option-1 probes measured 59.318 MHz for\npersistent counters alone and 61.346 MHz for registered training alone.\nCombining persistent counters with registered training measured 64.119 MHz\nin the same vendor flow. The former exposes WB/EX-to-counter training as\na worst path; registering that event isolates counter updates while the\npersistent bank removes reset-related logic. This is one predictor\nimplementation change with complementary parts, not an accuracy redesign.'''\ns=d['hypothesis'];s=s.replace('Keep reset priority; clear pending valid on reset.','Keep reset priority; clear all eight event bits on reset.')\ns=s.replace('Retain all 64 counters, binary encoding, weakly-taken synchronous reset,\\\\nPC[7:2] indexing, saturation and prediction policies.', '''Retain all 64 counters, binary encoding, PC[7:2] indexing, saturation and\nprediction policies. Initialize counters[i] to weakly taken 2'b10 in a\nsynthesizable initial loop, using the same initialization in Gowin,\nsimulation and formal. Remove only the bank's synchronous reset arm;\nits existing indexed saturating update is enabled by\n\"'!reset && train_valid_q. All counters hold during runtime reset. Reset\nPC, pipeline, register file, divider and RVFI order exactly as before;\nonly advisory predictor history survives. Discard any pending training\nevent when reset is asserted. No epoch, clearing sweep or startup stall\nis needed; correctness must hold for arbitrary retained history.'\"''')\ns=s.replace('Estimate six percent net improvement with low confidence pending timing.', '''Estimate five percent net improvement with medium confidence based on the\n64.119 MHz initial placement result; remaining placements and validation\nmust confirm this narrow margin.''')\nd['hypothesis']=s;d['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Add eight resettable pending training valid/index/outcome bits and\nfeed the existing binary counter update process from those registers.\nCapture all incoming event fields every non-reset clock, including a\nzero valid; consume the prior event once. Initialize counters[0:63] to\n2'b10 in a synthesizable initial loop and guard the unchanged indexed\nsaturator with \"'!reset && train_valid_q, removing counter reset writes.\nRetain table names/encoding, pre-edge lookup, fetch queue and immediate\nEX recovery; do not assume or force RAM inference.'\"'''\nd['changes'][1]['description']='''Model one-cycle pending training separately from accepted EX events,\nand retain the abstract counter history across runtime resets. Establish\nknown predictor states through training or fresh simulation rather than\nassuming reset restores weakly taken. Check consecutive same-index\noutcomes, saturation, pre-edge lookup, bubbles/stalls without duplicate\nupdates, pending-event cancellation on reset, retained history after\nreset, and an older event surviving younger recovery. Preserve every\narchitectural, queue, wrong-path-side-effect, trap, forwarding, arithmetic\nand RVFI-order assertion; add repeated-reset directed coverage.'''\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\nD.add_representer(str,lambda d,s:d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=88));print('Updated YAML to combined predictor architecture')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
