{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r9s2.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ns=d['hypothesis']\ns=s.replace('The goal is to terminate EX\\\\'s outcome/qualification fanout at a small\\\\nregister bank and let counter lookup, saturation and write selection\\\\noperate from registered inputs. Current timing probes expose a path\\\\nfrom WB write qualification through EX to the counter bank when reset\\\\nlogic is removed. The champion also has competing ALU/divider paths;\\\\nthis change does not eliminate those paths or guarantee a clock gain.', '''The goal is to terminate EX's outcome/qualification fanout at a small\nregister bank and let counter lookup, saturation and write selection\noperate from registered inputs. Reset removal alone exposes a path from\nWB write qualification through EX to the counter bank. In the combined\nprototype the worst vendor path returns to the divider, with competing\nWB-to-ALU paths. The predictor was not the champion's recorded worst\npath; attribute the gain to training isolation plus physical changes,\nnot a change to arithmetic depth or prediction accuracy.''')\na=s.index('Estimate five percent');s=s[:a]+'''An isolated prototype of exactly this two-part predictor change measured\nGowin placement-option Fmax values of 61.846, 64.119 and 64.119 MHz:\nmedian 64.119 MHz. Placement-0 logic is 4,128 LUT4 with 893 registers,\n49 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and six DSPs. It does not demonstrate a predictor\nRAM conversion; preserve the existing array and indexed saturation form.\nThe benchmark completed with unchanged 3,977,318 marker-bracketed cycles,\ncanonical CRCs, required UART validation, and no out-of-bounds access.\nThis implies 161.21165 iterations/s, 4.887 percent above 153.70, exceeding\nthe 160.7702 acceptance threshold by only 0.44145 iterations/s. Round the\nexpected gain to five percent with medium confidence. Final implementation\nmust reproduce the vendor median; the margin is small.\n\nThe prototype passed reference cosimulation of selftest and all three\nrandom programs, each with and without independent bus stalls. A directed\ncocotb probe passed 26 executions across runtime resets, observing exact\npre-edge predictions and pending event fields against a retained abstract\ncounter model. It observed 34 accepted training events, 33 applications\nand one deliberately reset-canceled event; it checked aliased outcomes,\nwrong predictions, wrong-path store/divide suppression, restart of RVFI\norder and precise PC traces. The standard formal run is pending; these\nmeasurements are prototype evidence, not a completed orchestrator gate.\n\nAdapt the full existing pipeline predictor observer to model the delayed\nwrite separately from EX acceptance, and preserve counter history across\nresets while clearing pending events. Preserve all architectural assertions\nand every formal, liveness, cosimulation, CRC/UART and bounds gate. No\nchanges outside rtl/if_stage.sv and its cocotb tests are needed. Keep the\nmeasured implementation structure rather than adding Gray encoding,\nentry-local update logic, RAM attributes, resizing or speculative state.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']=s\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\nD.add_representer(str,lambda d,s:d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final candidate schema valid; measured median and checks recorded')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
